{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uhsupsipashwanjn35l62yfc7sjxf6vlxkygikoabfz5h7xtdvja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01M8Xd1f59tGBgncMaSd2ciT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Produce ERRORS.md error surface table","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are producing a Phase-A analysis artifact for a C-to-Rust translation verification of **PCRE2 10.48 (8-bit, SUPPORT_UNICODE, no JIT)**.\n\nWorking dir: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/translated_rust`\nC source: `c_src/src/*.c`, `c_src/src/*.h`, public header `c_src/include/pcre2.h`\nDO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN `c_src/`. This is read-only analysis.\n\n## Your single deliverable\nWrite the file `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/translated_rust/ERRORS.md`\n\nIt is the **ERROR-SURFACE TABLE**: one row per DISTINCT way the C code rejects or errors on input, derived MECHANICALLY from the C source (not from docs, not from guesses).\n\n## Method (do this mechanically)\nGrep the C source for every rejection path. Cover at minimum:\n- `return PCRE2_ERROR_*` in every `.c` file (counts to orient you: pcre2_substring.c:14, pcre2_context.c:6, pcre2_config.c:3, pcre2_convert.c:20, pcre2_error.c:2, pcre2_valid_utf.c:30, pcre2_pattern_info.c:10, pcre2_dfa_match.c:18, pcre2_serialize.c:17, pcre2_jit_compile.c:20, pcre2_match.c:37, pcre2_substitute.c:11)\n- the compile-time error mechanism in `pcre2_compile.c` (`*errorcode = ERR<n>` / `errorcode = ERR<n>` / the `ERR0..ERRnn` enum and how it maps to the `PCRE2_ERROR_*` numbers 101..199 in `pcre2.h`). Include the compile errors that are reachable from a **caller-supplied pattern string** (malformed regex syntax). Group only when the trigger is genuinely identical; distinct syntax triggers = distinct rows.\n- `return NULL` paths in the public `pcre2_*_create` / `pcre2_compile` / `pcre2_substring_*` / `pcre2_serialize_*` functions and what the accompanying error output is.\n- every explicit range / bounds / null check on PUBLIC API arguments, e.g. `if (code == NULL) return PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`, magic-number checks (`PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC`), mode checks (`PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE`), `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` for unknown option bits, `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET`, `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSETLIMIT`, `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA`, `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING`, `PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING`, `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`, `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE`, `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSERIALIZEDDATA`, `PCRE2_ERROR_MIXEDTABLES`, limit errors (`MATCHLIMIT`, `DEPTHLIMIT`, `HEAPLIMIT`), substitute errors (-35, -57..-61, -69..-76), convert errors (`PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`), JIT errors (`PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION`, `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_UNSUPPORTED`, `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` from jit stubs).\n- all UTF-8 validity errors from `pcre2_valid_utf.c` (`PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR1` .. `UTF8_ERR21`) — one row each, with the exact byte sequence that triggers it.\n- every `PCRE2_ASSERT` / `assert` on public input paths.\n- out-of-range **enum-like integer** arguments crossing FFI: `pcre2_config()` `what` values, `pcre2_pattern_info()` `what` values, `pcre2_set_newline()` values, `pcre2_set_bsr()` values, `pcre2_set_optimize()` directive values, `pcre2_serialize_*`.\n\n## Required format\nStart with a short header explaining provenance, then ONE table with EXACTLY these columns:\n\n```\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n```\n\nRules for rows:\n- `function` = the exact public (or `_pcre2_`-prefixed exported) C symbol name, e.g. `pcre2_match_8`.\n- `trigger` = the CONCRETE invalid input a test can construct (e.g. \"`subject` UTF-8 byte 0x80 at offset 0 with PCRE2_UTF set\", \"`startoffset` > subject length\", \"pattern `a{2,1}`\"). Be specific enough that a test author needs no further C reading.\n- `expected C result` = the exact returned constant/sentinel AND, for compile failures, the numeric error code plus the `errorptr`/`erroroffset` values where determinable (e.g. \"NULL, errorcode=PCRE2_ERROR_QUANTIFIER_OUT_OF_ORDER (104)\").\n- Three distinct error branches = three rows. Do not merge distinct branches.\n- Number rows sequentially from 1.\n- Add a trailing `status` note column is NOT wanted — keep exactly the 4 columns above.\n\nAim for COMPLETE coverage; this will be a large table (expect 150–260 rows). Group the table into `###` subsections by C source file for readability, but keep the row numbering globally sequential and the column layout identical in every subsection.\n\nIf the file is too large for one write, create it with a first Write call and APPEND subsequent sections with additional edits — but ensure the final file is complete and well-formed.\n\nFinally, verify your own output: run `grep -c '^| [0-9]' ERRORS.md` and report the row count in your final message, plus a one-paragraph summary of the biggest error-surface clusters."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6287,"cache_read_input_tokens":34508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6287,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7","uuid":"e2314c94-fde6-4981-9241-02dc4d49c4b6","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:11:17.442Z"}
