oroffset` values where determinable (e.g. \"NULL, errorcode=PCRE2_ERROR_QUANTIFIER_OUT_OF_ORDER (104)\").\n- Three distinct error branches = three rows. Do not merge distinct branches.\n- Number rows sequentially from 1.\n- Add a trailing `status` note column is NOT wanted — keep exactly the 4 columns above.\n\nAim for COMPLETE coverage; this will be a large table (expect 150–260 rows). Group the table into `###` subsections by C source file for readability, but keep the row numbering globally sequential and the column layout identical in every subsection.\n\nIf the file is too large for one write, create it with a first Write call and APPEND subsequent sections with additional edits — but ensure the final file is complete and well-formed.\n\nFinally, verify your own output: run `grep -c '^| [0-9]' ERRORS.md` and report the row count in your final message, plus a one-paragraph summary of the biggest error-surface clusters.","uuid":"b9137e10-6572-4060-a6db-8f80edd73ef3","session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7"}
