g the C: name the exact option bits, the pattern shape, the subject shape.\n- Last column is a literal `[ ]` checkbox for later Phase-B sign-off.\n- Number rows sequentially from 1.\n- Group into `###` subsections by area (compile, match, dfa_match, substitute, substring, pattern_info, serialize, convert, context, low-level string/utf helpers, tables, jit stubs), with globally sequential numbering and identical columns everywhere.\n\nAim for COMPLETE coverage of distinct code paths; expect 150–300 rows. Bias toward the low-level entry points being represented, not just `pcre2_compile`+`pcre2_match`.\n\nIf the file is too large for one write, create it then append in further calls; ensure the final file is complete and well-formed.\n\nFinally verify your own output: run `grep -c '^| [0-9]' CONFIGS.md` and report the row count in your final message plus a one-paragraph summary of the axes with the most interaction risk."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6287,"cache_read_input_tokens":34508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6287,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7","uuid":"5d2a021c-761d-4c4d-8b66-0cddd7abcffb","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:11:53.279Z"}
