*`, `_pcre2_hspace_list_8`, `_pcre2_vspace_list_8`, `_pcre2_posix_class_maps8`, `_pcre2_default_tables_8`, `_pcre2_unicode_version_8`, `_pcre2_utf8_table*`, `_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8`, `_pcre2_ucp_gbtable_8`).\n   And all the public ones: `pcre2_compile_8`, `pcre2_match_8`, `pcre2_dfa_match_8`, `pcre2_next_match_8`, `pcre2_substitute_8`, `pcre2_substring_*`, `pcre2_pattern_info_8`, `pcre2_config_8`, `pcre2_serialize_*`, `pcre2_pattern_convert_8`, `pcre2_maketables_8`, `pcre2_code_copy_8`, `pcre2_code_copy_with_tables_8`, `pcre2_callout_enumerate_8`, `pcre2_get_*`, all context create/copy/free, `pcre2_jit_*` (no-JIT stubs), `pcre2_get_error_message_8`.\n\n## Required format\nShort provenance header, then a \"## Axes\" section briefly listing the axes you derived, then ONE table with EXACTLY these columns:\n\n```\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n```\n\nRules:\n- One row per MEANINGFUL COMBINATION the C actually treats differently (cross-product of the axes, pruned to distinct code paths). NOT one row per option in isolation — combinations are the point (e.g. \"CASELESS+UTF+UCP, multi-byte subject, ovector too small\" is one row).\n- `configuration` must be concrete enough to write a test from without re-reading the C: name the exact option bits, the pattern shape, the subject shape.\n- Last column is a literal `[ ]` checkbox for later Phase-B sign-off.\n- Number rows sequentially from 1.\n- Group into `###` subsections by area (compile, match, dfa_match, substitute, substring, pattern_info, serialize, convert, context, low-level string/utf helpers, tables, jit stubs), with globally sequential numbering and identical columns everywhere.\n\nAim for COMPLETE coverage of distinct code paths; expect 150–300 rows. Bias toward the low-level entry points being represented, not just `pcre2_compile`+`pcre2_match`.\n\nIf the file is too large for one write, create it then append in further calls; ensure the final file is complete and well-formed.\n\nFinally verify your own output: run `grep -c '^| [0-9]' CONFIGS.md` and report the row count in your final message plus a one-paragraph summary of the axes with the most interaction risk.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-tBNRGp-translated-rust/cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7/tasks/a7925d8568189d160.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
