ks.\n\n3. UTF and startoffset handling: what happens for startoffset 0, mid-subject, == length, > length; the UTF check via `PCRE2_UNSET`/`valid_utf`; BADUTFOFFSET conditions; MATCH_INVALID_UTF's separate \"check the subject in segments\" logic.\n\n4. ovector / match_data interaction: oveccount 0, 1, exactly-enough, oversized; `match_data->ovector` fill rules; what happens when there are more captures than ovector slots (`ovecsave`/`capture_top` truncation); `match_data->mark`, `startchar`, `rc` fields; heapframes allocation/growth and `heap_limit`; `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` ovector contents.\n\n5. Limits: match_limit, depth_limit, heap_limit — where each is checked and interactions with pattern-embedded limits from `(*LIMIT_MATCH=)`/`(*LIMIT_DEPTH=)`/`(*LIMIT_HEAP=)`.\n\n6. Interpreter opcode groups that are option/data sensitive and worth separate test rows: backreferences (OP_REF/OP_REFI, with MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF), recursion (OP_RECURSE) + recurse-loop check, atomic groups (OP_ONCE), possessive quantifiers, lookbehinds (fixed/variable, OP_REVERSE/OP_VREVERSE), \\X (OP_EXTUNI), script runs (OP_SCRIPT_RUN), XCLASS/ECLASS, callouts (OP_CALLOUT/OP_CALLOUT_STR) incl. AUTO_CALLOUT, (*MARK)/(*PRUNE)/(*SKIP)/(*THEN)/(*COMMIT)/(*ACCEPT)/(*FAIL), \\b/\\B \\A \\Z \\z \\G, newline handling for `.`/`$`/`^`/\\R under each PCRE2_NEWLINE_* and PCRE2_BSR_* value, OP_ANY vs OP_ALLANY (DOTALL), and \\C (backslash-C) in UTF.\n\nReturn a dense, organized list. Quote exact condition expressions where they are load-bearing. Include line numbers. Do not summarize away detail — I need enough to write tests from."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19516,"cache_read_input_tokens":38797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19516,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013AKCBbobyVBAS3x5b4Hmgw","session_id":"