STRICT, ASCII_BSD, ASCII_BSS, ASCII_BSW, ASCII_POSIX, ASCII_DIGIT, PYTHON_OCTAL, NO_BS0, NEVER_CALLOUT, TURKISH_CASING. For each, the exact construct whose meaning changes.\n\n3. In-pattern option setters that change state mid-compile: `(?i)(?m)(?s)(?x)(?xx)(?J)(?U)(?n)`, `(?-i)` etc, `(?^...)`, `(*UTF)`, `(*UCP)`, `(*NOTEMPTY)`, `(*CR)(*LF)(*CRLF)(*ANY)(*ANYCRLF)(*NUL)`, `(*BSR_UNICODE)(*BSR_ANYCRLF)`, `(*LIMIT_MATCH=n)(*LIMIT_DEPTH=n)(*LIMIT_HEAP=n)`, `(*NO_AUTO_POSSESS)(*NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR)(*NO_START_OPT)`, `(*NO_JIT)`, `(*CASELESS_RESTRICT)`, `(*TURKISH_CASING)`, `(*ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS)`. List each verb the code accepts.\n\n4. Compile-context settings and their effect: `pcre2_set_newline` for each of CR/LF/CRLF/ANY/ANYCRLF/NUL; `pcre2_set_bsr` UNICODE vs ANYCRLF; `pcre2_set_max_varlookbehind`; `pcre2_set_parens_nest_limit`; `pcre2_set_max_pattern_length`; `pcre2_set_max_pattern_compiled_length`; `pcre2_set_character_tables` (default vs pcre2_maketables); `pcre2_set_optimize` (PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_NONE/FULL, AUTO_POSSESS(_OFF), DOTSTAR_ANCHOR(_OFF), START_OPTIMIZE(_OFF)); `pcre2_set_compile_recursion_guard`.\n\n5. Pattern SHAPES the compiler handles on distinct paths, worth one test each: zero-length pattern; PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED length; pattern with NUL bytes inside; single literal char; long literal run (OP_CHAR vs OP_CHARI vs OP_NOT); classes (OP_CLASS, OP_NCLASS, OP_XCLASS, OP_ECLASS) incl. `[[:alpha:]]`, `[\\p{L}]`, `[^...]`, `[]` with ALLOW_EMPTY_CLASS, ranges crossing 0x80/0xFF, caseless class with UCP; extended classes `(?[...])` and ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS `[a && b]`; quantifiers `?`,`*`,`+`,`{n,m}`, possessive, ungreedy; groups: capturing, non-capturing `(?:)`, atomic `(?>)`, `(?|)` duplicate numbers, named `(?<n>)`/`(?'n')`/`(?P<n>)` with DUPNAMES; backreferences `\\1`,`\\g{-1}`,`\\k<n>`,`(?P=n)`; conditions `(?(1))`, `(?(<n>))`, `(?(R))`, `(?(R1))`, `(?(DEFINE))`, `(?(VERSION>=x))`, `(?(?=...))`; lookarounds: `(?=)`,`(?!)`,`(?<=)` fixed-length, `(?<=)` variable-length, `(?<!)`, non-atomic `(*napla:)`/`(*naplb:)`, alpha assertions `(*pla:)(*plb:)(*nla:)(*nlb:)(*atomic:)`; recursion `(?R)`,`(?1)`,`(?&name)`,`(?+1)`,`(?-1)`; `(*script_run:)`/`(*sr:)`/`(*asr:)`; verbs `(*MARK:x)`,`(*ACCEPT)`,`(*FAIL)`,`(*COMMIT)`,`(*PRUNE:x)`,`(*SKIP:x)`,`(*THEN:x)`; callouts `(?C)`,`(?C1)`,`(?C\"str\")` with each delimiter; `\\X`, `\\R`, `\\N`, `\\C`, `\\Q...\\E`, `\\K`, `\\b`,`\\B`,`\\A`,`\\Z`,`\\z`,`\\G`, `\\h\\H\\v\\V\\d\\D\\s\\S\\w\\W`, `\\p{..}`/`\\P{..}`/`\\p{Any}`/script extensions `\\p{scx:..}`, `\\o{}`, `\\x{}`, `\\ddd` octal, `\\cX`, `\\u`/`\\U` under ALT_BSUX; nesting deep enough to exercise parens_nest_limit; patterns large enough to exercise the two-pass parse (parsed_pattern buffer growth) and workspace growth.\n\n6. The auto-possessification and start-optimization/study steps that run at the END of compile: what `_pcre2_study` computes (firstcu/firstcutype/start_bitmap/reqcu/minlength/maxlookbehind/hascrorlf/matchempty), and which patterns exercise each branch. Which patterns make `PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODETYPE` be 0/1/2, `LASTCODETYPE` 0/1, `FIRSTBITMAP` non-NULL vs NULL.\n\n7. `_pcre2_check_escape` — its full API and every distinct escape class it returns, and how options (ALT_BSUX, EXTRA_ALT_BSUX, PYTHON_OCTAL, NO_BS0, ASCII_BSD/BSS/BSW, ALLOW_SURROGATE_ESCAPES, BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL, ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF, UTF, UCP, isclass flag) change its result.\n\nReturn a dense organized list with line numbers and exact condition expressions. This is a big file — be systematic and thorough; use grep -n for each macro. Enough detail to write tests from."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19516,"cache_read_input_tokens":38797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19516,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013AKCBbobyVBAS3x5b4Hmgw","session_id":"cde48455-d5