{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MnmWd1pMQPuwf4ERQyDkUr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Verification of the C -> Rust translation\n2\t\n3\tThe Rust `cdylib` is compared against the reference C build of `c_src/`\n4\t(built with the unmodified `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`).\n5\t\n6\t## 1. ABI / symbol parity\n7\t\n8\t```\n9\t$ ./tools/symdiff.sh <c>/libpcre2.so target/release/libpcre2.so\n10\tC symbols:    143\n11\tRust symbols: 143\n12\t--- missing from Rust:\n13\t--- extra in Rust (informational):\n14\t```\n15\t\n16\t`nm -D --defined-only` produces the identical set of 143 exported symbols with\n17\tidentical symbol *types* (`T`/`R`/`D`), including the macro-generated names such\n18\tas `_pcre2_compile_add_name_to_table8` (no underscore before the `8`) and\n19\t`_pcre2_compile_class_not_nested_8` (with one).\n20\t\n21\t## 2. Data tables are byte-identical\n22\t\n23\t`tools/dump_tables.c` dlopens a library and dumps every exported data table\n24\t(`_pcre2_ucd_records_8`, `_pcre2_ucd_stage1_8`, `_pcre2_ucd_stage2_8`,\n25\t`_pcre2_utt_8`, `_pcre2_utt_names_8`, `_pcre2_default_tables_8`,\n26\t`_pcre2_OP_lengths_8`, `_pcre2_ucd_*_sets_8`, ...). The dumps of the C and the\n27\tRust library are byte-for-byte equal (28 tables, ~120 KB of data).\n28\t\n29\t## 3. Structure layout parity\n30\t\n31\t`src/internal.rs` ends with `const _: () = assert!(...)` static assertions for\n32\tthe size of every shared structure and the offset of every field that the code\n33\tcomputes with `offsetof` (verified against the C build with a generated C\n34\tprogram): `pcre2_real_code` = 152, `heapframe` = 1048696,\n35\t`offset_of!(heapframe, ovector)` = 120, `match_block` = 272, `compile_block` =\n36\t360, etc. A layout regression therefore breaks the build.\n37\t\n38\t## 4. Differential behaviour tests\n39\t\n40\tAll harnesses dlopen **both** libraries and compare results call by call.\n41\t\n42\t| harness | what it covers | result |\n43\t|---|---|---|\n44\t| `tools/diffharness.c` | 135 curated patterns x 32 subjects x 9 match option sets: compile error code+offset, **the compiled byte code compared byte for byte**, all `pcre2_pattern_info()` items, `pcre2_match`, `pcre2_dfa_match`, ovectors, marks, startchar, `pcre2_substitute` (11 replacement/option combinations), substring extraction, substring lists, `pcre2_next_match`, match-data sizes, serialize/deserialize round trip, `pcre2_pattern_convert` (15 cases), `pcre2_config` (all 17 items), `pcre2_get_error_message` (all codes -80..230), `pcre2_maketables` | **116,595 checks, 0 mismatches** |\n45\t| `tools/apiharness.c` | `pcre2_callout_enumerate` (full callback log), `substring_*_byname`, `substring_nametable_scan`, `substring_length/copy_bynumber`, serialize with many codes + **cross-library decode**, compile with `pcre2_maketables`-generated tables, `code_copy_with_tables`, `next_match` loops, JIT stubs, general contexts | **1,556 checks, 0 mismatches** |\n46\t| `tools/fuzzharness.c`, `tools/fuzzharness2.c` | pseudo-random patterns built from ~160 syntax fragments x random subjects (incl. long subjects, invalid UTF-8) x random compile/extra/match options, newline and BSR conventions, optimization directives, match/depth/heap/offset limits, callouts and substitute callouts (the whole callback sequence is logged and compared), plus compiled-byte-code comparison | ~20 seeds x 20,000 iterations = **~4.6 million checks, 0 mismatches** |\n47\t\n48\tNotes on what is deliberately *not* compared: PCRE2 leaves some memory\n49\tuninitialised (the ovector when there is no match, the mark/startchar fields\n50\tafter a failed match, and the 0-3 alignment padding bytes between the name table\n51\tand the character lists inside a compiled pattern). Those regions contain\n52\twhatever the allocator returned, so they are excluded; everything else,\n53\tincluding every emitted opcode byte, is compared exactly.\n54\t\n55\t## Reproducing\n56\t\n57\t```sh\n58\tmkdir -p /tmp/cref && cd /tmp/cref && cmake <repo>/c_src -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && make\n59\tcd <repo> && cargo build --release\n60\tgcc -O1 tools/diffharness.c  -o /tmp/diffharness  -ldl\n61\tgcc -O1 tools/apiharness.c   -o /tmp/apiharness   -ldl\n62\tgcc -O1 tools/fuzzharness2.c -o /tmp/fuzzharness2 -ldl\n63\t/tmp/diffharness  /tmp/cref/libpcre2.so target/release/libpcre2.so\n64\t/tmp/apiharness   /tmp/cref/libpcre2.so target/release/libpcre2.so\n65\t/tmp/fuzzharness2 /tmp/cref/libpcre2.so target/release/libpcre2.so 20000 1\n66\t./tools/symdiff.sh /tmp/cref/libpcre2.so target/release/libpcre2.so\n67\t```\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013AKCBbobyVBAS3x5b4Hmgw","session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7","uuid":"8a0035a3-884e-4bc1-9644-da0bd9a5b235","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:15:59.420Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Produce CONFIGS.md configuration surface"}
