{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a821ee550f1ed45d8","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01D3mKNSZPQUyDpwNcVKFi6h","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-tBNRGp-translated-rust/cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7/tasks/a821ee550f1ed45d8.output","summary":"# Configuration-surface analysis of `pcre2_match()` — 8-bit, SUPPORT_UNICODE on, no JIT, LINK_SIZE=2\n\nAll line numbers refer to `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/translated_rust/c_src/src/pcre2_match.c` unless a different file is named.\n\nBuild facts that gate `#ifdef` blocks in your configuration:\n- `SUPPORT_JIT` **undefined** (`c_src/src/config.h:347`) → the whole \"JIT matching\" block (7008–7010, 7021–7023, 7090–7093, 7148–7242) is compiled out. `use_jit`, `jit_checked_utf` do not exist. `PCRE2_NO_JIT` is a *legal* option bit but is **never tested** anywhere in the library (only appears in `PUBLIC_MATCH_OPTIONS`, line 74) → pure no-op.\n- 8-bit + `SUPPORT_UNICODE` ⇒ `SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS` is defined (`pcre2_intmodedep.h:231-240`) ⇒ `OP_XCLASS` (2294) and `OP_ECLASS` (2436) **are** compiled in, along with RM100–RM103.\n- `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 8` ⇒ `memchr_found_first_cu/…cu2` caches exist (6988–6991), all `memchr` fast paths are live, `#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH != 8` search loops are dead, `REQ_CU_MAX == 5000` (`pcre2_internal.h:550`).\n- `LINK_SIZE=2` (`config.h:178`) ⇒ `GET/PUT` are 2-byte; group headers are `1 + LINK_SIZE = 3`; callout string fields at `1 + 3*LINK_SIZE`, `1 + 4*LINK_SIZE` (316–319).\n- Not EBCDIC ⇒ `0x2028`/`0x2029` cases live in `\\R`/`ANYNL` (2672–2673, 3328–3329, 4801, 5028 — note 5028 is `#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH != 8`, so in 8-bit the non-UTF `ANYNL` max-repeat loop does **not** test 0x2028/0x2029; a real behavioural axis).\n- Defaults: `MATCH_LIMIT 10000000`, `MATCH_LIMIT_DEPTH == MATCH_LIMIT`, `HEAP_LIMIT 20000000` (KiB) (`config.h:169,195,209`), installed in `PRIV(default_match_context)` (`pcre2_context.c:163-178`) with `offset_limit = PCRE2_UNSET`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Outer `pcre2_match()` — every option bit and gate, in execution order\n\n### 1.0 Pre-option plausibility gates (ordering is load-bearing for tests)\n\n| Line | Condition | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 7038 | `if (subject == NULL && length == 0) subject = null_str;` | NULL+0 is legal; `subject` becomes an internal 1-byte buffer `{0xcd}`. `original_subject` (7999) still holds **NULL**, so on success/nomatch `match_data->subject` is set back to NULL (8202/8224/8239). |\n| 7042 | `match_data == NULL` | `return PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` — **`match_data->rc` not written** (can't be). |\n| 7043 | `code == NULL \\|\\| subject == NULL` | `match_data->rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` |\n| 7045 | `(options & ~PUBLIC_MATCH_OPTIONS) != 0` | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`. `PUBLIC_MATCH_OPTIONS` (71–75) = `ANCHORED(0x80000000) \\| ENDANCHORED(0x20000000) \\| NOTBOL(0x1) \\| NOTEOL(0x2) \\| NOTEMPTY(0x4) \\| NOTEMPTY_ATSTART(0x8) \\| NO_UTF_CHECK(0x40000000) \\| PARTIAL_HARD(0x20) \\| PARTIAL_SOFT(0x10) \\| NO_JIT(0x2000) \\| COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT(0x4000) \\| DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK(0x40000)` = **0xE0044037**. Every other listed option (NO_START_OPTIMIZE, FIRSTLINE, USE_OFFSET_LIMIT, MATCH_INVALID_UTF, UTF, UCP, DOLLAR_ENDONLY, ALT_CIRCUMFLEX, MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF, CASELESS, MULTILINE, DOTALL…) passed at match time ⇒ **BADOPTION**. |\n| 7048–7049 | `start_match = subject + start_offset; req_cu_ptr = start_match - 1;` | Computed before validation. |\n| 7050–7053 | `length == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` | `length = PRIV(strlen)(subject)` |\n| 7054 | `true_end_subject = end_subject = subject + length;` | |\n| 7056 | `start_offset > length` | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET`. Note `start_offset == length` is **legal**. |\n| 7060 | `re->magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER` | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC` — checked **after** BADOFFSET |\n| 7065 | `(re->flags & PCRE2_MODE_MASK) != PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH/8` | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE` |\n\n### 1.1 Pattern-embedded match options folded in\n\n7080–7084:\n```c\n#define FF (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_SET|PCRE2_NE_ATST_SET)\n#define OO (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY|PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART)\noptions |= (re->flags & FF) / ((FF & (~FF+1)) / (OO & (~OO+1)));\n```\n`(*NOTEMPTY)` / `(*NOTEMPTY_ATSTART)` in the pattern set `options` bits 0x4 / 0x8 here. **Test axis:** identical behaviour whether the bit comes from `options` or from the pattern verb. Note `original_options` (6980) was snapshotted *before* this, and is what lands in `match_data->options` (8171).\n\n### 1.2 UTF/UCP/invalid-UTF state (7097–7101)\n```c\nutf         = (re->overall_options & PCRE2_UTF) != 0;\nallow_invalid = (re->overall_options & PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF) != 0;\nucp         = (re->overall_options & PCRE2_UCP) != 0;\n```\nAll three are **compile-time only**. `utf` feeds `IS_NEWLINE`/`WAS_NEWLINE`/`ACROSSCHAR`. `ucp` is used **only** for the caseless first_cu / req_cu othercase computation in this function (7566, 7588) — note the 8-bit-specific condition `if (first_cu > 127 && ucp && !utf) first_cu2 = UCD_OTHERCASE(first_cu);` (i.e. UCP-without-UTF, 8-bit only). `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` also implies `PCRE2_UTF` at compile time.\n\n### 1.3 Partial matching (7105–7113)\n```c\nmb->partial = ((options & PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD) != 0)? 2 :\n              ((options & PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT) != 0)? 1 : 0;\n```\n**HARD wins over SOFT** when both are given. Then:\n```c\nif (mb->partial != 0 && ((re->overall_options | options) & PCRE2_ENDANCHORED) != 0)\n  return match_data->rc = PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION;\n```\n⇒ 3 distinct rows (0/1/2) × ENDANCHORED-from-compile / -from-match / neither. Note ENDANCHORED from **either** source triggers the error.\n\n### 1.4 Offset limit (7118–7120)\n```c\nif (mcontext != NULL && mcontext->offset_limit != PCRE2_UNSET &&\n     (re->overall_options & PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT) == 0)\n  return match_data->rc = PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSETLIMIT;\n```\n`PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT` is compile-only. Rows: (no mcontext) / (mcontext, limit UNSET) / (mcontext, limit set, USE_OFFSET_LIMIT set) / (mcontext, limit set, USE_OFFSET_LIMIT clear ⇒ error).\n\n### 1.5 `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` — three touch points\n- 7126–7131: if `(match_data->flags & PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT) != 0` from a *previous* call, `free()` the old copy and clear the flag. **Test row: reuse the same match_data twice with COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT.**\n- 7132: `match_data->subject = NULL;` unconditionally, then 7136 `match_data->startchar = 0;`.\n- 8188–8201 (success only): if set and `length != 0`, `malloc(CU2BYTES(length))` + `memcpy`, set `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT`; **malloc failure ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`** overriding the successful match. If `length == 0` the copy is skipped, `match_data->subject = NULL`, **but the flag is still set** (8200) — a subsequent call will `free(NULL)`.\n- On partial/nomatch/error paths COPY is **ignored**; `match_data->subject = original_subject` (8224, 8239) or left NULL for hard errors.\n\n### 1.6 Anchoring / firstline / startline / bumpalong limit (7397–7401)\n```c\nanchored  = ((re->overall_options | options) & PCRE2_ANCHORED) != 0;\nfirstline = !anchored && (re->overall_options & PCRE2_FIRSTLINE) != 0;\nstartline = (re->flags & PCRE2_STARTLINE) != 0;\nbumpalong_limit = (mcontext->offset_limit == PCRE2_UNSET)?\n  true_end_subject : subject + mcontext->offset_limit;\n```\n- `PCRE2_ANCHORED` from *either* compile or match options. Also set implicitly by `is_anchored()` at compile time (`pcre2_compile.c:11112-11113`, gated by `PCRE2_OPTIM_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR`).\n- `PCRE2_FIRSTLINE` is **compile-only** and is **suppressed by anchoring** — `firstline && anchored` is unreachable.\n- `startline` = `PCRE2_STARTLINE` flag computed by the compiler only when `PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE` is on and the pattern is unanchored (`pcre2_compile.c:11196-11200`).\n- `bumpalong_limit` uses `true_end_subject`, so it is **not** clamped by the invalid-UTF fragment end.\n\n### 1.7 `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` / `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` gate (7270–7274)\n```c\nif (utf && ((options & PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK) == 0 || allow_invalid))\n```\n⇒ `allow_invalid` **overrides** `NO_UTF_CHECK`; the check always runs under MATCH_INVALID_UTF. Non-UTF patterns never check. 4 rows: {utf, !utf} × {NO_UTF_CHECK, !NO_UTF_CHECK} × {allow_invalid, !allow_invalid}.\n\n### 1.8 `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` (7625)\n```c\nif ((re->optimization_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE) != 0)\n```\nCompile-time; `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` clears the bit (`pcre2_compile.c:10414-10415`), as does `(*NO_START_OPT)` (`pcre2_compile.c:749`) and `pcre2_set_optimize(ctx, PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE, off)`. When off: no firstline scan, no first-CU/bitmap scan, no minlength check, no req_cu check — every position from `start_offset` is tried, so every callout fires. Also, with the bit off at compile time, `re->flags` never gets FIRSTSET/FIRSTMAPSET/STARTLINE/LASTSET and `re->minlength` stays 0 (`pcre2_compile.c:11122`), so `has_first_cu`/`start_bits`/`has_req_cu` are all false anyway.\n\n### 1.9 `PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK`\nOnly used inside `match()` at 5728 (see §6.2). Passed through as `mb->moptions` (7965).\n\n### 1.10 Options **not** tested in the outer function but read in `match()` from `mb->poptions`/`mb->moptions`\n`mb->poptions = re->overall_options` (7428); `mb->moptions = options | fragment_options` (7965).\n\n| Option | Where tested | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY`, `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` | 983–992 (`OP_END`/`OP_ACCEPT`) — `Feptr == Fstart_match && ((moptions & NOTEMPTY) != 0 \\|\\| ((moptions & NOTEMPTY_ATSTART) != 0 && Fstart_match == mb->start_subject + mb->start_offset))` | `RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH)` → backtracks into other alternatives, then bumpalong |\n| `PCRE2_ENDANCHORED` | 999–1014 — `Feptr < mb->end_subject && ((moptions\\|poptions) & ENDANCHORED)`; `if (Fop == OP_END) RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH); else return MATCH_NOMATCH;` | Note: after `(*ACCEPT)` it **hard-returns** (aborts this start position entirely) instead of backtracking |\n| `PCRE2_NOTBOL` | 6571 (`OP_CIRC`: `Feptr != mb->start_subject \\|\\| (moptions & NOTBOL)`), 6638 (`OP_CIRCM`: `(moptions & NOTBOL) != 0 && Feptr == mb->start_subject`) | `^` fails at subject start |\n| `PCRE2_NOTEOL` | 6585 (`OP_DOLL`), 6670 (`OP_DOLLM`, only when `Feptr >= mb->end_subject`) | `$` fails at end |\n| `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` | 6586 — `if ((poptions & DOLLAR_ENDONLY) == 0) goto ASSERT_NL_OR_EOS;` else fall into `OP_EOD` | `$` == `\\z` instead of `\\Z` |\n| `PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX` | 6640–6644 — `Feptr != start_subject && ((Feptr == mb->end_subject && (poptions & ALT_CIRCUMFLEX) == 0) \\|\\| !WAS_NEWLINE(Feptr))` | permits `^` to match after a final newline |\n| `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF` | 375 (`match_ref`, unset group ⇒ zero-length match), 5333 (repeated ref: `Lmin == 0 \\|\\| (poptions & MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF)` ⇒ `continue`) | |\n| `PCRE2_UTF` | 724, 393 | code-unit vs character stepping |\n| `PCRE2_UCP` | 725, 397 | property-based caseless/word tests without UTF |\n| `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK` | 7426, 1029 | `\\K` outside its lookaround ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` unless set |\n\n### 1.11 Other `re->flags`/fields latched into `mb` (7418–7438) — all separate test axes\n`mb->hasthen = (re->flags & PCRE2_HASTHEN)` (7422, gates the OP_BRA fast path at 5623); `mb->hasbsk = (re->flags & PCRE2_HASBSK)` (7423); `mb->allowemptypartial = (re->max_lookbehind > 0) || (re->flags & PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY)` (7424 — controls `SCHECK_PARTIAL` at 626); `mb->ignore_skip_arg = 0` (7429); `mb->mark = mb->nomatch_mark = NULL` (7430); name table/`name_count`/`name_entry_size` (7435–7437); `mb->start_code` (7438).\n\n### 1.12 Newline / `\\R` conventions (7442–7480)\n```c\nmb->bsr_convention = re->bsr_convention;      /* PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE=1 | PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF=2 */\nmb->nltype = NLTYPE_FIXED;\nswitch(re->newline_convention) {\n  CR   -> nllen=1, nl[0]=CR\n  LF   -> nllen=1, nl[0]=NL\n  NUL  -> nllen=1, nl[0]=NUL\n  CRLF -> nllen=2, nl[0]=CR, nl[1]=NL\n  ANY     -> nltype = NLTYPE_ANY      (nllen left uninitialized until is_newline sets it)\n  ANYCRLF -> nltype = NLTYPE_ANYCRLF\n  default -> PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL     /* line 7478 */\n}\n```\n6 × 2 = **12 newline/BSR combinations**, each of which changes `IS_NEWLINE`/`WAS_NEWLINE` (`pcre2_internal.h:473-497`: fixed form is `p <= PSEND - nllen && *p == nl[0] && (nllen==1 || p[1]==nl[1])`; ANY/ANYCRLF go through `PRIV(is_newline)` and **write back** `mb->nllen`). Consumers: `OP_ANY` (1062), `OP_EODN`/`ASSERT_NL_OR_EOS` (6605–6606), `OP_CIRCM` (6643), `OP_DOLLM` (6654), firstline scan (7639/7647), startline scan (7791/7799), the bumpalong CRLF skip (8069–8077), the firstline break (8051). `bsr_convention` consumers: 2675, 3331, 4137, 4268, 4798, 5025.\n\n### 1.13 `mcontext == NULL` (7390–7395)\n```c\nif (mcontext == NULL) { mcontext = &PRIV(default_match_context); mb->memctl = re->memctl; }\nelse mb->memctl = mcontext->memctl;\n```\n**Axis:** which allocator is used for heapframe growth — the *pattern's* memctl when `mcontext == NULL`, otherwise the *context's*. Note `match_data->memctl` (a third one) is what actually allocates `heapframes` in the outer function (7530–7533) and in `MATCH_RECURSE` (792, 799).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Start-of-match optimization block (7614–7954)\n\nThe bumpalong loop is `for(;;)` at 7614. Everything below is inside `if ((re->optimization_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE) != 0)` (7625) except §2.7.\n\n### 2.1 firstline temporary end clamp (7633–7649)\n```c\nif (firstline) {\n  PCRE2_SPTR t = start_match;\n  if (utf) { while (t < end_subject && !IS_NEWLINE(t)) { t++; ACROSSCHAR(t < end_subject, t, t++); } }\n  else       while (t < end_subject && !IS_NEWLINE(t)) t++;\n  end_subject = t;\n}\n```\nRestored at 7843 (`end_subject = mb->end_subject;`) — i.e. only the *scans* see the clamped end, `match()` sees the full `mb->end_subject`. **UTF vs non-UTF are separate code paths.** Recomputed on **every** bumpalong iteration (start_match moves forward, so `t` re-scans).\n\n### 2.2 Anchored + (first CU or bitmap) pre-check (7655–7678)\n```c\nif (anchored) {\n  if (has_first_cu || start_bits != NULL) {\n    BOOL ok = start_match < end_subject;\n    if (ok) { PCRE2_UCHAR c = *start_match;\n              ok = has_first_cu && (c == first_cu || c == first_cu2);\n              if (!ok && start_bits != NULL) ok = (start_bits[c/8] & (1u << (c&7))) != 0; }\n    if (!ok) { rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break; } } }\n```\nNote `has_first_cu` and `start_bits != NULL` are mutually exclusive in practice (7557–7575: `start_bits` only assigned in the `else` of `PCRE2_FIRSTSET`, and only when `!startline`) — so the \"both\" arm is dead but present. In 8-bit the `if (c > 255) c = 255;` clamp (7667) is compiled out.\n\n### 2.3 Unanchored, `has_first_cu`, **caseless** (`first_cu != first_cu2`) — 8-bit dual-memchr with caching (7705–7745)\n```c\nPCRE2_SPTR pp1 = NULL, pp2 = NULL;\nPCRE2_SIZE searchlength = end_subject - start_match;\nif (memchr_found_first_cu == NULL || start_match > memchr_found_first_cu)\n  { pp1 = memchr(start_match, first_cu, searchlength);\n    memchr_found_first_cu = (pp1 == NULL)? end_subject : pp1; }\nelse pp1 = (memchr_found_first_cu == end_subject)? NULL : memchr_found_first_cu;\n/* same for cu2 into memchr_found_first_cu2 */\nif (pp1 == NULL) start_match = (pp2 == NULL)? end_subject : pp2;\nelse             start_match = (pp2 == NULL || pp1 < pp2)? pp1 : pp2;\n```\nThe caches are reset to NULL at 7610–7611 (before the loop **and** on every `FRAGMENT_RESTART`). **Test rows:** (a) only the lower case present, (b) only the upper case present, (c) both present with each ordering, (d) neither present, (e) ≥3 bumpalong iterations so the cache-hit branches (7723, 7735) execute, (f) a firstline-clamped `end_subject` interacting with a cached `== end_subject` sentinel — note the sentinel is compared against the *current* (possibly clamped, possibly restored) `end_subject`, which differs between iterations under FIRSTLINE.\n\n`first_cu2` is produced at 7561–7571: `first_cu2 = TABLE_GET(first_cu, mb->fcc, first_cu)` plus the 8-bit UCP-not-UTF override `if (first_cu > 127 && ucp && !utf) first_cu2 = UCD_OTHERCASE(first_cu);`. So in 8-bit **UTF** mode a `first_cu > 127` keeps the flip-table value only.\n\n### 2.4 Unanchored, `has_first_cu`, **caseful** (7757–7760)\n```c\nstart_match = memchr(start_match, first_cu, end_subject - start_match);\nif (start_match == NULL) start_match = end_subject;\n```\nNo cache.\n\n### 2.5 The \"not found\" break, with partial/firstline escape hatch (7774–7778)\n```c\nif (mb->partial == 0 && start_match >= mb->end_subject) { rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break; }\n```\nCompares against `mb->end_subject` (the **true** fragment end), not the firstline-clamped `end_subject`. So: (i) `partial != 0` ⇒ still run the attempt at the end (needed for `/(?<=abc)def/` partially matching `\"abc\"`); (ii) FIRSTLINE clamped ⇒ `start_match < mb->end_subject` ⇒ still run, because a match may legitimately start with the first CU of a newline.\n\n### 2.6 Unanchored, no first CU: `startline` bump (7784–7811) and `start_bits` bitmap (7819–7838)\n```c\nelse if (startline) {\n  if (start_match > mb->start_subject + start_offset) {      /* skip on the first iteration */\n    if (utf) { while (start_match < end_subject && !WAS_NEWLINE(start_match))\n                 { start_match++; ACROSSCHAR(start_match < end_subject, start_match, start_match++); } }\n    else       while (start_match < end_subject && !WAS_NEWLINE(start_match)) start_match++;\n    if (start_match[-1] == CHAR_CR &&\n        (mb->nltype == NLTYPE_ANY || mb->nltype == NLTYPE_ANYCRLF) &&\n        start_match < end_subject && *start_match == CHAR_NL) start_match++; } }\nelse if (start_bits != NULL) {\n  while (start_match < end_subject) {\n    uint32_t c = *start_match;\n    if ((start_bits[c/8] & (1u << (c&7))) != 0) break;\n    start_match++; }\n  if (mb->partial == 0 && start_match >= mb->end_subject) { rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break; } }\n```\nNote the strict `else if` chain: **`has_first_cu` beats `startline` beats `start_bits`** (7684 / 7784 / 7819). `start_bits` is only non-NULL when `!startline` (7574), so the third arm is reachable only in that case. `start_bits` is a 256-bit map indexed by code unit; in 8-bit no `>255` clamp. `startline` has **no** \"not found ⇒ break\" check — it relies on the `start_match > end_subject` test at 8060.\n\n### 2.7 `re->minlength` check (7847–7860) — disabled for partial\n```c\nif (mb->partial == 0) {\n  if (end_subject - start_match < re->minlength) { rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break; }\n```\n`end_subject` here is the **restored** `mb->end_subject` (7843). Measured in *code units* even though `minlength` is in characters (deliberate; a UTF axis). `minlength` is only nonzero when START_OPTIMIZE was enabled at compile time.\n\n### 2.8 `req_cu` \"last code unit\" check (7862–7942)\n```c\np = start_match + (has_first_cu? 1:0);\nif (has_req_cu && p > req_cu_ptr) {\n  PCRE2_SIZE check_length = end_subject - start_match;\n  if (check_length < REQ_CU_MAX || (!anchored && check_length < REQ_CU_MAX * 1000)) {\n    if (req_cu != req_cu2) {            /* caseless: single memchr per case, no cache */\n      PCRE2_SPTR pp = p;\n      p = memchr(pp, req_cu, end_subject - pp);\n      if (p == NULL) { p = memchr(pp, req_cu2, end_subject - pp); if (p == NULL) p = end_subject; } }\n    else { p = memchr(p, req_cu, end_subject - p); if (p == NULL) p = end_subject; }\n    if (p >= end_subject) { rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break; }\n    req_cu_ptr = p; } }\n```\nAxes: `has_first_cu` (skips one CU) × caseless/caseful × `anchored` × `check_length` vs **5000** and **5,000,000** (8-bit `REQ_CU_MAX`) × `p > req_cu_ptr` cache state across bumpalong iterations (`req_cu_ptr` is initialised to `start_match - 1` at 7049 and only ever advances). Unlike the first-CU caseless path, this does **not** find the earliest occurrence — presence only. Both this and §2.7 are inside `if (mb->partial == 0)`.\n\n### 2.9 offset_limit / bumpalong limit (7950–7954)\n```c\nif (start_match > bumpalong_limit) { rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break; }\n```\nOutside the START_OPTIMIZE guard ⇒ **offset limit still applies with NO_START_OPTIMIZE**. Strict `>`, so a match starting exactly at `offset_limit` is allowed.\n\n### 2.10 Per-attempt state reset (7959–7971) and the bumpalong result switch (7990–8080)\n```c\ncb.start_match = start_match - subject;  cb.callout_flags |= PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH;\nmb->start_used_ptr = mb->last_used_ptr = start_match;\nmb->moptions = options | fragment_options;\nmb->match_call_count = 0;   /* NB: match_limit is per start position, not per pcre2_match call */\nmb->end_offset_top = 0;  mb->skip_arg_count = 0;\nrc = match(start_match, mb->start_code, re->top_bracket, frame_size, match_data, mb);\nif (mb->hitend && start_partial == NULL) { start_partial = mb->start_used_ptr; match_partial = start_match; }\n```\n- `MATCH_SKIP_ARG` (7999): `new_start_match = start_match` (retry same position), `mb->ignore_skip_arg = mb->skip_arg_count`.\n- `MATCH_SKIP` (8007): `if (mb->verb_skip_ptr > start_match) new_start_match = mb->verb_skip_ptr;` else fall through to NOMATCH.\n- `MATCH_NOMATCH`/`MATCH_PRUNE`/`MATCH_THEN` (8018–8028): `mb->ignore_skip_arg = 0; new_start_match = start_match + 1;` plus `if (utf) ACROSSCHAR(new_start_match < end_subject, new_start_match, new_start_match++);`\n- `MATCH_COMMIT` (8032): `rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; goto ENDLOOP;` (no bumpalong).\n- default (8038): `goto ENDLOOP` (match or error).\n- 8051: `if (firstline && IS_NEWLINE(start_match)) break;` — FIRSTLINE stops after failing *at* a newline.\n- 8060: `if (anchored || start_match > end_subject) break;` — note `>` not `>=`, so the position exactly at `end_subject` is tried.\n- 8069–8077 CRLF skip: `start_match > subject + start_offset && start_match[-1] == CHAR_CR && start_match < end_subject && *start_match == CHAR_NL && (re->flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF) == 0 && (nltype == ANY || nltype == ANYCRLF || nllen == 2)` ⇒ `start_match++`. **5 independent conditions ⇒ 5 negative test rows**, plus the `PCRE2_HASCRORLF` axis (pattern contains a literal `\\r` or `\\n`).\n- 8079: `mb->mark = NULL;` per attempt.\n\n---\n\n## 3. UTF and startoffset handling\n\n### 3.1 `start_offset` cases\n| Case | Path |\n|---|---|\n| `0` | `start_match == subject`; `req_cu_ptr = subject - 1` (one-before pointer, benign). UTF first-CU check at 7293: if `NOT_FIRSTCU(*subject)` and `start_offset == 0` ⇒ **`PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR20`** (isolated 0x80 byte), *not* BADUTFOFFSET. |\n| mid-subject, on a character boundary | `mb->check_subject` walks back `re->max_lookbehind` **characters** (7317–7327 loop: decrement once per char, then `while ((*p & 0xc0) == 0x80) p--`), so lookbehinds may read before `start_offset` but never before `subject`. |\n| mid-subject, mid-character, `!allow_invalid` | 7293–7301: `start_match < end_subject && NOT_FIRSTCU(*start_match)` and `start_offset > 0` ⇒ **`PCRE2_ERROR_BADUTFOFFSET`**. |\n| mid-character, `allow_invalid` | 7285–7292: `while (start_match < end_subject && NOT_FIRSTCU(*start_match)) { start_match++; skipped_bad_start = TRUE; }` ⇒ silently advances, and `skipped_bad_start` **suppresses the max_lookbehind rewind** (7314). |\n| `== length` | `start_match == end_subject`; the `start_match < end_subject` guard makes all first-CU checks no-ops; `check_subject = end_subject` then rewound by max_lookbehind; `valid_utf` runs over the tail. Optimizations: memchr on length 0 ⇒ NULL ⇒ `start_match = end_subject`; if `mb->partial == 0` ⇒ immediate NOMATCH break; `minlength > 0` ⇒ NOMATCH break. |\n| `> length` | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` (7056). |\n| `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` length + offset past the NUL | `length` is recomputed first, so this is BADOFFSET. |\n\n### 3.2 `valid_utf` loop (7345–7383)\n```c\nfor (;;) {\n  rc = PRIV(valid_utf)(mb->check_subject, length - (mb->check_subject - subject), &match_data->startchar);\n  if (rc == 0) break;\n  match_data->startchar += mb->check_subject - subject;      /* absolutize */\n  if (!allow_invalid || rc > 0) return match_data->rc = rc;  /* rc>0 = \"not a UTF error\" (never happens for valid_utf) */\n  end_subject = subject + match_data->startchar;\n  if (end_subject < start_match) {                          /* bad UTF inside the lookbehind region */\n    mb->check_subject = end_subject + 1;\n    while (mb->check_subject < start_match && NOT_FIRSTCU(*mb->check_subject)) mb->check_subject++;\n    end_subject = true_end_subject; }                       /* retry */\n  else { fragment_options = PCRE2_NOTEOL; break; } }\n```\nError codes surface as `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR1..21` with `match_data->startchar` = absolute code-unit offset of the bad sequence. `match_data->startchar` is pre-zeroed at 7136 \"in case the first code unit is invalid UTF\".\n\n### 3.3 MATCH_INVALID_UTF segment logic (8109–8163)\n```c\nif (utf && end_subject != true_end_subject && (rc == MATCH_NOMATCH || rc == PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL)) {\n  for (;;) {\n    start_match = end_subject + 1;\n    while (start_match < true_end_subject && NOT_FIRSTCU(*start_match)) start_match++;\n    if (start_match >= true_end_subject) { rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; match_partial = NULL; break; }\n    mb->check_subject = start_match;\n    rc = PRIV(valid_utf)(start_match, length - (start_match - subject), &match_data->startchar);\n    if (rc == 0) { mb->end_subject = end_subject = true_end_subject;\n                   fragment_options = PCRE2_NOTBOL; goto FRAGMENT_RESTART; }\n    else if (rc < 0) { mb->end_subject = end_subject = start_match + match_data->startchar;\n                       if (end_subject > start_match) { fragment_options = PCRE2_NOTBOL|PCRE2_NOTEOL;\n                                                        goto FRAGMENT_RESTART; } } } }\n```\n`FRAGMENT_RESTART` (7603) re-executes `start_partial = match_partial = NULL; mb->hitend = FALSE;` and clears both memchr caches. Distinct fragment_options states worth separate rows: **`0`** (first fragment, whole string valid), **`NOTEOL`** (first fragment, bad UTF later), **`NOTBOL`** (last fragment), **`NOTBOL|NOTEOL`** (middle fragment). Consequences: a partial match in a non-final fragment is discarded and matching continues; `\\z`/`\\Z` (`OP_EOD`/`OP_EODN`, 6592/6605) compare against `mb->true_end_subject` which is never shrunk, so they can only succeed at the real end; `^`(OP_CIRC) fails in later fragments via NOTBOL; `\\A`(OP_SOD, 6577) compares to `mb->start_subject` (the original `subject`) so it can only match at absolute offset 0; `\\G`(OP_SOM, 6681) compares to `mb->start_subject + mb->start_offset`, i.e. the **original** start_offset, not the fragment start.\n\nAlso note `mb->check_subject = subject` default (7251) when no UTF check runs — this is what `OP_REVERSE` (6200) and the word-boundary \"previous char\" test (6706) clamp against. So `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` + non-zero `start_offset` **changes how far lookbehind may reach**: with a check, `check_subject` = start_match minus max_lookbehind chars; without, `check_subject == subject`. `OP_VREVERSE` (6246/6262) uses `mb->start_subject` instead — an inconsistency worth a test row.\n\n---\n\n## 4. ovector / match_data interaction\n\n- `oveccount` is a `uint16_t` (`pcre2_intmodedep.h:712`). `pcre2_match_data_create` clamps: `if (oveccount < 1) oveccount = 1; if (oveccount > UINT16_MAX) oveccount = UINT16_MAX;` (`pcre2_match_data.c:57-58`). **So oveccount 0 is impossible via the public API**; `..._create_from_pattern` uses `top_bracket + 1` (`:86`).\n- Success fill (1045–1053, in `OP_END`):\n```c\nmatch_data->ovector[0] = Fstart_match - mb->start_subject;\nmatch_data->ovector[1] = Feptr - mb->start_subject;\ni = 2 * ((top_bracket + 1 > match_data->oveccount)? match_data->oveccount : top_bracket + 1);\nmemcpy(match_data->ovector + 2, Fovector, (i - 2) * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));\nwhile (--i >= Foffset_top + 2) match_data->ovector[i] = PCRE2_UNSET;\nreturn MATCH_MATCH;\n```\n  Rows: `oveccount == 1` (only pair 0 written, memcpy of 0 bytes, trailing loop no-op); `oveccount == top_bracket+1` (exact); `oveccount > top_bracket+1` (**slots beyond `top_bracket+1` are left completely untouched** — stale from a previous match); `oveccount < top_bracket+1` (truncation).\n- Return code (8180–8181): `match_data->rc = ((int)mb->end_offset_top >= 2*match_data->oveccount)? 0 : (int)mb->end_offset_top/2 + 1;` ⇒ **0 means \"matched but ovector too small\"**, which is what your \"more captures than slots\" row must assert. Note this is driven by `end_offset_top` (highest *set* capture), not by `top_bracket` — so an oversubscribed pattern whose high groups didn't participate still returns a positive count.\n- Gaps: unparticipating groups *below* `Foffset_top` are `PCRE2_UNSET` because the first frame's ovector was memset to 0xff (7545–7546: `memset((char*)heapframes + offsetof(heapframe,ovector), 0xff, frame_size - offsetof(heapframe,ovector))`) and copied frame-to-frame; groups *above* `Foffset_top` are explicitly set by the `while (--i …)` loop.\n- Captures are written at `OP_KET` for CBRA (6516–6520) and at `OP_CLOSE` (916–920), both doing `if (offset >= Foffset_top) Foffset_top = offset + 2;` and `Fcapture_last = number`.\n- Other fields on success (8182–8187): `subject_length = length`, `start_offset = start_offset`, `startchar = start_match - subject` (the bumpalong position, **not** ovector[0] when `\\K` moved it), `leftchar = mb->start_used_ptr - subject`, `rightchar = max(mb->last_used_ptr, mb->end_match_ptr) - subject`.\n- Always set (8168–8171): `code`, `mark = mb->mark`, `matchedby = PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_INTERPRETER`, `options = original_options` (pre-(*NOTEMPTY) fold).\n- `mark`: 8169 sets `mb->mark` (last *successful* mark); 8211 overwrites with `mb->nomatch_mark` for every non-MATCH_MATCH outcome, **including hard errors** — so an error return also clobbers `mark`. `Fmark`/`nomatch_mark` are set by `OP_MARK` (6778), `OP_COMMIT_ARG` (6810), `OP_PRUNE_ARG` (6823), `OP_THEN_ARG` (6874); `OP_SKIP_ARG` deliberately does **not** (comment 6836).\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (8222–8233): `subject = original_subject; subject_length = length; start_offset = start_offset; ovector[0] = match_partial - subject; ovector[1] = end_subject - subject; startchar = match_partial - subject; leftchar = start_partial - subject; rightchar = end_subject - subject; rc = PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL;` — **only pair 0 is written; all capture slots retain previous contents.** `ovector[1]` uses the possibly-shrunk `end_subject` (invalid-UTF fragment end). Reached when `match_partial != NULL`, i.e. `mb->hitend` fired at least once, even for PARTIAL_SOFT where `rc` came back as `MATCH_NOMATCH`.\n- Nomatch (8237–8243): `subject`, `subject_length`, `start_offset`, `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH`. `ovector` untouched.\n- Hard error (8215): only `match_data->rc = rc`; `subject` stays NULL (7132) and `subject_length`/`start_offset`/`ovector` are stale. **Test row: error return leaves match_data->subject == NULL.**\n\n### 4.1 heapframes allocation / growth / heap_limit\n- `frame_size = (offsetof(heapframe, ovector) + re->top_bracket * 2 * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE) + HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT - 1) & ~(HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT - 1)` (7495–7497).\n- Initial size (7516–7523):\n```c\nheapframes_size = frame_size * 10;\nif (heapframes_size < START_FRAMES_SIZE) heapframes_size = START_FRAMES_SIZE;   /* 20480 */\nif (heapframes_size / 1024 > mb->heap_limit) {\n  PCRE2_SIZE max_size = 1024 * mb->heap_limit;\n  if (max_size < frame_size) return match_data->rc = PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT;\n  heapframes_size = max_size; }\n```\n  ⇒ `heap_limit` of 0 with any pattern ⇒ **HEAPLIMIT before matching starts** (`max_size == 0 < frame_size`). `heap_limit` of e.g. 19 (KiB) with a small pattern ⇒ vector clamped to 19456 rather than 20480.\n- Reuse (7528–7540): `if (match_data->heapframes_size < heapframes_size) { free; malloc; on failure heapframes_size = 0 and PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY }`. **Test row: reuse a match_data across a small then large pattern (grow) and large then small (no realloc).**\n- Growth inside `match()` (758–803, `MATCH_RECURSE`):\n```c\nN = F + frame_size;\nif ((char*)N + frame_size >= frames_top) {\n  usedsize = (char*)N - (char*)heapframes;\n  if (heapframes_size >= PCRE2_SIZE_MAX/2) { if (heapframes_size == PCRE2_SIZE_MAX-1) return PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY;\n                                            newsize = PCRE2_SIZE_MAX - 1; }\n  else newsize = heapframes_size * 2;\n  if (newsize / 1024 >= mb->heap_limit) {\n    old_size = heapframes_size / 1024;\n    if (mb->heap_limit <= old_size) return PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT;\n    max_delta = 1024 * (mb->heap_limit - old_size);\n    if ((over_bytes = heapframes_size % 1024)) max_delta -= (1024 - over_bytes);\n    newsize = heapframes_size + max_delta; }\n  if (newsize - usedsize < frame_size) return PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT;\n  new = malloc(newsize); if (new == NULL) return PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY;\n  memcpy(new, heapframes, usedsize); ... frames_top = new + newsize; }\n```\n  Distinct rows: doubling succeeds; doubling clipped by heap_limit but still fits ≥1 frame; clipped and does **not** fit ⇒ HEAPLIMIT; `heap_limit <= old_size` ⇒ HEAPLIMIT; malloc fails ⇒ NOMEMORY. Note `F` and `N` are recomputed relative to `new`, and the growth reserves headroom of **two** frames (`(char*)N + frame_size >= frames_top`).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Limits\n\n| Limit | Effective value | Checked at | Error |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| match | `mb->match_limit = min(mcontext->match_limit, re->limit_match)` (7505–7506) | 873: `if (mb->match_call_count++ >= mb->match_limit) return PCRE2_ERROR_MATCHLIMIT;` — at the top of the main loop, i.e. **once per new frame** (`NEW_FRAME` falls through to it). Reset to 0 per bumpalong position (7969). | `PCRE2_ERROR_MATCHLIMIT` |\n| depth | `mb->match_limit_depth = min(mcontext->depth_limit, re->limit_depth)` (7508–7509) | 874: `if (Frdepth >= mb->match_limit_depth) return PCRE2_ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT;` — `Frdepth` is the frame index, incremented at 844. | `PCRE2_ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT` |\n| heap | `mb->heap_limit = min(mcontext->heap_limit, re->limit_heap)` (7502–7503), in **KiB** | 7518–7521 (initial allocation) and 774–791 (growth) | `PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` |\n\nPattern-embedded limits: `(*LIMIT_MATCH=n)`, `(*LIMIT_DEPTH=n)`/`(*LIMIT_RECURSION=n)`, `(*LIMIT_HEAP=n)` (`pcre2_compile.c:752-755`) default to `UINT32_MAX` when absent (`:10308-10310`) and land in `re->limit_match/limit_depth/limit_heap` (`:10908-10910`). **`min()` semantics ⇒ the pattern can only lower, never raise, the context limit — and vice versa.** Test matrix per limit: {pattern only, context only, both with pattern smaller, both with context smaller, neither (defaults 10000000/10000000/20000000)}. Note the outer function reads `mcontext->…` *after* the `mcontext == NULL` substitution (7390–7394), so the defaults come from `PRIV(default_match_context)`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Interpreter paths worth separate test rows\n\n### 6.1 Backreferences\n- `match_ref()` (357–495). Unset-group branch (373–381): `if (offset >= Foffset_top || Fovector[offset] == PCRE2_UNSET)` ⇒ `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF` set ⇒ `*lengthptr = 0; return 0` (match empty) else `return -1`.\n- Four caseless sub-paths: (a) UTF or UCP (397–448) with per-character `GETCHARINC` on **both** subject and reference, walking the *reference* length not the subject length; (b) Turkish casing `turkish_casing && UCD_ANY_I(d)` (427–432) requiring `REFI_FLAG_TURKISH_CASING` and **not** `REFI_FLAG_CASELESS_RESTRICT`; (c) `caseless_restrict && *pp < 128 ⇒ return -1` (439) for `ucd_caseless_sets`; (d) plain 8-bit `mb->lcc` table loop (454–465).\n- Caseful splits on `mb->partial`: unit-by-unit loop (476–481) vs. bulk `memcmp` (487–490). **A partial-vs-complete behavioural axis in pure-ASCII patterns.**\n- Return convention: `0` match, `<0` nomatch, `>0` **partial** (414, 457, 478); callers do `if (rrc > 0) Feptr = mb->end_subject; CHECK_PARTIAL(); RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH);` (5311–5313, 5345–5347, 5369–5371) — except the maximizing loop at 5397–5402 which deliberately does **not** advance `Feptr`.\n- Opcodes: `OP_REF`/`OP_REFI` (5267–5272, `Lcaseopts = Fecode[1+IMM2_SIZE]` when REFI) and `OP_DNREF`/`OP_DNREFI` (5249–5265, scans the name table for the **first set** group; if none is set, `Loffset` retains the last candidate). Repeat forms via `REF_REPEAT` (5278): CRSTAR..CRPOSQUERY, CRRANGE/CRMINRANGE/CRPOSRANGE (`Lmax == 0 ⇒ UINT32_MAX`), or none.\n- Zero-length set group ⇒ `continue` (5329) — infinite-loop guard.\n- Maximizing path has a `samelengths` fast path (5419–5427, backs up by `Llength`) and a **re-scan** slow path (5432–5449) taken only when caseless UTF makes iteration lengths differ (e.g. U+023A vs U+2C65). RM20/RM21/RM22.\n\n### 6.2 Recursion `OP_RECURSE` (5707–5776)\n- `number = (bracode == mb->start_code)? 0 : GET2(bracode, 1+LINK_SIZE)` — whole-pattern recursion is group 0.\n- Loop check (5718–5734):\n```c\nif (Feptr == P->eptr && mb->last_used_ptr == P->recurse_last_used &&\n     (mb->moptions & PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK) == 0)\n  return PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP;\n```\n  Requires an **already-active** recursion of the *same number*, same subject position, **and** unchanged `last_used_ptr`. Rows: loop detected; loop suppressed by DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK (then bounded by match/heap limit instead); same number but position advanced (no error); different number.\n- Verb containment (5761–5768): `rrc in [MATCH_COMMIT..MATCH_THEN] && mb->verb_current_recurse == (Lframe_type ^ GF_RECURSE)` ⇒ THEN may be converted to NOMATCH, else the whole recursion returns NOMATCH.\n- Return handling: whole-pattern at `OP_KET`/`OP_BRA` (6368–6398, detected by `Fcurrent_recurse == 0 && Fecode[1+LINK_SIZE] == OP_END`), group recursion at 6496–6512 (`Fcurrent_recurse == number`). Both restore captures via straight `memcpy` **unless** `*Fecode == OP_CREF`, in which case `recurse_update_offsets()` (512–564) selectively preser