MATCH_NOMATCH); Feptr++; if (utf) FORWARDCHARTEST(...)`. RM37.\n- Variable-lookbehind **end-point verification** appears in 4 places, each `branch_start[1 + LINK_SIZE] == OP_VREVERSE && Feptr != P->eptr ⇒ RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH)`: conditional assertion (6343–6345), `OP_ASSERTBACK_NA` (6409), `OP_ASSERTBACK` (6423), `OP_ASSERTBACK_NOT` (6452). `branch_start` is recomputed by walking the ALT chain at 6312–6314.\n- `re->max_lookbehind > 0` also forces `mb->allowemptypartial = TRUE` (7424) and governs the UTF-check rewind (7317).\n\n### 6.5 `\\X` — `OP_EXTUNI`\n- Single (2889–2903): `GETCHARINCTEST`, `PRIV(extuni)(fc, Feptr, mb->start_subject, mb->end_subject, utf, NULL)`, then `CHECK_PARTIAL()`.\n- Min-repeat (3237–3254) and max-repeat (4651–4714). The max-repeat **backtracking** is the interesting path: it re-derives grapheme breaks with `UCD_GRAPHBREAK` and `PRIV(ucp_gbtable)[lgb] & (1u << rgb)` (4697–4712), and uses `Feptr <= Lstart_eptr` (not `==`) because `\\C` can leave `Lstart_eptr` mid-character. RM219.\n\n### 6.6 `OP_SCRIPT_RUN`\nStart shares `GROUPLOOP` with `OP_ONCE` (5672); the check happens at the ket: `if (!PRIV(script_run)(P->eptr, Feptr, utf)) RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH);` (6481). Only reachable with Unicode support.\n\n### 6.7 XCLASS / ECLASS (8-bit: only present because SUPPORT_UNICODE ⇒ SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS)\n- `OP_XCLASS` (2294–2415): `PRIV(xclass)(fc, Lxclass_data, (const uint8_t*)mb->start_code, utf)`, min loop / REPTYPE_MIN (RM100) / REPTYPE_MAX with `Feptr-- <= Lstart_eptr` + `BACKCHAR` (RM101).\n- `OP_ECLASS` (2436–2559): `PRIV(eclass)(fc, Leclass_data, Leclass_data + Leclass_len, (const uint8_t*)mb->start_code, utf)`; RM102/RM103. `Leclass_len = Fecode - Leclass_data` after the `GET(Fecode,1)` skip.\n- `OP_CLASS` vs `OP_NCLASS` (2051): the **only** difference is `fc > 255` handling — `if (Fop == OP_CLASS) RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH)` / `break` (2105–2108, 2159–2162, 2213–2216); in 8-bit non-UTF the `>255` test is `#if`-ed out (2125, 2182, 2248) so the two are identical there. **Row: `[^x]` on a >255 codepoint under UTF vs non-UTF.**\n\n### 6.8 Callouts\n- `do_callout()` (268–330). `if (mb->callout == NULL) return 0;` (279) — `*lengthptr` is still set first, so patterns with callouts work with no callout function.\n- `*lengthptr = (*Fecode == OP_CALLOUT)? PRIV(OP_lengths)[OP_CALLOUT] : GET(Fecode, 1 + 2*LINK_SIZE);`\n- `callout_ovector = (PCRE2_SIZE *)(Fovector) - 2;` (291) with `capture_top = Foffset_top/2 + 1` (298) and slots [0],[1] temporarily forced to `PCRE2_UNSET` and restored (322–327). **Row: assert `offset_vector[0]/[1] == PCRE2_UNSET` inside a callout, and that they're restored after.**\n- Numerical vs string: `callout_number = Fecode[1 + 2*LINK_SIZE]` vs `callout_string_offset = GET(Fecode, 1 + 3*LINK_SIZE)`, `callout_string = Fecode + (1 + 4*LINK_SIZE) + 1`, `callout_string_length = *lengthptr - (1 + 4*LINK_SIZE) - 2` (306–320). With LINK_SIZE=2 these are byte offsets 5 / 7 / 10.\n- Return: `> 0 ⇒ RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH)`, `< 0 ⇒ RRETURN(rrc)` (propagates e.g. `PCRE2_ERROR_CALLOUT`), `0 ⇒ Fecode += length` (5991–5995).\n- `cb.version = 2` (7407); `cb.subject_length = end_subject - subject` — the **fragment** length under invalid UTF (7409). `cb.callout_flags`: `PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH` OR-ed per bumpalong (7960), `PCRE2_CALLOUT_BACKTRACK` OR-ed at every `RETURN_SWITCH` (6913), cleared after each callout (328).\n- Conditional-group callout: a callout between `OP_COND` and an assertion condition is handled specially, adjusting `Llength -= length` (6026–6037) — this is the AUTO_CALLOUT path.\n- `cb.mark = mb->nomatch_mark` (301), `cb.capture_last = Fcapture_last`, `cb.pattern_position = GET(Fecode,1)`, `cb.next_item_length = GET(Fecode, 1+LINK_SIZE)`.\n\n### 6.9 Verbs\n| Verb | Opcode/line | Behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| `(*MARK:n)` | `OP_MARK` 6777–6794 | `Fmark = mb->nomatch_mark = Fecode + 2`; on `MATCH_SKIP_ARG` compares `PRIV(strcmp)(Fecode+2, mb->verb_skip_ptr)` and converts to `MATCH_SKIP` with `mb->verb_skip_ptr = Feptr`. RM12 |\n| `(*FAIL)`/`(*F)` | `OP_FAIL` 6796 | `RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH)` |\n| `(*COMMIT)` | 6803–6807 / `_ARG` 6809–6814 | sets `mb->verb_current_recurse`, returns `MATCH_COMMIT` → outer loop `rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; goto ENDLOOP` (8032) i.e. **no bumpalong**. RM13/RM36 |\n| `(*PRUNE)` | 6816–6827 | `MATCH_PRUNE` → outer treats exactly like NOMATCH (advance 1 char). RM14/RM15 |\n| `(*SKIP)` | 6829–6834 | `mb->verb_skip_ptr = Feptr`; outer: `if (mb->verb_skip_ptr > start_match) new_start_match = mb->verb_skip_ptr;` else degrade to NOMATCH (8007–8013). RM16 |\n| `(*SKIP:n)` | 6844–6861 | `mb->skip_arg_count++`; `if (skip_arg_count <= mb->ignore_skip_arg) { skip the verb }`; else `MATCH_SKIP_ARG` → outer retries the **same** position with `ignore_skip_arg = skip_arg_count` (7999–8002). Does **not** set `nomatch_mark`. RM17 |\n| `(*THEN)` | 6866–6879 | `mb->verb_ecode_ptr = Fecode`; converted to NOMATCH by whichever enclosing group sees `mb->verb_ecode_ptr < next_ecode && (*Fecode == OP_ALT \\|\\| *next_ecode == OP_ALT)` — occurrences at 5581–5587 (BRAPOS), 5681–5687 (GROUPLOOP), 5764–5766 (RECURSE); swallowed unconditionally by assertions (5806, 5833, 6127). At top level acts like PRUNE (8020). RM18/RM19 |\n| `(*ACCEPT)` | `OP_ACCEPT` 940 / `OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT` 931 | In an assertion: records `assert_accept_frame`, `MATCH_ACCEPT`; consumers copy `Fovector`/`offset_top`/`mark` out of it (5799–5803, 5942–5946, 6110–6113). |\n\n### 6.10 Anchors / boundaries\n- `\\A` = `OP_SOD` (6576): `Feptr != mb->start_subject`.\n- `\\G` = `OP_SOM` (6680): `Feptr != mb->start_subject + mb->start_offset`.\n- `\\K` = `OP_SET_SOM` (6689): `Fstart_match = Feptr`; validated at `OP_END` (1022–1031) — `Fstart_match < mb->start_subject + mb->start_offset || Fstart_match > Feptr` ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` unless `mb->allowlookaroundbsk`.\n- `\\Z` = `OP_EODN` (6603) and the `$`-fallthrough label `ASSERT_NL_OR_EOS`: `Feptr < mb->true_end_subject && (!IS_NEWLINE(Feptr) || Feptr != mb->true_end_subject - mb->nllen)`, with the CRLF-split partial special case (6608–6616).\n- `\\z` = `OP_EOD` (6591): `Feptr < mb->true_end_subject`; then always `if (mb->partial != 0) { hitend = TRUE; if (partial > 1) return PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL; }`.\n- `^`/`$` non-multiline: `OP_CIRC` 6570, `OP_DOLL` 6584. Multiline: `OP_CIRCM` 6637, `OP_DOLLM` 6651.\n- `\\b`/`\\B`/UCP variants (6702–6770): four opcodes; the \"previous char\" floor is `mb->check_subject` (6706, **not** `start_subject`); UCP variants use `UCD_CHARTYPE`+`ucp_gentype` (`category == ucp_L || ucp_N || chartype == ucp_Mn || ucp_Pc`), non-UCP use `CHMAX_255(fc) && (mb->ctypes[fc] & ctype_word)`; both update `start_used_ptr`/`last_used_ptr`. Final test: `(*Fecode++ == OP_WORD_BOUNDARY || Fop == OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY)? cur == prev : cur != prev`.\n\n### 6.11 `.` — `OP_ANY` vs `OP_ALLANY` (DOTALL) and `\\C`\n- `OP_ANY` (1061–1072): `IS_NEWLINE(Feptr)` ⇒ nomatch, plus the CRLF partial special case `mb->partial != 0 && Feptr == mb->end_subject - 1 && nltype == NLTYPE_FIXED && nllen == 2 && *Feptr == nl[0]`. Note the **single** case uses `Feptr == mb->end_subject - 1` whereas every repeat case uses `Feptr + 1 >= mb->end_subject` (3273, 4734, 4986) — same meaning, different expression.\n- `OP_ALLANY` (1076–1087) falls through from `OP_ANY`; `Feptr++` then `if (utf) ACROSSCHAR(...)`.\n- `OP_ANYBYTE` = `\\C` (1095–1103): raw `Feptr++`, **no** ACROSSCHAR — can land mid-character. Only generated in UTF mode (in non-UTF `\\C` becomes `OP_ALLANY`; see the commented-out case at 3550–3556). Consequences: every maximizing backtrack loop uses `Feptr-- <= Lstart_eptr` instead of `==` (2232, 2406, 2550, 4640, 4959) precisely to survive `\\C`; the non-UTF loop at 5215 uses `==`. Repeat forms: 3299–3302 (UTF min: `if (Feptr > mb->end_subject - Lmin) RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH); Feptr += Lmin;`), 4770–4778 (UTF max), 4998–5007 (non-UTF, merged with ALLANY).\n- `\\R` = `OP_ANYNL` (2646–2679 single; 3304–3335 UTF min; 4780–4808 UTF