shing branch start states |\n| `PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST` | 891 | At the first `OP_KET==end_code` acceptance: `return match_count;` **immediately from `internal_dfa_match`**. Consequence: the ENDANCHORED post-check at 3305-3308 is **bypassed**, and only one (the shortest) match end is ever recorded |\n| `PCRE2_ANCHORED` | 3467 | `anchored = (options & (PCRE2_ANCHORED\\|PCRE2_DFA_RESTART)) != 0 \\|\\| (re->overall_options & PCRE2_ANCHORED) != 0`. Effects: no bumpalong (4042 `if (rc != PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH \\|\\| anchored)`), `firstline = FALSE` (3474), first-cu check becomes a single-position test (3741-3760), and req_cu search window shrinks to `REQ_CU_MAX` instead of `REQ_CU_MAX*1000` (3962-3963) |\n| `PCRE2_ENDANCHORED` | 3413, 3305-3308 | Only post-hoc: `if (match_count >= 0 && ((mb->moptions\\|mb->poptions) & PCRE2_ENDANCHORED) != 0 && ptr < end_subject) match_count = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH;`. **NOTE: the test is on the DFA scan position `ptr`, not on the individual recorded match ends.** So with `oveccount >= 2` shorter, non-end-anchored ends can still be returned in `ovector[2..]` (e.g. `a|ab` + ENDANCHORED on `\"ab\"` returns 2 pairs). Does **not** stop bumpalong |\n| `PCRE2_NOTBOL` | 947, 953 | `OP_CIRC`: `ptr == start_subject && (mb->moptions & PCRE2_NOTBOL) == 0`. `OP_CIRCM`: first disjunct of 953 disabled |\n| `PCRE2_NOTEOL` | 1023, 1050, 1071 | `OP_DOLL`: whole body skipped → `$` never matches. `OP_DOLLM`: falls to `else if (IS_NEWLINE(ptr)) ADD_ACTIVE(...)` — multiline `$` **still matches at internal newlines**, just not at end of subject |\n| `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY` | 875-878 | Acceptance requires `ptr > current_subject \\|\\| ((moptions & PCRE2_NOTEMPTY)==0 && (...))` |\n| `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` | 875-878 | `... ((moptions & PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART) == 0 \\|\\| current_subject > start_subject + mb->start_offset)` |\n| `PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT` | 1032-1033, 1057-1058, 3855, 3912, 3924, 3280-3281 | Enables the `new_count<=0` partial check only when `match_count < 0` (no complete match yet). Disables the `minlength` and `req_cu` optimizations (3924). Lets the bumpalong run at `end_subject` when first-cu/bitmap search fails (3855, 3912) |\n| `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD` | 963, 1015, 1025, 1038, 1052, 1063, 991, 1290, 1321, 1351, 1379, 1408, 2129, 2308, 2341, 3278 | (a) `OP_EOD`/`OP_EODN` reached at/after end → **immediate `return PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`** (964, 1016) even if a full match was already recorded; (b) partial reported regardless of `match_count`; (c) enables the \"partial CRLF\" logic for `.`, `$`, `\\X`, `\\R` |\n| `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` | 3590 | Skips both `NOT_FIRSTCU` offset check and `valid_utf` scan. With invalid UTF and this set, behavior is undefined (no `MATCH_INVALID_UTF` fallback exists in DFA) |\n| `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` | 3679-3684, 4061-4074 | On entry: if `(match_data->flags & PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT) != 0` frees old copy (3679) — **but only after the UTF check / BADOFFSETLIMIT / INTERNAL early exits, so those leak the previous copy**. On success: applied only when `rc >= 0` (**not** for `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`); `length == 0` → `subject = NULL`; malloc failure → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (-48) |\n| `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` (compile) | 3708 | Clears `PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE` (0x4) at compile (`pcre2_compile.c:10414`); gate is `(re->optimization_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE) != 0 && (options & PCRE2_DFA_RESTART) == 0`. Also settable as `(*NO_START_OPT)` (`pcre2_compile.c:749`) |\n| `PCRE2_FIRSTLINE` (compile) | 3474, 3719-3735, 3920, 4085 | `firstline = !anchored && (re->overall_options & PCRE2_FIRSTLINE) != 0`. Scan fudges `end_subject = t` where `t` is the first `IS_NEWLINE` position; restored at 3920. Bumpalong terminator at 4085: `if (firstline && IS_NEWLINE(start_match)) break;` |\n| `PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT` (compile) | 3505-3507, 4019 | `bumpalong_limit = subject + mcontext->offset_limit`; `if (start_match > bumpalong_limit) break;` (4019). Default `bumpalong_limit = end_subject` (3475) |\n| `PCRE2_UTF` (compile) | 3463 | `utf = (re->overall_options & PCRE2_UTF) != 0`; drives UTF validation (3590), `GETCHARLENTEST` (735), `ACROSSCHAR` in bumpalong (4090) and firstline/startline scans, `BACKCHAR` in `\\b` (1107), char-wise lookbehind stepping (612-621), and charcount adjustment for `OP_RECURSE`/`OP_ONCE`/`OP_BRAPOS` (3006-3013, 3126-3128, 3223-3230) |\n| `PCRE2_UCP` (compile) | 559, 3642, 3666 | `utf_or_ucp = utf \\|\\| (mb->poptions & PCRE2_UCP) != 0` (559) — controls `OP_CHARI`/`OP_NOTI`/`*I` caseless folding via `UCD_OTHERCASE` vs `fcc` table. 8-bit-specific first/req cu caseless: `if (first_cu > 127 && !utf && (re->overall_options & PCRE2_UCP) != 0) first_cu2 = UCD_OTHERCASE(first_cu)` (3642, 3666) |\n| `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` (compile) | 1028, 1055 | `OP_DOLL`: removes the \"`$` before final newline\" alternative (`(mb->poptions & PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY) == 0 && IS_NEWLINE(ptr) && ptr == end_subject - mb->nllen`). `OP_DOLLM` likewise at 1055 (**note: PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY is documented as ignored with MULTILINE, but here it DOES gate `OP_DOLLM`'s newline branch**) |\n| `PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX` (compile) | 954 | `OP_CIRCM`: `((ptr != end_subject \\|\\| (mb->poptions & PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX) != 0) && WAS_NEWLINE(ptr))` — allows `^` to match after a trailing newline at end of subject |\n| `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` (compile) | 3419 | → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UINVALID_UTF` (-66), unconditional |\n| `PCRE2_NO_JIT` | 3399 | → -34 (no JIT path exists in this file at all; `match_data->matchedby = PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` at 3691) |\n\n### 1.4 Context limits (3493-3524)\n```c\nmcontext == NULL: match_limit/depth/heap from PRIV(default_match_context)\nmcontext != NULL: from mcontext->{match_limit, depth_limit, heap_limit}\n3517: if (mb->match_limit       > re->limit_match) mb->match_limit       = re->limit_match;\n3520: if (mb->match_limit_depth > re->limit_depth) mb->match_limit_depth = re->limit_depth;\n3523: if (mb->heap_limit        > re->limit_heap)  mb->heap_limit        = re->limit_heap;\n```\n`(*LIMIT_MATCH=n)` / `(*LIMIT_DEPTH=n)` / `(*LIMIT_HEAP=n)` in the pattern can only lower.\n\n---\n\n## 2. `workspace` / `wscount`\n\n### 2.1 Minimum and capacity arithmetic\n```c\n3407: if (wscount < 20) { rc = PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE; goto EXIT; }   /* wscount is in ints */\n570:  wscount -= 2;\n571:  wscount = (wscount - (wscount % (INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK * 2))) / (2 * INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK);\n```\nSo the usable capacity is **`states = floor((wscount - 2) / 6)`** simultaneous states **per vector**, and there are two vectors:\n```c\n580: active_states  = (stateblock *)(workspace + 2);\n581: next_new_state = new_states = active_states + states;\n```\n- `workspace[0]` = which half is current (0/1), `workspace[1]` = `active_count`.\n- `wscount = 20` → 3 states/vector (minimum functional). `wscount = 1000` → 166. `wscount = 20*(1+top_bracket)` → `floor((20+20*top_bracket-2)/6) ≈ 3.3*(1+top_bracket)` states. The `20 * (1 + re->top_bracket)` heuristic is \"20 ints ≈ 3 states per capture group\"; it is a *heuristic only* — nothing in this file checks it.\n\n### 2.2 `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE` (-43) sites\n| Line | Condition |\n|---|---|\n| 3407 | `wscount < 20` (outer, before anything else) |\n| 496 | `ADD_ACTIVE(x,y)`: `active_count++ >= states` |\n| 506 | `ADD_ACTIVE_DATA(x,y,z)`: same |\n| 515 | `ADD_NEW(x,y)`: `new_count++ >= states` |\n| 525 | `ADD_NEW_DATA(x,y,z)`: same |\n\nNote the counter is **post-incremented before the test's else**, so `active_count`/`new_count` are left one past capacity when the error fires. Recursive calls pass `wscount = RWS_RSIZE = 1000` (2816, 2915, 2986, 3075, 3162) → **166 states** regardless of the caller's `wscount`; so an assertion/atomic group/recursion body with >166 simultaneous states gives -43 no matter how large the user's workspace is.\n\n### 2.3 `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_BADRESTART` (-38)\n```c\n3454: if ((options & PCRE2_DFA_RESTART) != 0)\n3456:   if ((workspace[0] & (-2)) != 0 ||          /* workspace[0] must be exactly 0 or 1 */\n3456:       workspace[1] < 1 ||                    /* must be >= 1 saved state */\n3457:       workspace[1] > (int)((wscount - 2)/INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK))   /* (wscount-2)/3 */\n3458:     { rc = PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_BADRESTART; goto EXIT; }\n```\nThree independent failure triggers. Note the upper bound uses `/3`, but real capacity is `/6` — values in `(floor((wscount-2)/6), floor((wscount-2)/3)]` pass the check and then overrun on the `memcpy` at 673. Also `wscount` is `PCRE2_SIZE` (unsigned), so `wscount-2` is safe only because `wscount >= 20` was already checked.\n\n### 2.4 Restart read-back\n```c\n668: if (rlevel == 1 && (mb->moptions & PCRE2_DFA_RESTART) != 0)\n670:   do { end_code += GET(end_code, 1); } while (*end_code == OP_ALT);\n671:   new_count = workspace[1];\n672:   if (!workspace[0])\n673:     memcpy(new_states, active_states, (size_t)new_count * sizeof(stateblock));\n694: workspace[0] = 0;\n```\nWritten each character iteration:\n```c\n719: workspace[0] ^= 1;\n720: workspace[1] = active_count;\n```\nRequirements for a valid restart (test contract):\n1. Same `workspace` pointer and **same `wscount`** as the partial-matching call (the `new_states` base offset is `wscount`-derived; a different `wscount` silently reads the wrong half).\n2. Same compiled `code`.\n3. `start_offset` must be where the partial match ended (`ovector[1]` from the partial); the DFA is forced anchored there.\n4. `rlevel == 1` gate means only the top-level invocation restarts; nested calls (assertions/`OP_ONCE`/`OP_RECURSE`/possessive) always start fresh — so restarting a partial match that ended *inside* an assertion loses that state.\n5. `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` also forces `anchored` and kills start optimizations and `firstline`.\n\n### 2.5 Recursion workspace (RWS) — separate from `wscount`\n```c\n3384: int base_recursion_workspace[RWS_BASE_SIZE];   /* 7680 ints = 30 KiB, on the C stack */\n3386: rws->next = NULL; rws->size = RWS_BASE_SIZE; rws->free = RWS_BASE_SIZE - RWS_ANCHOR_SIZE;  /* 7676 */\n4117: while (rws->next != NULL) { ... mb->memctl.free(next, ...) }   /* freed at EXIT */\n```\n`more_workspace()` (420-457):\n```c\n426: if (rws->next != NULL) new = rws->next;                 /* reuse chained block */\n437: else newsize = (rws->size >= UINT32_MAX/(sizeof(int)*2))? UINT32_MAX/sizeof(int) : rws->size*2;\n438:      newsizeK = newsize/(1024/sizeof(int));               /* /256 */\n440:      if (newsizeK + mb->heap_used > mb->heap_limit) newsizeK = mb->heap_limit - mb->heap_used;\n442:      newsize = newsizeK*256;\n444:      if (newsize < RWS_RSIZE + ovecsize + RWS_ANCHOR_SIZE) return PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT;  /* -63 */\n447:      if (new == NULL) return PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY;        /* -48 */\n448:      mb->heap_used += newsizeK;\n454: new->free = new->size - RWS_ANCHOR_SIZE;  *rwsptr = new;\n```\nPer-nesting-level reservation:\n- assertions / `OP_COND` assertion / `OP_ONCE` / `OP_BRAPOS*`: `RWS_RSIZE + RWS_OVEC_OSIZE = 1004` ints → ~7 levels fit in the 7676-int base block\n- `OP_RECURSE`: `RWS_RSIZE + RWS_OVEC_RSIZE = 3000` ints → 2 levels in the base block\n\nHeap-limit thresholds (from 444): first growth is 7680*2 = 15360 ints = **60 KiB**; the minimum acceptable clamp is `newsizeK >= ceil(1008/256) = 4` KiB for `ovecsize=4`, and `ceil(3004/256) = 12` KiB for `ovecsize=2000`. So `heap_limit` below ~4 KiB (assertions) / ~12 KiB (recursion) yields **`PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` (-63)** as soon as the base block is exhausted.\n\n---\n\n## 3. ovector semantics unique to the DFA\n\n`offsetcount = (uint32_t)match_data->oveccount * 2` (4033), then `offsetcount &= (uint32_t)(-2)` (568).\n\nMatch recording, `OP_KET`/`OP_KETRMIN`/`OP_KETRMAX`/`OP_KETRPOS` when `code == end_code` (873-893):\n```c\n880: if (match_count < 0) match_count = (offsetcount >= 2)? 1 : 0;\n881: else if (match_count > 0 && ++match_count * 2 > (int)offsetcount) match_count = 0;\n883: count = ((match_count == 0)? (int)offsetcount : match_count * 2) - 2;\n884: if (count > 0) (void)memmove(offsets + 2, offsets, (size_t)count * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));\n886: if (offsetcount >= 2)\n888:   offsets[0] = (PCRE2_SIZE)(current_subject - start_subject);\n889:   offsets[1] = (PCRE2_SIZE)(ptr - start_subject);\n891: if ((mb->moptions & PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST) != 0) return match_count;\n```\nSemantics:\n- **One start, many ends.** `offsets[0]` is always the same value (`current_subject`) for every pair; `offsets[2k+1]` are the distinct match ends. Pairs are ordered **longest first** (each new, longer end is memmove-shifted to the front).\n- **Return value never exceeds `oveccount`.** Once `match_count*2 > offsetcount` it is latched to `0` (the `match_count > 0` guard at 881 prevents it recovering). `rc == 0` means \"ovector too small; the `oveccount` longest matches are present\". This matches `pcre2_match`'s convention (`pcre2_match.c:8181`).\n- `oveccount == 0`: `offsetcount == 0`; the first acceptance sets `match_count = 0`; **nothing is written to `ovector`**; the function returns `0` (success). `count = -2` so no memmove.\n- `oveccount == 1`: 1 pair kept = the longest end; return `1` if exactly one end was found, `0` if two or more were found.\n- `oveccount == 2`: returns `2` if exactly two ends; `0` if three or more (2 longest kept).\n- `oveccount == n`, `m` distinct ends: return `m` if `m <= n`, else `0` with the `n` longest.\n- `PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST`: returns at the very first acceptance, so `rc` is `1` (or `0` when `oveccount==0`) and the ovector holds the **shortest** match.\n\n`PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (-2) contents (4046-4050):\n```c\n4046: if (rc == PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL && match_data->oveccount > 0)\n4048:   match_data->ovector[0] = (PCRE2_SIZE)(start_match - subject);\n4049:   match_data->ovector[1] = (PCRE2_SIZE)(end_subject - subject);\n```\ni.e. `[bumpalong start, end of subject]`. With `oveccount == 0` **nothing is written** but -2 is still returned.\n\nFields set on `rc >= 0 || rc == PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (4052-4059):\n```c\nmatch_data->subject_length = length;\nmatch_data->start_offset   = start_offset;\nmatch_data->leftchar       = mb->start_used_ptr - subject;   /* earliest consulted */\nmatch_data->rightchar      = mb->last_used_ptr  - subject;   /* latest consulted */\nmatch_data->startchar      = start_match - subject;\n```\n- `match_data->startchar` = the bumpalong start position. **Difference from `pcre2_match`:** for a partial match `pcre2_match` sets `startchar = match_partial - subject` (`pcre2_match.c:8229`), whereas the DFA sets it to `start_match` for both full and partial — for the DFA these coincide, since `start_match` *is* where the partial began.\n- `mb->start_used_ptr`/`last_used_ptr` initialized to `start_match` (4023-4024) each bumpalong iteration; pushed back by lookbehind (635-636), `\\b`/`\\B` (1105, 1127-1133), and advanced at 708 (`if (ptr > mb->last_used_ptr) mb->last_used_ptr = ptr;`).\n- `match_data->rc = rc` (4124); `match_data->matchedby = PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` (3691); `match_data->mark = NULL` always (3690; `cb.mark = NULL` at 3487 — **no (*MARK) support**); `cb.capture_top = 1`, `cb.capture_last = 0` (3485-3486 — **no capture support**).\n- NOMATCH exit (4110-4114) sets `subject`, `subject_length`, `start_offset` and `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH`, but does **not** set `leftchar`/`rightchar`/`startchar`.\n\n`PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC` (-41) — not in this file; raised because `matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` by:\n- `pcre2_substring.c:75` `pcre2_substring_copy_byname`\n- `pcre2_substring.c:163` `pcre2_substring_get_byname`\n- `pcre2_substring.c:270` `pcre2_substring_length_byname`\n- `pcre2_substitute.c:850` `pcre2_substitute` with `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` (`use_existing_match`)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Start-of-match optimizations (3698-4019)\n\nMaster gate (3708): `(re->optimization_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE) != 0 && (options & PCRE2_DFA_RESTART) == 0`.\n\n| Order | Lines | Condition / effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| firstline fudge | 3719-3735 | `if (firstline)`: scan `t` from `start_match` while `t < end_subject && !IS_NEWLINE(t)` (UTF: `t++; ACROSSCHAR(...)`); `end_subject = t` |\n| anchored first-cu / bitmap | 3741-3760 | `if (has_first_cu \\|\\| start_bits != NULL)`: `ok = start_match < end_subject`; then `c = *start_match; ok = has_first_cu && (c == first_cu \\|\\| c == first_cu2); if (!ok && start_bits != NULL) ok = (start_bits[c/8] & (1u<<(c&7))) != 0; if (!ok) break;` |\n| unanchored first-cu | 3766-3858 | 8-bit uses `memchr` twice (caseless) with `memchr_found_first_cu`/`memchr_found_first_cu2` caches (3795-3826); caseful single `memchr` (3840). Then `if ((mb->moptions & (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD\\|PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT)) == 0 && start_match >= mb->end_subject) break;` (3855) |\n| startline | 3863-3891 | only when `!has_first_cu`; `if (start_match > mb->start_subject + start_offset)` advance while `!WAS_NEWLINE(start_match)`; then CR/LF fudge: `start_match[-1]==CHAR_CR && (nltype==NLTYPE_ANY \\|\\| nltype==NLTYPE_ANYCRLF) && start_match<end_subject && *start_match==CHAR_NL → start_match++` |\n| start bitmap | 3898-3915 | only when `!has_first_cu && !startline`; `while (start_match < end_subject) { c=*start_match; if ((start_bits[c/8] & (1u<<(c&7))) != 0) break; start_match++; }`; then same partial-guarded `break` (3912) |\n| restore | 3920 | `end_subject = mb->end_subject;` |\n| minlength | 3924, 3933 | inside `if ((mb->moptions & (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD\\|PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT)) == 0)`: `if (end_subject - start_match < re->minlength) goto NOMATCH_EXIT;` |\n| req_cu | 3957-4011 | `p = start_match + (has_first_cu? 1:0); if (has_req_cu && p > req_cu_ptr)`; window `check_length = end_subject - start_match`; only if `check_length < REQ_CU_MAX \\|\\| (!anchored && check_length < REQ_CU_MAX*1000)` i.e. `< 5000` (anchored) / `< 5000000` (unanchored); 8-bit caseless does two sequential `memchr`s (3975-3979); `if (p >= end_subject) break;` else `req_cu_ptr = p;` |\n| bumpalong limit | 4019 | `if (start_match > bumpalong_limit) break;` |\n| bumpalong step | 4086-4106 | `start_match++`; UTF `ACROSSCHAR`; `if (start_match > end_subject) break;`; then CR/LF skip: `start_match[-1]==CHAR_CR && start_match<end_subject && *start_match==CHAR_NL && (re->flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF)==0 && (nltype==NLTYPE_ANY \\|\\| nltype==NLTYPE_ANYCRLF \\|\\| nllen==2)` |\n\nFlag setup (3633-3674): `has_first_cu` from `re->flags & PCRE2_FIRSTSET` (0x10); `first_cu2` folded when `PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS` (0x20) via `fcc` table, plus UCP 8-bit special at 3642. `start_bits = re->start_bitmap` only when `!(flags & PCRE2_FIRSTSET) && !startline && (flags & PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET)` (3652-3653). `has_req_cu` from `PCRE2_LASTSET` (0x80), `PCRE2_LASTCASELESS` (0x100). `startline = (re->flags & PCRE2_STARTLINE) != 0` (3473).\n\n### Differences from `pcre2_match` (`pcre2_match.c:7615-7950`)\n1. **`PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` disables the whole block** (3709). `pcre2_match` has no equivalent (7625 has only the `optimization_flags` test).\n2. **`anchored` includes `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART`** (3467), so restart also kills `firstline`.\n3. `pcre2_match` initialises `memchr_found_first_cu*` inside the function body just before the loop (7610-7611); DFA initialises them as declarations (3361-3362) — identical effect.\n4. DFA has **no `hitend`/`match_partial`/`start_partial` cross-bumpalong partial tracking** — partial is decided inside `internal_dfa_match` per start position and returned at once (4042); `pcre2_match` keeps scanning after a soft partial and reports it only at the end (`pcre2_match.c:8222-8233`).\n5. DFA has **no `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` re-scan / `end_subject` truncation loop** (`pcre2_match.c:7348-7359`, 8139-8155).\n6. DFA has **no JIT dispatch**, no `cb.callout_flags |= PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH`, no `PCRE2_CALLOUT_BACKTRACK`.\n7. DFA's minlength failure uses `goto NOMATCH_EXIT` (3933), i.e. abandons all further start positions, exactly like `pcre2_match`'s `rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break;` (7856-7860).\n8. `mb->partial` (0/1/2) in `pcre2_match` vs. raw `mb->moptions & (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD|PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT)` tests in the DFA.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Opcodes / features the DFA REJECTS\n\n### 5.1 `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM` (-42)\n**Explicit sites:**\n| Line | Condition | Pattern that triggers it |\n|---|---|---|\n| 825 | `if (coptable[codevalue] > 0 && codevalue >= OP_TYPESTAR)` and `d == OP_ANYBYTE` | `\\C*`, `\\C+`, `\\C?`, `\\C{n,m}` (quantified `\\C`) |\n| 2943 | `case OP_RECURSE:` … `if (code[1 + LINK_SIZE] == OP_CREF)` | recursion with an **argument list** (`pcre2_compile.c:8197-8210` emits `OP_CREF` after `OP_RECURSE`) |\n| 3259 | `default:` of the main opcode switch | everything in the table below |\n\n**Opcodes with NO `case` label → fall to 3259 (`default: return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM`):**\n| Opcode (enum #) | Pattern construct |\n|---|---|\n| `OP_END` (0) | unreachable (`end_code` is the final `OP_KET`) |\n| `OP_SET_SOM` (3) | **`\\K`** |\n| `OP_ANYBYTE` (14) | **`\\C`** (bare, in UTF **and** non-UTF — the DFA never supports `\\C`) |\n| `OP_REF`(114), `OP_REFI`(115), `OP_DNREF`(116), `OP_DNREFI`(117) | **back references** `\\1`, `(?i)\\1`, `\\k<name>` (duplicate names) — and hence any quantified backref, since the ref opcode is hit first |\n| `OP_REVERSE` (126) | only reachable via a broken lookbehind path; normally consumed by `revlen` at 644 |\n| `OP_VREVERSE` (127) | **variable-length lookbehind** (`(?<=a{2,4}b)`). `pcre2_compile.c:8683-8686` emits it when `lookbehindminlength != lookbehindlength && != LOOKBEHIND_MAX`; 644 computes `revlen = 0` for it, so the state lands directly on `OP_VREVERSE` |\n| `OP_ASSERT_NA` (132), `OP_ASSERTBACK_NA` (133) | **non-atomic lookarounds** `(*napla:…)`, `(*naplb:…)`, `(?*…)` |\n| `OP_ASSERT_SCS` (134) | **scan-substring** `(?(*scs:…)…)` |\n| `OP_SCRIPT_RUN` (136) | **script runs** `(*script_run:…)` / `(*sr:…)` / `(*atomic_script_run:…)` |\n| `OP_CREF`(147), `OP_DNCREF`(148), `OP_RREF`(149), `OP_DNRREF`(150) | not reachable as standalone states (only as `condcode`) |\n| `OP_FALSE`(151), `OP_TRUE`(152) | not reachable as standalone states |\n| `OP_MARK`(156), `OP_PRUNE`(157), `OP_PRUNE_ARG`(158), `OP_SKIP`(159), `OP_SKIP_ARG`(160), `OP_THEN`(161), `OP_THEN_ARG`(162), `OP_COMMIT`(163), `OP_COMMIT_ARG`(164) | **all backtracking verbs except `(*FAIL)`** |\n| `OP_ACCEPT` (166) | **`(*ACCEPT)`** at top level |\n| `OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT` (167) | **`(*ACCEPT)` inside an assertion** |\n| `OP_CLOSE` (168) | emitted immediately before `OP_ACCEPT` |\n| `OP_DEFINE` (170) | rewritten to `OP_FALSE` before compile finishes → unreachable |\n\n### 5.2 `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UCOND` (-40) — `OP_COND`/`OP_SCOND`, lines 2855-2881\n```c\n2855: if (condcode == OP_CREF || condcode == OP_DNCREF || condcode == OP_DNRREF)\n2857:   return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UCOND;\n2876: unsigned int value = GET2(code, LINK_SIZE + 2);\n2877: if (value != RREF_ANY) return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UCOND;\n```\n- `OP_CREF` → `(?(1)yes|no)`, `(?(<name>)…)` (unique name) → **-40**\n- `OP_DNCREF` → `(?(<dupname>)…)` → **-40**\n- `OP_DNRREF` → `(?(R&dupname)…)` → **-40**\n- `OP_RREF` with `value != RREF_ANY` → `(?(R1)…)`, `(?(R&name)…)` (specific group) → **-40**\n\n**Supported condition types:**\n- `OP_FALSE` / `OP_FAIL` (2862) → `(?(DEFINE)…)`, `(?(VERSION<…)…)` false → take the \"no\" branch: `ADD_ACTIVE(state_offset + codelink + LINK_SIZE + 1, 0)`\n- `OP_TRUE` (2867) → `ADD_ACTIVE(state_offset + LINK_SIZE + 2, 0)`\n- `OP_RREF` with `value == RREF_ANY` → `(?(R)…)`: `mb->recursive != NULL` → yes-branch at `state_offset + LINK_SIZE + 2 + IMM2_SIZE`, else no-branch\n- assertion conditions (2885-2927) via recursive `internal_dfa_match`\n- auto-callout between `OP_COND` and an assertion condition handled at 2839-2848 (`extracode = 1 + LINK_SIZE`)\n\n### 5.3 `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_RECURSE` (-39) — line 2995\n```c\n2995: if (rc == 0) return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_RECURSE;\n```\nOnly for `OP_RECURSE`. `rc == 0` means the nested call's ovector overflowed. Its size is `RWS_OVEC_RSIZE/OVEC_UNIT = 2000/2 = 1000` `PCRE2_SIZE` slots = **500 match-end pairs**. So a recursed group with **> 500 distinct match ends** at one position → -39. Not tunable by the caller.\n\n### 5.4 `PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP` (-52) — lines 2960-2967\n```c\n2960: for (dfa_recursion_info *ri = mb->recursive; ri != NULL; ri = ri->prevrec)\n2964:   if (recno == ri->group_num && ptr == ri->subject_position &&\n2965:       mb->last_used_ptr == ri->last_used_ptr)\n2966:     return PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP;\n```\nUnconditional (there is **no** `PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK` honoured — that option is rejected at 3399). `recno = (callpat == mb->start_code)? 0 : GET2(callpat, 1 + LINK_SIZE)` (2939-2940).\n\n### 5.5 Features that ARE supported\n| Feature | Line | Mechanism |\n|---|---|---|\n| Atomic groups `(?>…)` | 3136 `case OP_ONCE` | recursive `internal_dfa_match` with `offsetcount = 2`; `charcount = local_offsets[1]-local_offsets[0]`; `charcount == 0` → `ADD_ACTIVE(next_state_offset,0)` (3192); else fast-path `ptr += charcount; clen = 0;` when `i+1 >= active_count && new_count == 0` (3202); else `ADD_NEW_DATA(-next_state_offset, 0, charcount-1)`; `KETRMAX`/`KETRMIN` also add `repeat_state_offset` (3183-3185, 3213-3219, 3232-3233) |\n| Possessive groups `(…)++` | 3030-3034 `OP_BRAPOS/SBRAPOS/CBRAPOS/SCBRAPOS/BRAPOSZERO` | loop of recursive calls until `charcount == 0` or NOMATCH (3065-3092); `matched_count > 0 \\|\\| allow_zero` gates the continuation |\n| Possessive single-char / class quantifiers | 1302, 1333, 1363, 1420, 2467, 2509, 2550, 2623, 2704, 2720, 2736, 2755 | `active_count--; next_active_state--;` removes the already-pushed \"zero more\" state |\n| Lookaheads / lookbehinds (fixed & branch-fixed length) | 2784-2826 | recursive call; `if ((rc >= 0) == (codevalue == OP_ASSERT \\|\\| codevalue == OP_ASSERTBACK)) ADD_ACTIVE(endasscode + LINK_SIZE + 1 - start_code, 0)` |\n| Lookbehind setup | 592-654 | `max_back` = max `GET2(end_code, 2+LINK_SIZE)` over branches; UTF steps back char-by-char (612-621); `gone_back` clamped; per-branch `ADD_NEW_DATA(-bstate, 0, gone_back - back)` for branches with `back <= gone_back` |\n| Recursion `(?R)`, `(?1)`, `(?&name)` | 2932 | recursive call, `charcount`-delayed states (3001-3024) |\n| Callouts | 3244-3253 (+2839-2848 in conditions) | `do_callout_dfa` (360-398); `rrc < 0` → `return rrc` (abandon); `rrc == 0` → `ADD_ACTIVE(state_offset + callout_length, 0)`; `rrc > 0` → thread dies. `cb.version = 2`, `capture_top = 1`, `capture_last = 0`, `mark = NULL` |\n| `(*FAIL)` / `(?!)` | 2781-2782 `case OP_FAIL: break;` | thread simply dies (no error) |\n| `\\X` (`OP_EXTUNI`) | 2302-2312 + `OP_EXTUNI_EXTRA` variants at 1561, 1822/1828, 2111 | `PRIV(extuni)(c, ptr+clen, mb->start_subject, end_subject, utf, &ncount)`; `ADD_NEW_DATA(-(state_offset+1), 0, ncount)`; `if (nptr >= end_subject && PARTIAL_HARD) reset_could_continue = TRUE` (2308) |\n| `\\p`/`\\P` | 1164-1271 (+`OP_PROP_EXTRA` at 1440, 1692/1698, 1985) | all `PT_*` types: `PT_LAMP, PT_GC, PT_PC, PT_SC, PT_SCX, PT_ALNUM, PT_SPACE, PT_PXSPACE, PT_WORD, PT_CLIST, PT_UCNC, PT_BIDICL, PT_BOOL` |\n| `OP_XCLASS`, `OP_ECLASS` | 2643-2673 | `PRIV(xclass)(c, code+1+LINK_SIZE, (const uint8_t*)mb->start_code, utf)`; `PRIV(eclass)(c, code+1+LINK_SIZE, ecode, …, utf)` |\n| UCP word boundaries `\\b`/`\\B` | 1095-1155 | `OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY` / `OP_NOT_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY` use `UCD_CHARTYPE` + `PRIV(ucp_gentype)`: `category == ucp_L \\|\\| ucp_N \\|\\| chartype == ucp_Mn \\|\\| ucp_Pc` |\n\n---\n\n## 6. `internal_dfa_match` recursion, RWS growth, limits\n\n### 6.1 Recursion sites and their parameters\n| Site | Line | `offsets` size (slots) | `wscount` | RWS reservation (ints) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `OP_ASSERT`/`_NOT`/`OP_ASSERTBACK`/`_NOT` | 2808 | `RWS_OVEC_OSIZE/OVEC_UNIT = 2` | 1000 | 1004 |\n| `OP_COND`/`OP_SCOND` assertion condition | 2907 | 2 | 1000 | 1004 |\n| `OP_RECURSE` | 2978 | `RWS_OVEC_RSIZE/OVEC_UNIT = 1000` | 1000 | 3000 |\n| `OP_BRAPOS`/`SBRAPOS`/`CBRAPOS`/`SCBRAPOS`/`BRAPOSZERO` (loop) | 3067 | 2 | 1000 | 1004 |\n| `OP_ONCE` | 3154 | 2 | 1000 | 1004 |\n\nCommon preamble at each site (e.g. 2793-2804):\n```c\nRWS_anchor *rws = (RWS_anchor *)RWS;\nif (rws->free < RWS_RSIZE + <ovecsize>) { rc = more_workspace(&rws, <ovecsize>, mb); if (rc != 0) return rc; RWS = (int *)rws; }\nlocal_offsets   = (PCRE2_SIZE *)(RWS + rws->size - rws->free);\nlocal_workspace = ((int *)local_offsets) + <ovecsize>;\nrws->free -= RWS_RSIZE + <ovecsize>;\n   ... recursive call ...\nrws->free += RWS_RSIZE + <ovecsize>;\n```\nError propagation: `if (rc < 0 && rc != PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH) return rc;` (2822, 2921), `else if (rc != PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH) return rc;` (3025, 3236), `if (rc != PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH) return rc;` (3083). So `WSSIZE`/`MATCHLIMIT`/`DEPTHLIMIT`/`HEAPLIMIT`/`UITEM`/`UCOND` from a nested call abort the whole match.\n\n### 6.2 Limits inside `internal_dfa_match` (566-567)\n```c\n566: if (mb->match_call_count++ >= mb->match_limit)      return PCRE2_ERROR_MATCHLIMIT;  /* -47 */\n567: if (rlevel++ > mb->match_limit_depth)               return PCRE2_ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT;  /* -53 */\n```\n- `mb->match_call_count = 0` at 3535 — **reset once per `pcre2_dfa_match()` call, NOT per bumpalong iteration**. So `match_limit` in the DFA counts **total `internal_dfa_match` invocations** (1 per bumpalong position + 1 per nested assertion/atomic/recursion evaluation). It has nothing to do with backtracking. Trivially: `match_limit = 0` → the very first call returns -47.\n- `rlevel` starts at `0` (passed at 4036), post-incremented; the top call passes `1` down. Error when `rlevel > match_limit_depth`. So `match_limit_depth = 0` → top-level call passes (`0 > 0` false), first nested call fails (`1 > 0`). Max nesting depth ≈ `match_limit_depth + 1`.\n- `heap_limit` is used only by `more_workspace` (440-445) → `PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` (-63); `mb->heap_used` accumulates in KiB (448) and is never decremented (blocks are cached on `rws->next` and freed only at 4117-4122).\n\n### 6.3 Partial-match decision (3274-3295)\n```c\n3274: if (new_count <= 0)\n3276:   if (could_continue &&\n3278:       ( (mb->moptions & PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD) != 0\n3280:         || ((mb->moptions & PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT) != 0 && match_count < 0) ) &&\n3284:       ( partial_newline ||\n3286:         ( ptr >= end_subject &&\n3288:           ( ptr > mb->start_used_ptr || mb->allowemptypartial ) ) ))\n3293:     match_count = PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL;\n3294:   break;\n```\n- `could_continue` set at 800-801: `if (clen == 0 && poptable[codevalue] != 0) could_continue = TRUE;` — i.e. some state wanted to inspect a character but the subject ended. Also set explicitly by `OP_ANY`/`OP_DOLL`/`OP_DOLLM`/`TYPE*` CRLF cases (996, 1026, 1043, 1053, 1068, 1295, 1326, 1356, 1384, 1413) and via `reset_could_continue` carried to the next iteration (704-706, 772, 1040, 1065, 2130, 2309, 2342).\n- `mb->allowemptypartial = (re->max_lookbehind > 0) || (re->flags & PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY) != 0` (3531-3532).\n- Post-loop ENDANCHORED check at 3305-3308 (see §1.3).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Newline handling in the DFA\n\n`mb->nltype` / `mb->nllen` / `mb->nl[]` from `re->newline_convention` (3541-3579):\n| `PCRE2_NEWLINE_*` | value | `mb->nltype` | `mb->nllen` | `mb->nl[]` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `CR` | 1 | `NLTYPE_FIXED` | 1 | `{0x0D}` |\n| `LF` | 2 | `NLTYPE_FIXED` | 1 | `{0x0A}` |\n| `NUL` | 6 | `NLTYPE_FIXED` | 1 | `{0x00}` |\n| `CRLF` | 3 | `NLTYPE_FIXED` | 2 | `{0x0D,0x0A}` |\n| `ANY` | 4 | `NLTYPE_ANY` | (set dynamically) | — |\n| `ANYCRLF` | 5 | `NLTYPE_ANYCRLF` | (set dynamically) | — |\n| other | — | → `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL` (3576) | | |\n\n`IS_NEWLINE(p)` / `WAS_NEWLINE(p)` (`pcre2_internal.h:473-496`) with `NLBLOCK=mb`, `PSSTART=start_subject`, `PSEND=end_subject`:\n- FIXED: `p <= end - nllen && p[0]==nl[0] && (nllen==1 || p[1]==nl[1])`\n- ANY / ANYCRLF: `p < end && PRIV(is_newline)(p, nltype, end, &mb->nllen, utf)` — **mutates `mb->nllen`** to the length of the matched newline. This side effect is depended on by `OP_EODN` (1013) and `OP_DOLL` (1029), which evaluate `IS_NEWLINE(ptr)` *before* reading `mb->nllen`.\n- `PRIV(is_newline)` (`pcre2_newline.c`): ANYCRLF matches `LF`(len 1), `CR`(len 2 if `ptr<end-1 && ptr[1]==LF`, else 1). ANY additionally matches `VT`(0x0B), `FF`(0x0C), `NEL`(0x85, len `utf?2:1` in 8-bit), `LS`(0x2028) and `PS`(0x2029) (len 3 in 8-bit UTF).\n\n### 7.1 `.` — `OP_ANY` (987-1003) and `OP_TYPE*` with `d == OP_ANY`\n```c\n988: if (clen > 0 && !IS_NEWLINE(ptr))\n990:   if (ptr + 1 >= mb->end_subject && (mb->moptions & PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD) != 0 &&\n992:       NLBLOCK->nltype == NLTYPE_FIXED && NLBLOCK->nllen == 2 && c == NLBLOCK->nl[0])\n996:     could_continue = partial_newline = TRUE;\n1000:  else ADD_NEW(state_offset + 1, 0);\n```\nPer convention: `LF` → `.` excludes only `\\n`. `CR` → excludes only `\\r`. `NUL` → excludes only `\\0`. **`CRLF` → `.` excludes only a CR *immediately followed by* LF; a lone `\\r` and a lone `\\n` are matched by `.`.** `ANY` → excludes CR, LF, VT, FF, NEL, LS, PS. `ANYCRLF` → excludes CR, LF.\nThe CRLF-partial branch (990-997) fires only for `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD` + `NLTYPE_FIXED` + `nllen==2` + `c == CR` + `ptr+1 >= mb->end_subject`. Same code duplicated for `OP_TYPEPLUS/MINPLUS/POSPLUS` (1289-1296), `OP_TYPEQUERY/…` (1320-1327), `OP_TYPESTAR/…` (1350-1357), `OP_TYPEEXACT` (1378-1385), `OP_TYPEUPTO/…` (1407-1414).\nNote `OP_ALLANY` (1006-1009) is `if (clen > 0) ADD_NEW(state_offset+1, 0)` — no newline logic; `(?s).` compiles to `OP_ALLANY`.\n\n### 7.2 `$` — `OP_DOLL` (1022-1046, non-multiline)\n```c\n1023: if ((mb->moptions & PCRE2_NOTEOL) == 0)\n1025:   if (clen == 0 && (mb->moptions & PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD) != 0) could_continue = TRUE;\n1027:   else if (clen == 0 ||\n1028:       ((mb->poptions & PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY) == 0 && IS_NEWLINE(ptr) &&\n1029:          (ptr == end_subject - mb->nllen)))\n1031:     ADD_ACTIVE(state_offset + 1, 0);\n1032:   else if (ptr + 1 >= mb->end_subject &&\n1033:            (mb->moptions & (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD|PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT)) != 0 &&\n1034:            nltype == NLTYPE_FIXED && nllen == 2 && c == nl[0])\n1038:     if (PARTIAL_HARD) { reset_could_continue = TRUE; ADD_NEW_DATA(-(state_offset+1), 0, 1); }\n1043:     else could_continue = partial_newline = TRUE;\n```\nSo `$` matches at end of subject, or immediately before a **final** newline (of `mb->nllen` code units — the length reported by the ANY/ANYCRLF probe). `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` removes the pre-newline case. `PCRE2_NOTEOL` disables it entirely.\n\n### 7.3 `$` multiline — `OP_DOLLM` (1049-1073)\nSame, except the newline need not be final: condition at 1054-1055 is `clen == 0 || ((mb->poptions & PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY) == 0 && IS_NEWLINE(ptr))`. With `PCRE2_NOTEOL` set, the `else if (IS_NEWLINE(ptr)) ADD_ACTIVE(state_offset+1, 0)` at 1071-1072 keeps internal-newline matches alive.\n\n### 7.4 `^` — `OP_CIRC` (946-949) / `OP_CIRCM` (952-957)\n```c\n947: if (ptr == start_subject && (mb->moptions & PCRE2_NOTBOL) == 0)\n953: if ((ptr == start_subject && (mb->moptions & PCRE2_NOTBOL) == 0) ||\n954:     ((ptr != end_subject || (mb->poptions & PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX) != 0) && WAS_NEWLINE(ptr)))\n```\n`start_subject == subject` (offset 0), **not** `subject + start_offset` — so `^` with `start_offset > 0` matches only via `WAS_NEWLINE` (multiline). `PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX` allows `^` at `end_subject` right after a trailing newline.\n\n### 7.5 `\\A`, `\\G`, `\\Z`, `\\z`\n| Opcode | Line | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `OP_SOD` (`\\A`) | 970-972 | `ptr == start_subject` |\n| `OP_SOM` (`\\G`) | 975-977 | `ptr == start_subject + start_offset` |\n| `OP_EODN` (`\\Z`) | 1012-1019 | `clen == 0 \\|\\| (IS_NEWLINE(ptr) && ptr == end_subject - mb->nllen)`; with `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD` → **`return PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`** |\n| `OP_EOD` (`\\z`) | 960-967 | `ptr >= end_subject`; with `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD` → **`return PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`** |\n\n### 7.6 `\\R` — `OP_ANYNL` (2320-2354) and its `OP_ANYNL_EXTRA` variants\n```c\n2321: if (clen > 0) switch(c