st-relevant observations / latent issues\n\n1. **`PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST` bypasses the ENDANCHORED post-check** — `return match_count` at 891 skips 3305-3308.\n2. **ENDANCHORED in the DFA tests the scan position `ptr`, not each match end** (3307) — shorter ends can be returned in `ovector[2..]`.\n3. **`PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` leak** — the free at 3679-3684 sits *after* the `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSETLIMIT` (3506), `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL` (3576), `PCRE2_ERROR_BADUTFOFFSET` (3599) and `valid_utf` (3625) exits.\n4. **`DFA_BADRESTART` bound is 2× too loose** (`/3` at 3457 vs. real capacity `/6` at 571) → the `memcpy` at 673 can overrun for a hand-crafted `workspace[1]`.\n5. **`OP_VREVERSE` (variable-length lookbehind) reads the wrong field at 600** (`GET2(end_code, 2+LINK_SIZE)` is the *min* length for VREVERSE) and then always yields `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM` at 3259.\n6. `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` gates `OP_DOLLM` (1055) even though it is documented as ignored under `PCRE2_MULTILINE`.\n7. `match_call_count` is reset once (3535) not per bumpalong start, so `match_limit` is effectively \"total starts + nested evaluations\".\n8. Nested calls always get `wscount = 1000` (166 states) — the user's `wscount` does not size assertion/atomic/recursion sub-matches.\n9. `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` for `match_data == NULL` (3396) returns **without** setting `match_data->rc`; every other error goes through `EXIT` and sets it (4124).\n10. `offsetcount &= (uint32_t)(-2)` (568) — odd `oveccount*2` is impossible, but the nested calls pass `2` and `1000`, both even.\n11. `OP_ONCE`/`OP_BRAPOS` fast path sets `clen = 0` (3118, 3205) after moving `ptr`, which suppresses the `ptr += clen` advance at 3299 — the new state fires at the already-advanced `ptr`.\n12. Duplicate-state suppression (785-790): `active_states[j].offset == state_offset && active_states[j].count == current_state->count` — this is what terminates empty-loop patterns; note it compares `count` but not `data`.","usage":{"total_tokens":128478,"tool_