11 | 827 | `use_existing_match && match_data==NULL` | `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` |\n| 12 | 840-872 | MATCHED consistency checks | see §A.7 |\n| 13 | 887-917 | internal match_data creation | see §A.7 |\n| 14 | 921 | `internal_match_data != NULL` | `options &= ~PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` |\n| 15 | 925-926 | `ovector`, `ovector_count` cached | |\n| 16 | 930-933 | `scb.version=0; scb.input=subject; scb.output=(PCRE2_SPTR)buffer; scb.ovector=ovector` | set **once** |\n| 17 | 937-947 | `utf && (options & PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK)==0` | `valid_utf(replacement, rlength, &match_data->startchar)`; on failure sets `match_data->leftchar=0`, returns the UTF error code (`*blength` stays UNSET) — **this validates the REPLACEMENT, not the subject** |\n| 18 | 951-952 | `suboptions = options & SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS; options &= ~SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS` | |\n| 19 | 956-961 | `start_offset > length` | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` (-33), `match_data->leftchar=0` |\n| 20 | 965 | `!replacement_only` | `CHECKMEMCPY(subject, start_offset)` |\n\nNo NULL check exists for `code`, `buffer`, or `blength`. `SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS` mask = lines 48-52 = `EXTENDED|GLOBAL|LITERAL|MATCHED|OVERFLOW_LENGTH|REPLACEMENT_ONLY|UNKNOWN_UNSET|UNSET_EMPTY`.\n\n**Side effect at EXIT (1766-1769):** `if (internal_match_data != NULL) free(internal_match_data); else match_data->rc = rc;` — with an **external** match_data and **no** `SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED`, the caller's `match_data->rc` is overwritten with the substitute return value (substitution count on success, error code on failure). Not done for early returns (lines 797-909).\n\n---\n\n## A.1 Every option bit tested, and exactly what it changes\n\n### Substitute-specific bits (`suboptions`)\n\n| Option | Value | Lines tested | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL` | 0x100 | 1715 | Loop continues while `pcre2_next_match()` returns TRUE. Cleared at runtime (1673) if the substitute callout returns `< 0`. |\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_EXTENDED` | 0x200 | 1290, 1472 | (a) enables `${name:-…}` / `${name:+…:…}` (1290, requires additionally `!star && ptr < repend-2 && *ptr==':'`); (b) enables the whole backslash branch (1472): `\\L \\l \\U \\u \\E \\Q`, `\\n \\r \\t \\a \\e \\f`, `\\b`→BS, `\\v`→VT, `\\0dd \\o{} \\xhh \\x{} \\cX \\N{U+…}`, `\\1..\\n`, `\\g<n>`, `\\g<name>`, and `\\`+non-alphanumeric literals. Without EXTENDED, `\\` is an ordinary literal code unit (1617-1631). |\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNSET_EMPTY` | 0x400 | 1212, 1415 | Group is unset (`PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` from `length_bynumber`) **and** `special == 0` → `continue` (emit nothing) instead of returning `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`. Also used for `$+` when no group is set (1212). Has **no** effect when `special != 0` (`:-` / `:+` handle unset themselves). |\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNKNOWN_UNSET` | 0x800 | 1191, 1258, 1371, 1408 | Converts \"no such group\" into \"unset\": (a) `$+` with `top_bracket==0` (1191) → group 0 rather than `NOSUBSTRING`; (b) `$nn` with `nn > top_bracket` (1258) → skip remaining digits, treat as unset; (c) name not in nametable (1371) → `group = top_bracket+1` (guaranteed nonexistent); (d) `length_bynumber` returning `NOSUBSTRING` (1407-1411) → rewritten to `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`. Combine with `UNSET_EMPTY` to actually emit nothing. |\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_OVERFLOW_LENGTH` | 0x1000 | 649, 675 | On buffer exhaustion, set `overflowed=TRUE` and keep accumulating `extra_needed` instead of `goto NOROOM`. Final: `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` (1748-1755). |\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_LITERAL` | 0x8000 | 1054 | Single `CHECKMEMCPY(replacement, rlength)` per match; the whole char-by-char scanner is skipped. **Takes precedence over EXTENDED** (tested first). No `$`, no `\\`, no case forcing. |\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` | 0x10000 | 824, 840, 898, 979 | First iteration takes `rc = match_data->rc` instead of calling `pcre2_match` (979-983), then clears the flag. Triggers the 6 consistency checks (§A.7) and forces creation of an internal copy of the match_data (898-917). |\n| `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_REPLACEMENT_ONLY` | 0x20000 | 796, 825, 965, 1045, 1669, 1735 | Suppresses **4** verbatim copies: pre-`start_offset` prefix (965), inter-match fragment (1045), callout-rejection re-copy of the matched text (1669), trailing tail (1735-1739). Required if `partial`. Trailing NUL is still written (1741-1742). |\n\n### Match-pass-through / pattern bits\n\n| Option | Lines | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` (0x8) | never named in substitute.c | Only produced internally: `pcre2_next_match` sets `*poptions = PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` after an empty match (`pcre2_match_next.c:158`). Stored in `goptions`, OR-ed into the match call at 984. A caller-supplied `NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` survives in `options` and applies to **every** attempt. |\n| `PCRE2_ANCHORED` (0x80000000) | never named | Pure pass-through to `pcre2_match`. **This version never adds ANCHORED for the empty-match retry** (older PCRE2 used `NOTEMPTY_ATSTART|ANCHORED`). With caller-supplied ANCHORED + GLOBAL, every iteration must match exactly at the current `start_offset`. |\n| `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` (0x40000000) | 869, 938, 988 | Suppresses the replacement-string UTF validation (938); passed to `pcre2_match` for the subject; **auto-set after the first match** if `utf` (988) so the subject is validated only once; exempted from the DIFFSUBSOPTIONS comparison on both sides (869-870). |\n| `PCRE2_UTF` (0x00080000) | 758, 324, 392, 1564 | Read from `code->overall_options` only. Controls: `read_name_subst` UCD path (218), default case callout's UCD path (324/368) and `ord2utf` re-encoding (392), replacement UTF validation (938), `ord2utf` for `\\x{}` escapes (1564), `GETCHARINCTEST` in `LOADLITERAL` (1623), and `do_case_copy`'s `GETCHARINCTEST`. Passing `PCRE2_UTF` in `options` is **not** in `SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS`, so it survives to `pcre2_match` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` (`PUBLIC_MATCH_OPTIONS`, `pcre2_match.c:71-74`). |\n| `PCRE2_UCP` (0x00020000) | 325 | Read from `code->overall_options`. In the default case callout, `(utf \\|\\| ucp) && ch >= 128` selects the UCD path. **8-bit UCP-without-UTF hazard:** the UCD path may yield `ch > 255`, and line 396 then stores `temp[0] = ch` (truncated to one byte). E.g. `0xFF` (ÿ) upper-cased → U+0178 → emitted as byte `0x78` (`'x'`). Note the numeric collision: `PCRE2_UCP == PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_REPLACEMENT_ONLY == 0x00020000` (different namespaces, harmless here). |\n| `PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT` (0x10) / `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD` (0x20) | 759, 796, 1153, 1170 | Must be paired with `REPLACEMENT_ONLY` (796) else `BADOPTION`. When a partial match actually occurs, `pcre2_match` returns `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` and line 996 (`rc < 0`) propagates it. `$'` (1153-1157) and `$_` (1170-1174) → `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` (-76). `` $` `` is **allowed** in partial mode (only `subject[0..ovector[0]]` is read). SOFT can still produce a full match, in which case substitution proceeds normally. |\n| `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` (0x4000) | 861, 921 | Stripped at 921 whenever `internal_match_data != NULL` (i.e. whenever `match_data==NULL` was passed **or** `SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` is set). It only survives when an external match_data is supplied without `SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` — then every internal `pcre2_match` malloc/frees a subject copy. In the MATCHED path (861-863) it is what permits the subject **pointer** to differ from `match_data->subject`, with `memcmp` used instead. Line 915 clears `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` on the internal copy so the shared subject buffer is not double-freed. It **is** compared by the DIFFSUBSOPTIONS check (it is not in `SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS`). |\n\n---\n\n## A.2 Replacement mini-syntax — every branch, in dispatch order\n\nOuter scanner loop: 1064-1632. Per-iteration state: `ptrstack[20]`/`ptrstackptr` (973-974), `forcecase` (975), `casestart_offset` (976), `casestart_extra_needed` (977).\n\n### A.2.0 Pre-dispatch\n- **1078-1084** `ptr >= repend`: if `ptrstackptr == 0` → break (done); else pop `repend`, `ptr` (2 slots) and continue → returning from a nested `${…:…}` text.\n- **1088-1097** `escaped_literal` (in `\\Q`): `\\E` (`ptr[0]=='\\\\' && ptr<repend-1 && ptr[1]=='E'`) → clear, `ptr += 2`; otherwise `goto LOADLITERAL`.\n  - **QUIRK (worth a test):** `escaped_literal` is declared at **line 754, outside the global loop**. An unterminated `\\Q` leaves it TRUE across global iterations, so with `GLOBAL|EXTENDED` and replacement `\\Qabc`, substitution #1 emits `abc` but #2+ emit the literal text `\\Qabc` (the `\\` is emitted as a plain code unit because `ptr[1]=='Q'`, not `'E'`).\n\n### A.2.1 `$` branch (1101-1465) — no EXTENDED needed unless noted\n\n| Form | Lines | Condition / behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| `$` at end | 1110 | `++ptr >= repend` → `BAD` = `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPLACEMENT` (-35) |\n| `$$` | 1111 | `*ptr == '$'` → `goto LOADLITERAL` (emits one `$`, `ptr` advanced past the second) |\n| `$&` | 1126-1131 | `group = 0`, `special = 0` → `GROUP_SUBSTITUTE` (whole match) |\n| `` $` `` | 1132-1163 | sanity `substring_length_bynumber(md,0,&sublength)`; `subptr=subject`, `subptrend=subject+ovector[0]` → `SUBPTR_SUBSTITUTE` (pre-match text). Legal in partial mode. |\n| `$'` | 1132-1163 | same, but `if (partial)` → `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS`; `subptr=subject+ovector[1]`, `subptrend=subject+length` |\n| `$_` | 1165-1179 | `if (partial)` → `PARTIALSUBS`; whole input `subject..subject+length` |\n| `$+` | 1180-1217 | Only when `!(ptr+1<repend && ptr[1]=='{')`. `top_bracket==0` → `UNKNOWN_UNSET`? group=0 : `NOSUBSTRING`(-49). `top_bracket>0` → `oveccount < top_bracket+1` → `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE`(-54); then scan `group = top_bracket … 1` for first `ovector[2*group] != PCRE2_UNSET`. `group==0` (none set) → `UNSET_EMPTY`? `continue` : `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`(-55). |\n| `$+{name}` | 1180 | Excluded from `$+`; falls to `read_name_subst` on `\"+{…\"` → `+` not a word char → empty name → `BAD` |\n| `${…}` | 1219-1224, 1288-1324 | `inparens=TRUE`; `++ptr >= repend` → `BAD`. Terminator required at 1316-1320 else `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE`(-58) |\n| `$<name>` | 1225-1233, 1326-1331 | `inangle=TRUE`. **Numbers and `*` are disabled** (`!star && !inangle` at 1242; `!inangle` at 1235), so only names. Missing `>` → `BAD` |\n| `$*name` / `${*name}` | 1235-1240, 1336-1354 | `!inangle && next == '*'` → `star=TRUE`. `${*…}` disables the extended `:` branch (`!star` at 1291) |\n| `$*MARK` / `${*MARK}` | 1338-1353 | `strcmp_c8(name, \"MARK\") == 0` (case-**sensitive**). `mark = pcre2_get_mark(md)`; `mark == NULL` → **emit nothing, no error**. Else `fraglength = mark[-1]` (length stored in the code unit *before* the mark → marks may contain embedded NULs). Any other `*name` → `BAD` |\n| `$n`, `$nn`, `${n}` | 1242-1270 | Requires `!star && !inangle && next in '0'..'9'`. Greedy digits, `group = group*10 + d`. `group > top_bracket` is checked **only inside** the `while(++ptr…)` body: `UNKNOWN_UNSET` → skip remaining digits + break, else `NOSUBSTRING` at the offending digit. **Single-digit `$5` with `top_bracket=2` never trips this check** — it reaches `length_bynumber` which returns `NOSUBSTRING` at 1405, so the error is the same but `*blength` (the reported offset) differs from the multi-digit case. `$0` is always valid. |\n| `$name`, `${name}`, `$<name>` | 1271-1280 | `read_name_subst(&ptr, repend, utf, code->tables+ctypes_offset)`; failure → `BAD`. Then `name_len = ptr-name_start`, copied into `PCRE2_UCHAR name[MAX_NAME_SIZE+1]`, NUL-terminated |\n| `${name:-default}` | **EXTENDED only** 1290-1312 | `(suboptions & EXTENDED) && !star && ptr < repend-2 && *ptr==':'`; `special = *(++ptr)`; must be `'+'` or `'-'` else `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSTITUTION`(-59). For `'-'`: `text1_start = ++ptr`, `find_text_end(..., last=TRUE)`. At 1424-1448: `rc==0` (group **is** set) → `goto LITERAL_SUBSTITUTE` (use the group); group unset → push `(ptr, repend)`, reprocess `text1` |\n| `${name:+ifset:ifunset}` | **EXTENDED only** 1290-1311 | `'+'`: `find_text_end(..., last=FALSE)` → `text1` ends at unescaped `:` or `}`; if `*ptr==':'` then `text2_start=++ptr`, `find_text_end(..., TRUE)`. At 1433-1447: push `(ptr, repend)`; `rc==0` (set) → reprocess `text1`; unset → reprocess `text2` (may be NULL/NULL = empty). `ptrstackptr >= PTR_STACK_SIZE` (20, i.e. 10 nesting levels) → `BAD` |\n| `${name:…}` without EXTENDED | 1314-1321 | else-branch requires `*ptr=='}'` → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE` |\n| `${n:}`, i.e. `ptr >= repend-2` | 1291 | Guard fails → else-branch → `REPMISSINGBRACE` |\n\n**`GROUP_SUBSTITUTE` (1361-1463)**\n- `group < 0` (name path, 1367-1398): `pcre2_substring_nametable_scan(code, name, &first, &last)`. `NOSUBSTRING && UNKNOWN_UNSET` → `group = top_bracket+1`. Else `rc<0` → `PTREXIT`; then walk `entry = first..last` step `rc`: `ng = GET2(entry,0)`; if `ng < ovector_count`: remember the **first** such `ng`, and `break` on the first with `ovector[ng*2] != PCRE2_UNSET`. If none in the ovector at all → `group = GET2(first,0)` (which will then give `UNAVAILABLE`).\n- `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber(match_data, group, &sublength)` (1404). Error mapping at 1405-1418: `NOSUBSTRING + UNKNOWN_UNSET` → `UNSET`; any non-`UNSET` error → `PTREXIT`; `UNSET` with `special==0` → `UNSET_EMPTY ? continue : PTREXIT`.\n- `LITERAL_SUBSTITUTE` (1452-1454): `subptr = subject+ovector[group*2]`, `subptrend = subject+ovector[group*2+1]`.\n- `SUBPTR_SUBSTITUTE` (1458-1463): `forcecase != NONE && substitute_case_callout == NULL` → `CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT`, else `CHECKMEMCPY`.\n\n### A.2.2 `\\` branch (1472-1613) — **requires `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_EXTENDED`**\n\nCase-forcing is recognised **before** `check_escape` (1478-1520), so `\\U`/`\\L`/`\\u`/`\\l` never reach it:\n\n| Escape | Lines | `new_forcecase` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `\\L` | 1480-1484 | `{LOWER, single_char=FALSE}` |\n| `\\l` | 1486-1497 | `{LOWER, TRUE}`; if `ptr+2 < repend && ptr[0]=='\\\\' && ptr[1]=='U'` → `{REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST(4), FALSE}`, `ptr += 2` (Perl `\\l\\U`) |\n| `\\U` | 1499-1503 | `{UPPER, FALSE}` |\n| `\\u` | 1505-1516 | `{TITLE_FIRST, TRUE}`; if `ptr+2 < repend && ptr[0]=='\\\\' && ptr[1]=='L'` → `{TITLE_FIRST, FALSE}`, `ptr += 2` (Perl `\\u\\L`) |\n| `\\E` | 1547-1550 (`case ESC_E: goto SETFORCECASE`) | `new_forcecase` is `{NONE, FALSE}` → turns forcing off |\n\n`SETFORCECASE` (1524-1540): if `substitute_case_callout != NULL && forcecase.to_case != NONE` → `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` first (flush the pending region), then `forcecase = new_forcecase; casestart_offset = buff_offset; casestart_extra_needed = extra_needed; continue`.\n\nNote the `\\l\\U` / `\\u\\L` lookahead uses `ptr + 2 < repend` (strictly), so `\\l\\U` at the very end of the replacement is **not** collapsed into REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST — it is treated as `\\l` then a separate `\\U`.\n\nEverything else goes through `PRIV(check_escape)(&ptr, repend, &ch, &errorcode, code->overall_options, code->extra_options, code->top_bracket, FALSE, NULL)` (1543-1544). `cb == NULL` filter (`pcre2_compile.c:1617-1626`): for table-zero escapes, **only** `0-9`, `c`, `o`, `x`, `g` are accepted; anything else → `ERR3` → `errorcode != 0` → `BADESCAPE` = `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE` (-57). `alt_bsux` is forced FALSE, so `\\x` always uses Perl syntax.\n\nResult dispatch (1547-1612):\n\n| `rc` | Lines | Behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ESC_E` | 1549 | `goto SETFORCECASE` (turn off forcing). Isolated `\\E` outside any forcing = no-op. |\n| `ESC_Q` | 1552-1554 | `escaped_literal = TRUE; continue` |\n| `0` (data char) | 1556-1576 | `utf ? ord2utf(ch,temp) : temp[0]=ch,chlen=1`; then case-forced copy or `CHECKMEMCPY`. Covers: `\\a`(BEL), `\\e`(ESC), `\\f`(FF), `\\n`(LF), `\\r`(CR), `\\t`(HT); `\\0`, `\\00`, `\\000` and `\\1..\\7` falling back to octal; `\\o{ddd}`; `\\xhh`, `\\x{…}`; `\\cX`; `\\N{U+dddd}` (UTF only, `pcre2_compile.c:1560-1568`); every `\\`+non-alphanumeric (`\\$`, `\\\\`, `\\}`, `\\{`, `\\:`, `\\<`, `\\>`, `\\;`, `\\=`, `\\?`, `\\@`, `\\[`, `\\]`, `\\^`, `\\_`, `` \\` ``) |\n| `ESC_b` | 1557,1560 | `ch = CHAR_BS` (0x08) — **not** word boundary |\n| `ESC_v` | 1558,1561 | `ch = CHAR_VT` (0x0B) — **not** vertical whitespace class |\n| `ESC_g` | 1578-1602 | `\\g<name>`: requires `*ptr=='<'`, then `read_name_subst`, then `*ptr=='>'`; any failure → `BADESCAPE`. Sets `special=0`, `group=-1` → `GROUP_SUBSTITUTE`. (`\\g<number>` is consumed inside `check_escape` and returns `-(n+1)`, incl. `\\g<0>`.) |\n| `rc < 0` | 1604-1610 | Backreference: `special=0; group = -rc - 1` → `GROUP_SUBSTITUTE` (covers `\\1`..`\\9`, `\\10`+, `\\g<n>`) |\n| any other `rc > 0` | 1611 | `BADESCAPE`. Explicitly rejects `\\A \\B \\C \\D \\G \\H \\K \\N`(plain) `\\P \\R \\S \\V \\W \\X \\Z \\d \\h \\k \\p \\s \\w \\z` |\n\n**`find_text_end` (76-180)** — validates `${…:…}` texts eagerly, even for the branch that will not be taken:\n- `literal` mode (from `ESC_Q`) exits only on a literal `\\E` (89-93).\n- `}` at `nestlevel==0` → success, `ptr` at `}` (96-100).\n- `:` at `nestlevel==0 && !last` → success, `ptr` at `:` (102).\n- `$` followed by `{` → `nestlevel++`, `ptr += 1` (104-111). **Bare `$name` does not nest.**\n- `\\` (113-172): `ptr[1] in {L,l,U,u}` → `ptr += 1; continue` (skipped, unvalidated). Else `check_escape`; `errorcode != 0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE`. Accepted: `0`, `ESC_b`, `ESC_v`, `ESC_E`, `ESC_Q`(→literal), `ESC_g`, and any `erc < 0`. Any other positive escape → `ptr = esc_end_ptr; PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE`.\n- Fell off the end → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE` (175).\n\n### A.2.3 Literal code unit (1617-1631 / `LOADLITERAL`)\n`ch_start = ptr; GETCHARINCTEST(ch, ptr)` — one **character** in UTF, one code unit otherwise. Then case-forced copy or `CHECKMEMCPY(ch_start, ptr-ch_start)`.\n\n### A.2.4 `read_name_subst` (201-261)\n- `ptr >= ptrend` → FALSE.\n- No \"must not start with a digit\" rule (comment 211-212).\n- UTF: `GETCHAR(c,ptr); type=UCD_CHARTYPE(c)`; accept while `type==ucp_Nd || ucp_gentype[type]==ucp_L || c=='_'`; `ptr++; FORWARDCHARTEST(ptr,ptrend)`.\n- Non-UTF 8-bit: `MAX_255(*ptr)` is `TRUE` always, so the gate is `(ctypes[*ptr] & ctype_word) != 0` (0x10 = alnum or `_`) from `code->tables + ctypes_offset` — so bytes ≥ 128 depend on the (possibly custom) character tables.\n- `ptr - nameptr > MAX_NAME_SIZE` (128, `config.h:223`) → FALSE (counted in **code units**).\n- `ptr == nameptr` (empty) → FALSE.\n- On both paths `*ptrptr = ptr` is written (so `PTREXIT`'s reported offset reflects the partial scan).\n\n---\n\n## A.3 Substitute case callout / default casing\n\n### Internal `to_case` values (268-275)\n`NONE=0`, `LOWER=1`, `UPPER=2`, `TITLE_FIRST=3` (public, `pcre2.h:517-519`), `REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST=4` (**internal only, never passed to a user callout**). `case_state = { int to_case; BOOL single_char; }`.\n\nReachable `(to_case, single_char)` pairs: `(LOWER,FALSE)`=`\\L`, `(LOWER,TRUE)`=`\\l`, `(UPPER,FALSE)`=`\\U`, `(TITLE_FIRST,TRUE)`=`\\u`, `(TITLE_FIRST,FALSE)`=`\\u\\L`, `(REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST,FALSE)`=`\\l\\U`.\n\n### Invocation sites\n| Site | Lines | Macro |\n|---|---|---|\n| `$*MARK` text | 1346-1350 | `CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT` if callout NULL, else plain `CHECKMEMCPY` (deferred) |\n| group / `` $` `` / `$'` / `$_` content (`SUBPTR_SUBSTITUTE`) | 1459-1463 | ditto |\n| escape-produced data char | 1571-1575 | ditto |\n| literal code unit | 1626-1630 | ditto |\n| `\\L\\l\\U\\u\\E` boundary flush | 1532-1534 | `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` → `CHECKCASECPY_CALLOUT` (callout only) |\n| end of the replacement string | 1641-1643 | `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` (callout only) |\n\n**Two distinct architectures:**\n- **No callout (`substitute_case_callout == NULL`)** — transformation is applied *eagerly*, per fragment, via `default_substitute_case_callout` (297-434). Source and destination must not overlap (assert 320-321), which holds because the source is always the subject, the mark, `temp[]`, or the replacement.\n- **Callout set** — text is first copied **verbatim** into the output; at each `\\L\\l\\U\\u\\E` boundary and at the end of the replacement, `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` (714-737) rewinds `buff_offset` to `casestart_offset`, restores `lengthleft`, and re-transforms the region **in place** through `do_case_copy` (443-605). Consequence: the transform spans *everything* emitted since the escape (literals, group content, marks, escape chars) as one unit, and the user callout is invoked with **overlapping** `input`/`output` pointers.\n\n### `default_substitute_case_callout` (297-434)\n- `input_len == 0` → return 0 (328).\n- 330-354 map `to_case` to `(next_to_upper, rest_to_upper)` and mutate `state->to_case`: `TITLE_FIRST → LOWER` (346), `REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST → UPPER` (352). `default:` is `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE()` + return 0.\n- 356-358: `single_char` → `state->to_case = NONE` (so `\\l`/`\\u` affect exactly one character).\n- Per character (`GETCHARINCTEST`, 365):\n  - **Unicode path (368-380):** `(utf || ucp) && ch >= 128` → `type = UCD_CHARTYPE(ch); if (ucp_gentype[type]==ucp_L && type != (next_to_upper ? ucp_Lu : ucp_Ll)) ch = UCD_OTHERCASE(ch);`. Only the simple 1:1 othercase table. **The TODO at 375-379 states explicitly: no `SpecialCasing.txt` mappings (ß→SS, ligatures, final sigma), not fully correct even for ordinary mappings, and `PCRE2_EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING` is NOT consulted.** Grep confirms `TURKISH_CASING` appears nowhere in `pcre2_substitute.c`. `ucp_Lt` characters are gentype `L` and are therefore othercased.\n  - **Table path (383-389):** `MAX_255(ch)` (always TRUE in 8-bit) → `if ((code->tables + cbits_offset + (next_to_upper?cbit_upper:cbit_lower))[ch/8] & (1<<(ch%8))) == 0) ch = (code->tables + fcc_offset)[ch];` — flip only if not already in the target class; uses the *pattern's* tables.\n  - Re-encode: `utf ? ord2utf(ch,temp) : temp[0]=ch, chlen=1` (391-397).\n  - Write only if `!overflow && chlen <= output_cap` (399-408); otherwise set `overflow` and keep counting.\n  - `written` accumulates; `chlen > ~0 - written` → return `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` (410-411).\n  - `next_to_upper = rest_to_upper` (414).\n  - `single_char` (418-430): `memcpy` the remainder verbatim if it fits, add `rest_len` to `written`, return.\n- Returns the number of code units **required** (may exceed `output_cap`).\n- `CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT` (687-700) does **not** check for `~0`, so the default path cannot produce `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE`.\n\n### `do_case_copy` (443-605) — callout path\n- `PCRE2_ASSERT(input_len != 0)` (468) — never called with an empty region (`DELAYEDFORCECASE` guards with `chars_outstanding > 0`, 718).\n- **Fast path (485-494):** `single_char == FALSE` and `to_case ∈ {LOWER, UPPER, TITLE_FIRST}` → one call `substitute_case_callout(input, input_len, output, output_cap, to_case, data)` with `input == output`. `TITLE_FIRST` → `state->to_case = LOWER`.\n- **Split path:** `single_char==TRUE` → `ch1_to_case = to_case`, `rest_to_case = NONE`; `REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST` → `ch1_to_case = LOWER`, `rest_to_case = UPPER`.\n  - 509-518: copy the first character into local `ch1[6]` via `GETCHARINCTEST`.\n  - 529-561: size-discovery loop. `ch1_cap = ch1_len`; `max_ch1_cap = output_cap - rest_len`. Call the callout on `ch1`; `rc == ~0` → propagate; `rc <= ch1_cap` → done; `rc > max_ch1_cap` → `ch1_overflow = TRUE`; else `memmove` the rest right by `rc`, `ch1_cap = rc`, retry. The loop deliberately re-calls with identical input in case the callout is non-deterministic (comment 523-527).\n  - 563-573 (`rest_to_case == NONE`): `memmove(output+rc, rest, rest_len)` when no overflow; `rc2 = rest_len`; `state->to_case = NONE`.\n  - 574-596 (`REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST`): second callout on `rest` with `to_case = UPPER`, using a `dummy[1]`/cap 0 if `ch1_overflow`; `rc2 == ~0` → propagate; if `ch1_overflow && rc2 < rest_len` then `rc2 = rest_len` (so the reported total always exceeds `output_cap`); `state->to_case = UPPER`.\n  - 598-604: `rc2 > ~0 - rc` → return `~0`; else return `rc + rc2`.\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE` (-69)** is produced **only** at `CASEERROR` (1775-1777), reached only from `CHECKCASECPY_CALLOUT` (708) when `do_case_copy` returns `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` — i.e. the user callout returned `PCRE2_SIZE_MAX`, or an internal `rc+rc2` overflow. So `PCRE2_SIZE_MAX` is the documented callout failure sentinel.\n- **`pessimistic_case_inflation(len) = (len >> 3) + 10`** (289-293). Used by `DELAYEDFORCECASE` when already `overflowed` (722), because the callout cannot be invoked without a buffer. Comment 280-287: with a case callout **plus** `OVERFLOW_LENGTH`, **more than two calls may be needed** to converge on the buffer size.\n- `to_case = 4` (`REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST`) and `0` are never passed to the user callout; only 1/2/3.\n\n---\n\n## A.4 Substitute callout (`pcre2_set_substitute_callout`)\n\nInvoked at **1648-1710**, once per successful match, **after** the replacement has been emitted (and after the trailing `DELAYEDFORCECASE`), and **before** the GLOBAL-continue decision.\n\nGuard: `mcontext != NULL && mcontext->substitute_callout != NULL`.\n\nBlock (`pcre2.h:616-626`), all fields written by substitute:\n| Field | Set at | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `version` | 930 | `0` |\n| `input` | 931 | the (possibly `null_str`-substituted) subject pointer |\n| `output` | 932 | `(PCRE2_SPTR)buffer` (base, not current) |\n| `output_offsets[0]` | 1046 | `buff_offset` **before** the replacement was emitted |\n| `output_offsets[1]` | 1655 | `buff_offset` **after** the replacement |\n| `ovector` | 933 | `pcre2_get_ovector_pointer(match_data)` (the internal copy when MATCHED / when `match_data==NULL` was passed) |\n| `oveccount` | 1047 | `rc` after `if (rc==0) rc = ovector_count` (1043) — i.e. pairs set, or the full ovector count when the ovector was too small |\n| `subscount` | 1654 | `subs`, 1-based |\n\nReturn value:\n- **`0`** — accept. Nothing else happens.\n- **`> 0`** — reject this substitution: rewind `buff_offset -= newlength`, `lengthleft += newlength` (1667-1668), then `if (!replacement_only) CHECKMEMCPY(subject+ovector[0], ovector[1]-ovector[0])` (1669) — the original matched text is restored. **With `REPLACEMENT_ONLY` the rejected match contributes nothing at all.** Global loop continues.\n- **`< 0`** — reject as above **and** `suboptions &= ~PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL` (1673), so the loop exits at 1715 with `start_offset = ovector[1]` and the tail of the subject is copied.\n- **`subs` still counts a rejected substitution** (incremented at 1037 before the callout), so the return value of `pcre2_substitute` counts *attempted* substitutions.\n\n**Overflowed path (1686-1709):** when `overflowed` is TRUE the callout is **not** called at all. Instead: `newlength = (buff_offset - output_offsets[0]) + (extra_needed - sub_start_extra_needed)` (saturating at `~0`), `oldlength = ovector[1]-ovector[0]`; if `oldlength > newlength` then `extra_needed += oldlength - newlength` (overflow → `TOOLARGEREPLACE`). I.e. the size probe is pessimistic over both accept and reject, and a negative return is deliberately ignored during the sizing pass (1706-1708).\n\n---\n\n## A.5 Output buffer sizing\n\n- **In:** `*blength` = capacity in **code units, including room for the trailing NUL**. `lengthleft = buff_length = *blength` (778). Immediately `*blength = PCRE2_UNSET` (779).\n- **Out, success (1760-1764):** `rc = subs` (≥ 0), `*blength = buff_offset - 1` = length **excluding** the trailing NUL. The NUL is always written (1741-1742).\n- **Out, `overflowed` (1748-1755):** `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (-48), `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` = the **total required capacity including the NUL**. `extra_needed > ~0 - buff_length` → `TOOLARGEREPLACE` (-70).\n- **Out, `NOROOM` (1771-1773):** `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `*blength` stays `PCRE2_UNSET`. Reached whenever the buffer is exhausted and `OVERFLOW_LENGTH` is clear (649, 675).\n- **Out, replacement-syntax error (1783-1792):** `BAD`→`BADREPLACEMENT`, `BADESCAPE`→`BADREPESCAPE`, and every `goto PTREXIT` set `*blength = (PCRE2_SIZE)(ptr - replacement)` — an **offset into the replacement string** where the error was detected. Applies to: `BADREPLACEMENT`, `BADREPESCAPE`, `REPMISSINGBRACE`, `BADSUBSTITUTION`, `NOSUBSTRING`, `NOUNIQUESUBSTRING`, `UNAVAILABLE`, `UNSET`, `PARTIALSUBS`.\n- **Out, everything else** (`BADOFFSET`, `BADSUBSPATTERN`, `TOOMANYREPLACE`, `TOOLARGEREPLACE`, `REPLACECASE`, `INTERNAL_DUPMATCH`, match errors, UTF errors, DIFFSUBS*, `NULL`, `BADOPTION`, `DFA_UFUNC`, `NOMEMORY` from match_data create): `*blength == PCRE2_UNSET`.\n\n**One-pass vs two-pass (`CHECKMEMCPY`, 638-660):**\n```\nif (overflowed)        { extra_needed += n (overflow→TOOLARGEREPLACE); }\nelse if (lengthleft < n) { if (!OVERFLOW_LENGTH) goto NOROOM;\n                           overflowed = TRUE; extra_needed = n - lengthleft; }\nelse                   { memcpy(buffer+buff_offset, from, n);\n                         buff_offset += n; lengthleft -= n; }\n```\nOnce `overflowed` is set nothing further is written to `buffer`, but matching, replacement parsing, and error detection all continue to completion. `CHECKCASECPY_BASE` (668-685) is analogous but obtains `chkcc_rc` from a casing helper first, and `CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT` passes `output_cap = overflowed ? 0 : lengthleft` (692) then folds `chkcc_rc` into `extra_needed`.\n\n**Boundary matrix (required = final output length incl. NUL):**\n| `*blength` in | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `> required` | `rc = subs`, `*blength = required-1`, bytes past that untouched |\n| `== required` (exactly enough) | `rc = subs`, `*blength = required-1` |\n| `== required-1` (one too small) | the trailing-NUL `CHECKMEMCPY(temp,1)` at 1742 overflows → `NOMEMORY`; with `OVERFLOW_LENGTH`, `*blength = required` |\n| `0` with `buffer == NULL` | `lengthleft = 0`; any non-empty copy overflows; the NUL copy always overflows → `NOMEMORY`, and with `OVERFLOW_LENGTH` `*blength = 0 + extra_needed = required`. This is the canonical \"size probe\". (Zero-length `CHECKMEMCPY`s still execute `memcpy(NULL, from, 0)`, which is technically UB but harmless in practice.) |\n\n**Two-call protocol caveats:** exact convergence in two calls is guaranteed **only** when there is no `substitute_case_callout`. With a case callout, `DELAYEDFORCECASE` in the overflowed state uses the `(n>>3)+10` estimate (722), which can underestimate → more calls needed (documented at 280-287).\n\n---\n\n## A.6 GLOBAL / empty-match advance\n\nAll advance logic now lives in `pcre2_next_match` (`pcre2_match_next.c:96-169`), called at **1716**:\n```\nif ((suboptions & PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL) == 0 ||\n    !pcre2_next_match(match_data, &start_offset, &goptions))\n  { start_offset = ovector[1]; break; }\nPCRE2_ASSERT(start_offset == ovector[1]);            /* 1728 */\n```\n`pcre2_next_match` branches (uses `match_data->rc`, `->start_offset`, `->ovector`, `->subject_length`):\n1. **`rc < 0`** (108-109) → FALSE. Cannot happen here (substitute breaks on NOMATCH at 994 / exits on `rc<0` at 996).\n2. **`ovector[0] != start_offset && ovector[1] == start_offset`** (129-141) — `\\K`-in-lookaround. `start_offset >= subject_length` → FALSE; else `*pstart_offset = do_bumpalong(md, ovector[1])`, `*poptions = 0`. **Unreachable from `pcre2_substitute`**, because it implies `ovector[1] < ovector[0]`, which line 1001-1005 has already rejected with `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSPATTERN` (-60). This is exactly what makes the assert at 1728 valid.\n3. **Empty match: `ovector[0] == ovector[1]`** (147-160) — `ovector[0] >= subject_length` → FALSE (done); else `*pstart_offset = ovector[1]` (**same offset**) and `*poptions = PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`.\n4. **Non-empty match** (166-168) → `*pstart_offset = ovector[1]`, `*poptions = 0`.\n\nKey consequences for tests:\n- `goptions` is only ever `0` or `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`. **`PCRE2_ANCHORED` is never added.**\n- After an empty match, the retry is *unanchored* with `NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`, so `pcre2_match` performs its own internal bumpalong and may return a match starting **later** than `start_offset` — including another *empty* match at a later position (NOTEMPTY_ATSTART only forbids an empty match **at the start offset**). The gap `[start_offset, ovector[0])` is then copied by `fraglength = ovector[0] - start_offset` (1044-1045).\n- If that retry returns `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH`, the global loop simply **breaks** (994) — there is no explicit \"advance one char and retry\" in `pcre2_substitute` any more.\n- **CRLF / UTF advancement** is therefore handled by `pcre2_match`'s internal bumpalong, not by substitute. `do_bumpalong` (`pcre2_match_next.c:49-88`) — which skips `CR LF` atomically when `code->newline_convention ∈ {PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF, ANY, ANYCRLF}` (61-71) and otherwise advances one full character with `FORWARDCHARTEST` in UTF (76-84) or `offset+1` — is reachable **only** via branch 2, i.e. never from `pcre2_substitute`.\n- **Progress assertions:** 1001-1005 → `BADSUBSPATTERN` if `ovector[1] < ovector[0]` **or** `ovector[0] < start_offset`. 1015-1023 → `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL_DUPMATCH` (-65) unless `subs == 0` or `ovector[1] > ovecsave[1]` or (`ovector[1]==ovector[0] && ovecsave[1] > ovecsave[0] && ovector[1]==ovecsave[1]`) — i.e. the only permitted non-advancing case is an empty match immediately after a non-empty match ending at the same point. `ovecsave[]` updated at 1026-1027.\n- `subs == INT_MAX` → `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOMANYREPLACE` (-61) (1032-1036).\n- `if (rc == 0) rc = ovector_count;` (1043) normalises \"ovector too small\" for `scb.oveccount`.\n\n---\n\n## A.7 `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED`\n\n**Requirements on the incoming `match_data`, in order (840-872):**\n| Check | Line | Error |\n|---|---|---|\n| `match_data != NULL` | 827 | `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` (-51) |\n| `match_data->rc < 0 && != PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` | 845-846 | returns `match_data->rc` verbatim. Catches `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (-2), `MATCHLIMIT`, `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` (-75), etc. Deliberately duplicates the later `rc<0` guard because the rest of the block may be uninitialised (comment 842-844). |\n| `match_data->matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` | 849-850 | `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC` (-41) |\n| `code != match_data->code` | 852-853 | `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSPATTERN` (-71) — **pointer identity**, not structural equality |\n| `length != match_data->subject_length` **or** `!(original_subject == match_data->subject \\|\\| ((flags & PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT) && (length==0 \\|\\| memcmp(subject, match_data->subject, length)==0)))` | 859-864 | `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSSUBJECT` (-72). `original_subject` is captured at **762**, before the `NULL→null_str` rewrite, so `subject==NULL, length==0` correctly matches `match_data->subject==NULL`. `length` is post-`ZERO_TERMINATED` resolution (819). Without `COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` the pointers must be **identical**; with it, contents are compared. |\n| `start_offset != match_data->start_offset` | 866-867 | `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSOFFSET` (-73) |\n| `(options & ~(SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS\\|PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK)) != (match_data->options & ~PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK)` | 869-871 | `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSOPTIONS` (-74). Compares `ANCHORED, ENDANCHORED, NOTBOL, NOTEOL, NOTEMPTY, NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, PARTIAL_HARD, PARTIAL_SOFT, NO_JIT, COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT, DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK` exactly; substitute-only bits and `NO_UTF_CHECK` are exempt. `match_data->options` is set by `pcre2_match` (`pcre2_match.c:8171 = original_options`). |\n\n**Internal match_data copy (898-917):** `pairs = min(code->top_bracket+1, match_data->oveccount)`; `pcre2_match_data_create(match_data->oveccount, &gcontext)` (NULL → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`); `memcpy(internal, external, offsetof(pcre2_match_data, ovector) + 2*pairs*sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE))`; then `heapframes = NULL`, `heapframes_size = 0`, `flags &= ~PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT`. **The caller's block is never modified.** `gcontext.memctl` comes from `mcontext` if non-NULL, else from `code` (890-892, 902-904).\n\n**Notes:**\n- `match_data->rc == PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` is **valid**: iteration 1 sets `rc = NOMATCH` (981) → break (994) → 0 substitutions, whole subject copied (or, with `REPLACEMENT_ONLY`, only the NUL).\n- `match_data->rc == 0` (ovector too small) is valid; `rc` becomes `ovector_count` at 1043.\n- `MATCHED | GLOBAL` is valid: the first match comes from the block, subsequent ones from `pcre2_match` on the internal copy.\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` (-76) is unrelated to MATCHED**: it is produced only at 1155 and 1172, for `$'` and `$_` when the caller passed `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD/SOFT`.\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` (-75) is never generated by `pcre2_substitute.c`.** It originates in `pcre2_match.c:1030` (`Fstart_match < start_subject+start_offset || Fstart_match > Feptr`, when `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK` is clear) and is merely propagated by 996 (or returned verbatim by 845-846 in the MATCHED path). Substitute's own `\\K` guard is `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSPATTERN` (-60) at 1001-1005, which fires when `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK` **is** set and a `\\K` moved the match start.\n\n---\n\n## A.8 `start_offset`, zero-terminated, degenerate inputs\n\n| Configuration | Behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| `start_offset > length` | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` (-33), `match_data->leftchar = 0` (956-961) |\n| `start_offset == length` | Valid; an empty match at the end is possible |\n| `0 < start_offset < length` | `subject[0..start_offset)` copied verbatim unless `REPLACEMENT_ONLY` (965). All matches must start at `>= start_offset` (1001) |\n| `start_offset` mid-UTF-character | Not validated by substitute; `pcre2_match` returns `PCRE2_ERROR_BADUTFOFFSET` (`pcre2_match.c:7161`) unless `NO_UTF_CHECK` |\n| `subject == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` (`length = ~0`) | `length = PRIV(strlen)(subject)` (819). Applied **before** the DIFFSUBSSUBJECT/DIFFSUBSOFFSET comparisons |\n| `subject == NULL, length == 0` | `subject = null_str` (`{0xcd}`), `original_subject` remains NULL for the MATCHED comparison |\n| `subject == NULL, length != 0` | `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` (-51) |\n| `length == 0` (non-NULL) | Only an empty match at offset 0 is possible; output is `replacement` + NUL (or the NUL alone with no match) |\n| `replacement == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` | `rlength = PRIV(strlen)(replacement)` (808) |\n| `replacement == NULL, rlength == 0` | `replacement = null_str`; behaves as an empty replacement |\n| `replacement == NULL, rlength != 0` | `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` |\n| `rlength == 0` | `repend == replacement`; the scanner breaks immediately at 1078-1080; with `LITERAL`, `CHECKMEMCPY(ptr, 0)` = no-op. Each match deletes its matched text |\n| Replacement containing embedded NULs | Fully supported (length-driven, never NUL-scanned after 808) |\n| Output always | Trailing binary zero written at 1741-1742, counted in the capacity but excluded from `*blength` |\n\n---\n\n# PART B — `pcre2_substring.c`\n\nShared preconditions (none are checked): `match_data != NULL`, `stringname != NULL`, `match_data` must have been through a match (`->code`, `->matchedby`, `->rc`, `->subject`, `->subject_length` are **uninitialised** in a fresh `pcre2_match_data_create` block — `pcre2_match_data.c:54-68` only sets `oveccount`, `flags`, `heapframes*`).\n\n## B.1 `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber` (311-352) — the engine everything else uses\n\n```\ncount = match_data->rc;\nif (count == PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL)                          /* 317-321 */\n  { if (stringnumber > 0) return PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL;  count = 0; }\nelse if (count < 0) return count;                          /* 322 */\n\nif (matchedby != PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER)          /* 324-332 */\n  { if (stringnumber >  code->top_bracket) return PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING;   /* 326 */\n    if (stringnumber >= oveccount)         return PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE;   /* 328 */\n    if (ovector[stringnumber*2]==PCRE2_UNSET) return PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET; }    /* 330 */\nelse                                                       /* 333-337 */\n  { if (stringnumber >= oveccount)         return PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE;   /* 335 */\n    if (count != 0 && stringnumber >= (uint32_t)count) return PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET; }\n\nleft  = ovector[stringnumber*2];  right = ovector[stringnumber*2+1];         /* 339-340 */\nif (left > subject_length || right > subject_length) return PCRE2_ERROR_INVALIDOFFSET; /* 344-348, LCOV-excluded */\nif (sizeptr != NULL) *sizeptr = (left > right)? 0 : right - left;            /* 350 */\nreturn 0;\n```\n\nDistinct valid configurations:\n| Config | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `rc > 0`, `n <= top_bracket`, `n < oveccount`, group **set** | `0`, `*sizeptr = right-left` |\n| group **unset** (`ovector[2n] == PCRE2_UNSET`) | `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` (-55) |\n| `n > top_bracket` (no such group) | `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING` (-49) — **checked BEFORE `UNAVAILABLE`**, so `n=5, top_bracket=2, oveccount=1` gives `NOSUBSTRING`, not `UNAVAILABLE` |\n| `n <= top_bracket` but `n >= oveccount` | `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE` (-54) |\n| `rc == 0` (ovector too small) | Non-DFA: no effect at all — the three non-DFA checks don't consult `count`. Groups `< oveccount` are readable |\n| **partial match**, `n == 0` | `count := 0`; `0 <= top_bracket`; `0 < oveccount`; `ovector[0]` set by `pcre2_match.c:8228` → returns `0`, size = `end_subject - match_partial` (length of the partial fragment) |\n| **partial match**, `n > 0` | `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (-2) |\n| `rc < 0` other (`NOMATCH`, `MATCHLIMIT`, …) | that code, verbatim |\n| **DFA** match, `n < oveccount && (count==0 \\|\\| n < count)` | `0` — **no `top_bracket` check at all**, so numbers beyond the pattern's group count are accepted (DFA pairs are alternative match lengths, not captures) |\n| **DFA**, `n >= oveccount` | `UNAVAILABLE` |\n| **DFA**, `count != 0 && n >= count` | `UNSET` |\n| **DFA**, `count == 0` (ovector too small, `pcre2_dfa_match.c:880-883`) | any `n < oveccount` accepted |\n| `\\K` producing `left > right` | `0` with `*sizeptr = 0` (350) |\n| `sizeptr == NULL` | Valid: pure existence/set probe, returns `0` |\n| `left/right > subject_length` | `PCRE2_ERROR_INVALIDOFFSET` (-67), documented internal-error-only |\n| `matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_JIT` | Treated identically to `INTERPRETER` |\n\n## B.2 `pcre2_substring_copy_bynumber` (116-130)\n1. `rc = length_bynumber(md, n, &size)`; `rc < 0` → return it (all of B.1's codes).\n2. `if (size + 1 > *sizeptr) return PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY;` (124) — the buffer must hold `size` units **plus** the NUL.\n3. `if (size != 0) memcpy(buffer, subject + ovector[n*2], CU2BYTES(size));` (125-126) — guarded so `PCRE2_UNSET` is never added to `subject`.\n4. `buffer[size] = 0; *sizeptr = size; return 0;` (127-129).\n\n| Config | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `*sizeptr == size + 1` (exactly enough) | `0`, `*sizeptr = size`, `buffer[size]==0` |\n| `*sizeptr == size` (one too small) | `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (-48); **`*sizeptr` is NOT updated** (unlike `pcre2_substitute`, this gives no size hint) |\n| `*sizeptr > size + 1` | `0`; bytes past `buffer[size]` untouched |\n| `size == 0` (zero-length substring) | Needs `*sizeptr >= 1`; `memcpy` skipped, `buffer[0]=0`, `*sizeptr=0` |\n| `*sizeptr == 0` | Always `NOMEMORY` (since `size+1 >= 1 > 0`) |\n| No DFA guard here | A DFA match_data reaches B.1's DFA branch and can succeed |\n\n## B.3 `pcre2_substring_get_bynumber` (204-223)\n1. `length_bynumber` → propagate `rc < 0`.\n2. `yield = PRIV(memctl_malloc)(sizeof(pcre2_memctl) + (size + 1) * PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH, (pcre2_memctl *)match_data)` (213-214) — note this uses `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH` (= 8 in 8-bit mode), **not** `CU2BYTES`, so it over-allocates by 8×. Upstream behaviour; a faithful translation only needs to not under-allocate. `NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`.\n3. `yield += sizeof(pcre2_memctl)`; `if (size != 0) memcpy(...)`; `yield[size] = 0`; `*stringptr = yield`; `*sizeptr = size`; return 0.\nNo DFA guard. Zero-length substring → a 1-unit `\"\"`. Must be released with `pcre2_substring_free`.\n\n## B.4 `pcre2_substring_free` (236-244)\n`string == NULL` → no-op. Else `memctl = (pcre2_memctl *)((char *)string - sizeof(pcre2_memctl)); memctl->free(memctl, memctl->memory_data)`. Passing anything not produced by `get_byname`/`get_bynumber` is UB.\n\n## B.5 `pcre2_substring_copy_byname` (68-91) / `get_byname` (156-179) / `length_byname` (263-286)\nStructurally identical (only the delegate differs):\n1. **`matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC` (-41)** (74/162/269) — checked **first**, before the name even exists.\n2. `entrysize = pcre2_substring_nametable_scan(match_data->code, stringname, &first, &last)`; `< 0` → return it (`NOSUBSTRING`).\n3. `failrc = PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE`.\n4. `for (entry = first; entry <= last; entry += entrysize)`: `n = GET2(entry, 0)`; `if (n < match_data->oveccount) { if (ovector[n*2] != PCRE2_UNSET) return <delegate>(md, n, …); failrc = PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET; }`.\n5. `return failrc`.\n\n| DUPNAMES configuration | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Unique name, group set | delegate on that number |\n| Unique name, group unset, `n < oveccount` | `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` (-55) |\n| Unique name, `n >= oveccount` | `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE` (-54) — the loop body is skipped entirely |\n| Name absent from nametable | `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING` (-49) from `nametable_scan` |\n| Duplicates, ≥1 set | delegate on the **first set** one, scanning `first→last`. Nametable order for equal names = **order of appearance in the pattern**, which is ascending group number unless `(?\\|` is used (`pcre2_compile_cgroup.c:146-156`) |\n| Duplicates, all in ovector but all unset | `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` |\n| Duplicates, **all** `n >= oveccount` | `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE` |\n| Duplicates, mix: some `n >= oveccount`, the rest unset | `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` (`failrc` is upgraded by any in-range entry) |\n| Partial match | Not short-circuited here; the delegate returns `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` for `n > 0`, or succeeds for `n == 0` |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` | **Never produced** by the `*_byname` functions — they pass non-NULL `firstptr`/`lastptr`, so duplicates are enumerated rather than rejected |\n\nNote the asymmetry with `pcre2_substitute`'s own name resolution (1367-1398): substitute continues past a set entry only via `break`, but if **no** entry is in the ovector it falls back to `group = GET2(first,0)` and then calls `length_bynumber`, which yields `UNAVAILABLE` — the same code, by a different route.\n\n## B.6 `pcre2_substring_nametable_scan` (485-526)\n```\nbot = 0; top = code->name_count; entrysize = code->name_entry_size;   /* all uint16_t */\nnametable = (PCRE2_SPTR)((const char *)code + sizeof(pcre2_real_code));\nwhile (top > bot) {\n  mid = (top + bot) / 2;  entry = nametable + entrysize*mid;\n  c = PRIV(strcmp)(stringname, entry + IMM2_SIZE);       /* IMM2_SIZE == 2 */\n  if (c == 0) {\n    lastentry = nametable + entrysize*(name_count - 1);\n    first = last = entry;\n    while (first > nametable  && strcmp(name, first-entrysize+IMM2_SIZE)==0) first -= entrysize;\n    while (last  < lastentry  && strcmp(name, last +entrysize+IMM2_SIZE)==0) last  += entrysize;\n    if (firstptr == NULL) return (first == last)? (int)GET2(entry,0) : PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING;\n    *firstptr = first; *lastptr = last; return entrysize;\n  }\n  if (c > 0) bot = mid + 1; else top = mid;\n}\nreturn PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING;\n```\n| Config | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `name_count == 0` (no named groups) | loop never entered → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING` (-49) |\n| Name not present | `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING` |\n| Present, unique, `firstptr != NULL` | `entrysize` (> 0), `*firstptr == *lastptr` |\n| Present, `k` duplicates, `firstptr != NULL` | `entrysize`; `(*lastptr - *firstptr)/entrysize + 1 == k`; numbers read with `GET2(entry, 0)` |\n| Present, unique, `firstptr == NULL` | the group number (`GET2(entry,0)`, ≥ 1) |\n| Present, duplicated, `firstptr == NULL` | `PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` (-50) |\n| `firstptr == NULL, lastptr != NULL` | only `firstptr` is tested (516) — `lastptr` is never written |\n| Name is a proper prefix of a table entry | `PRIV(strcmp)` is NUL-terminated, so `\"ab\"` vs entry `\"abc\"` compares unequal; correct chop |\n| `name_entry_size` | `max(namelen) + IMM2_SIZE + 1` over all names (`pcre2_compile.c:5715-5716`) |\n| Return type | `int`, and `entrysize` is `uint16_t`, so the \"length of each entry\" return is always positive and distinguishable from the error codes |\n\n## B.7 `pcre2_substring_number_from_name` (546-551)\nExactly `return pcre2_substring_nametable_scan(code, stringname, NULL, NULL);`. No match_data involved, no DFA check. Valid configs: unique name → number; duplicate name → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING`; absent / `name_count==0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING`.\n\n## B.8 `pcre2_substring_list_get` (377-437)\n```\nif ((count = match_data->rc) < 0) return count;      /* 389 */\nif (count == 0) count = match_data->oveccount;       /* 390 */\ncount2 = 2*count;  ovector = match_data->ovector;\nsize = sizeof(pcre2_memctl) + sizeof(PCRE2_UCHAR *);              /* final NULL   394 */\nif (lengthsptr != NULL) size += sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE) * count;       /* 395 */\nfor (i = 0; i < count2; i += 2) {                                 /* 397-401 */\n  size += sizeof(PCRE2_UCHAR *) + CU2BYTES(1);\n  if (ovector[i+1] > ovector[i]) size += CU2BYTES(ovector[i+1] - ovector[i]); }\nmemp = memctl_malloc(size, (pcre2_memctl *)match_data);            /* 403-404, NULL → NOMEMORY */\n*listptr = listp = (PCRE2_UCHAR **)((char *)memp + sizeof(pcre2_memctl));\nlensp = (PCRE2_SIZE *)((char *)listp + sizeof(PCRE2_UCHAR *) * (count + 1));\nif (lengthsptr == NULL) { sp = (PCRE2_UCHAR *)lensp; lensp = NULL; }\nelse { *lengthsptr = lensp; sp = (PCRE2_UCHAR *)((char *)lensp + sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)*count); }\nfor (i = 0; i < count2; i += 2) {                                 /* 420-433 */\n  size = (ovector[i+1] > ovector[i])? ovector[i+1]-ovector[i] : 0;\n  if (size != 0) memcpy(sp, match_data->subject + ovector[i], CU2BYTES(size));\n  *listp++ = sp; if (lensp != NULL) *lensp++ = size; sp += size; *sp++ = 0; }\n*listp = NULL; return 0;\n```\n| Config | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `rc < 0` (`NOMATCH`, **`PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`**, any error) | returned verbatim; nothing allocated. There is **no** partial-match special case |\n| `rc == n > 0` | exactly `n` pointers + a terminating NULL pointer; `lengths[0..n-1]` |\n| `rc == 0` (ovector too small) | `count = oveccount`; all `oveccount` pairs are emitted (they are all filled in this case) |\n| \"0 pairs\" | **Not reachable** — `pcre2_match_data_create` clamps `oveccount` to `[1, UINT16_MAX]` (`pcre2_match_data.c:57-58`), and `rc==0` maps to `oveccount >= 1`; `rc>0` implies `>= 1`. Minimum output is 1 entry + NULL |\n| Many pairs | Single allocation; strings laid out contiguously after the pointer (and optional lengths) array, each NUL-terminated |\n| Gap / trailing **unset** group inside `0..count-1` | `ovector[i+1] > ovector[i]` is FALSE for `UNSET/UNSET`, so `size = 0`; `memcpy` skipped (guard at 428, comment 424-426 — avoids `subject + PCRE2_UNSET` overflow); entry is a valid pointer to `\"\"` with length 0. **Unset and genuinely-empty groups are indistinguishable** in the output |\n| Trailing groups beyond `rc` | Not emitted at all (list has exactly `count` entries) |\n| `\\K` giving `ovector[i] > ovector[i+1]` | `size = 0`, empty string |\n| `lengthsptr == NULL` | No lengths array allocated (395 skipped); `*lengthsptr` untouched; binary data is then unrecoverable |\n| `lengthsptr != NULL` | `*lengthsptr` = array of exactly `count` `PCRE2_SIZE` values |\n| DFA match_data | **No DFA guard.** Works, but the \"captures\" are the DFA's alternative match lengths for group 0 |\n| `match_data->subject == NULL` with all sizes 0 | Safe (memcpy guarded) |\n| Allocation failure | `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (-48); `*listptr`/`*lengthsptr` untouched |\n| `int count` | Bounded by `UINT16_MAX`, so `count2 = 2*count` cannot overflow |\n\n## B.9 `pcre2_substring_list_free` (450-458)\n`list == NULL` → no-op. Else `memctl = (pcre2_memctl *)((char *)list - sizeof(pcre2_memctl)); memctl->free(memctl, memctl->memory_data)`. Must be the exact `*listptr` returned by `list_get` (never `*lengthsptr`).\n\n---\n\n# Quick reference: full error inventory for `pcre2_substitute`\n\n| Code | Value | Site(s) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` | -34 | 797 (`partial` without `REPLACEMENT_ONLY`) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` | -51 | 804, 815, 827 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` | -48 | 895, 909 (match_data alloc); 1750 (`overflowed`); 1772 (`NOROOM`) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC` | -41 | 850 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSPATTERN` / `SUBJECT` / `OFFSET` / `OPTIONS` | -71/-72/-73/-74 | 853 / 864 / 867 / 871 |\n| UTF-validity codes | various | 940-945 (replacement); via 996 (subject) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` | -33 | 959 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSPATTERN` | -60 | 1003 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL_DUPMATCH` | -65 | 1021 (debug-unreachable) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOMANYREPLACE` | -61 | 1034 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` | -76 | 1155 (`$'`), 1172 (`$_`) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING` | -49 | 1193 (`$+`, no groups), 1265 (`$nn > top_bracket`), 1412 via `length_bynumber` |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE` | -54 | 1204 (`$+` short ovector), 1412 via `length_bynumber` |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` | -55 | 1213 (`$+`), 1416 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSTITUTION` | -59 | 1296 (`${n:` not followed by `+`/`-`) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE` | -58 | 1318; `find_text_end`:175 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPLACEMENT` | -35 | `BAD` 1783: 1110, 1221, 1230, 1237, 1276, 1329, 1353, 1433 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE` | -57 | `BADESCAPE` 1787: 1545, 1585, 1590, 1594, 1611; `find_text_end`:137, 169 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` | -50 | 1378 (propagated from `nametable_scan` — cannot occur here, `firstptr` is non-NULL) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE` | -69 | `CASEERROR` 1775, from `CHECKCASECPY_CALLOUT`:708 (user callout returned `PCRE2_SIZE_MAX`) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOLARGEREPLACE` | -70 | 1779: `CHECKMEMCPY`:644, `CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT`:696, `DELAYEDFORCECASE`:724, 1702, 1753 |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` | -2 | via 996 / 846 |"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence