gates the fixup pass (`11012`).\n\n**Script runs**: `(*sr:…)`⇒`META_SCRIPT_RUN`⇒`OP_SCRIPT_RUN` (`6903`); `(*asr:…)` ⇒ `META_SCRIPT_RUN` + `META_ATOMIC` + `NSF_ATOMICSR` (`4844-4870`) ⇒ two `META_KET`s at `5847-5855`; `(*script_run:…)`, `(*atomic_script_run:…)`.\n\n**Verbs** (`527-556`, `4881-4972`)\nAccepted names: `` (empty ⇒ MARK, requires arg), `MARK`(+1), `ACCEPT`(-1), `F`(-1), `FAIL`(-1), `COMMIT`(0), `PRUNE`(0), `SKIP`(0), `THEN`(0).\n- `has_arg > 0` ⇒ `:` mandatory else ERR66; `has_arg < 0` ⇒ optional arg becomes a preceding `META_MARK` + `add_after_mark` (`4947-4951`); `has_arg == 0` with arg ⇒ `verbs[i].meta + 0x00010000` (`_ARG` variant, `4958-4959`).\n- Empty arg `(*MARK:)` ⇒ treated as no arg (`4911-4913`) ⇒ ERR66 for MARK.\n- `(*ACCEPT)`: `6488-6506` closes open captures with `OP_CLOSE`, uses `OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT` when `cb->assert_depth > 0`, sets `cb->had_accept` ⇒ `10977-10982` `reqcu = 0; reqcuflags = REQ_NONE; re->flags |= PCRE2_HASACCEPT`.\n- `(*PRUNE)`/`(*SKIP)` set `cb->had_pruneorskip` ⇒ disable `.*` anchoring (`8958`, `9089`).\n- `(*THEN)` sets `PCRE2_HASTHEN` (`6518`, `6530`).\n- Arg length limited by `MAX_MARK`=255 (`3364-3369`, ERR76).\n- Tests: `(*MARK:x)`, `(*:x)`, `(*ACCEPT)`, `(*ACCEPT:x)`, `(*F)`, `(*FAIL)`, `(*FAIL:x)`, `(*COMMIT)`, `(*COMMIT:x)`, `(*PRUNE)`, `(*PRUNE:x)`, `(*SKIP)`, `(*SKIP:x)`, `(*THEN)`, `(*THEN:x)`, `(a)(*ACCEPT)`, `(?=(*ACCEPT))`, 255-char and 256-char MARK args.\n\n**Callouts** (`5287-5406`, `7201-7276`)\n- `(?C)` ⇒ number 0; `(?C1)`…`(?C255)`; `(?C256)`⇒ERR38.\n- String form delimiters (`pcre2_tables.c:84-93`): start ``` ` ``` `'` `\"` `^` `%` `#` `$` `{`; ends are the same except `{`→`}`. Doubled delimiter escapes it (`5357`).\n- Tests: `(?C)`, `(?C0)`, `(?C255)`, ``(?C`s`)``, `(?C's')`, `(?C\"s\")`, `(?C^s^)`, `(?C%s%)`, `(?C#s#)`, `(?C$s$)`, `(?C{s})`, `(?C\"a\"\"b\")` (doubled), `(?C1)(?C2)a`, `a(?C1)` +AUTO_CALLOUT, `(?(?C1)(?=a)b|c)`.\n- `META_CALLOUT_STRING` two-pass length: `7221 *lengthptr += pptr[3] + (1 + 4*LINK_SIZE)`.\n\n**Escapes to cover as distinct compile paths**\n`\\X` (`3684`, needs SUPPORT_UNICODE), `\\R`, `\\N`, `\\C` (`3658-3670`, `8360-8368`), `\\Q…\\E` (`3428-3441`, `3295-3316`, in-class `3975-3998`, `4536-4541`), lone `\\E`, `\\Q\\E` empty in a condition (`3432-3438`), `\\K` (`8338-8343`, `8381-8383`), `\\b \\B \\A \\Z \\z \\G` (`3705`, non-quantifiable), `\\h \\H \\v \\V` (`3690`, `4508-4513`), `\\d \\D \\s \\S \\w \\W` (`3697-3703`, `4519-4529`), `\\p{L} \\P{L} \\p{^L} \\p{Any} \\P{Any} \\p{Lu}` (`3711-3730`, `4531-4568`), `\\p{sc:Latin}` / `\\p{scx:Latin}` / `\\p{Script=Latin}` / `\\p{Script_Extensions=Latin}` / `\\p{bc=AL}` / `\\p{bidiclass=AL}` (`2372-2406`, `PT_SC`/`PT_SCX`/`bidi` prefix), single-letter `\\pL`, `\\p{ l _ }` (loose matching `2295-2300`), `\\o{101}`, `\\o{ 101 }`, `\\x{41}`, `\\x{ 41 }`, `\\x41`, `\\x4`, `\\101`, `\\0`, `\\00`, `\\000`, `\\08`, `\\cA`, `\\c[`, `\\c?`(⇒0x7f), `\\a \\e \\f \\n \\r \\t`, `\\$ \\\\ \\. \\[` (non-alphanumeric literals, `1517`), `\\u`/`\\U` under ALT_BSUX / EXTRA_ALT_BSUX.\n\n**Two-pass growth**\n- `parsed_pattern` heap allocation: `10746-10756` `if (parsed_size_needed > PARSED_PATTERN_DEFAULT_SIZE (1024))` ⇒ malloc. Trigger with a >1024-char pattern, or a ~260-char pattern + `PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT` (×5 factor from `3008`+`10741`), or a 1021-char pattern + `EXTRA_MATCH_WORD` (+4). Also test right at the boundary (1024 / 1025).\n- `groupinfo` heap allocation: `10777-10787` `if (cb.bracount >= GROUPINFO_DEFAULT_SIZE/2 (128))` **and** `has_lookbehind` ⇒ malloc `2*(bracount+1)` uint32. Trigger: 128+ capture groups plus any lookbehind.\n- Workspace overrun guards: `6167-6182` `code >= cb.start_workspace + workspace_size` (ERR52, unreachable) and `code > … - WORK_SIZE_SAFETY_MARGIN` ⇒ **ERR86 \"pattern too complicated\"** — trigger with a deeply nested group chain near 250 parens plus long content.\n- `nest_save` stack overflow: `4998`/`5667` `++top_nest >= end_nests` ⇒ ERR84 — `end_nests` computed at `3204-3210` from `workspace_size`; with 6000 code units / `sizeof(nest_save)`(16) ≈ 375 entries, but `parens_nest_limit` 250 caps it first; test with `pcre2_set_parens_nest_limit(60000)` and >375 nested option-groups `(?i:(?i:…))`.\n- `MAX_PATTERN_SIZE` overflow: `6205` and `10840-10849` ⇒ ERR20; trigger with `x{65535}` repeated, or `(?:aaaa…){60000}`.\n- `char_lists_size` accounting: `pcre2_compile_class.c:1762-1773` ERR20 for very large XCLASS char-list sets.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Auto-possessification and study\n\n**Order at end of compile:** (1) `11012-11067` recursion offset fixup; (2) `11084-11096` `PRIV(auto_possessify)` if `PCRE2_OPTIM_AUTO_POSSESS`; (3) `11108-11113` `is_anchored` ⇒ `PCRE2_ANCHORED`; (4) `11122-11270` start-optimize block: `find_firstassertedcu`, firstcu/`PCRE2_FIRSTSET`/`PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS`, `is_startline`⇒`PCRE2_STARTLINE`, reqcu/`PCRE2_LASTSET`/`PCRE2_LASTCASELESS`, `PRIV(study)`, `minlength` floor.\n\n**`_pcre2_study(re)`** (`pcre2_study.c:1914-2084`) computes:\n- **start_bitmap / `PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET`**: only if `(re->flags & (PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_STARTLINE)) == 0` (`1930`). `set_start_bits` (`1092-1890`) returns `SSB_DONE`/`SSB_CONTINUE`/`SSB_FAIL`/`SSB_TOODEEP`(depth>1000, `1106`)/`SSB_UNKNOWN`. Bitmap only kept on `SSB_DONE` (`1950`). Then the 1-or-2-bit collapse (`1958-2038`) may convert the bitmap into `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` (+`PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS` if two case-partner bits) and clear `PCRE2_LASTSET` when it collides (`2031-2034`).\n  - `FIRSTBITMAP` non-NULL: `[abc]x`, `\\d`, `a|b|c` (3+ distinct first units), `\\w+`, `[^\\n]` (`1735-1783` class handling), `\\p{L}`+UTF via `study_char_list` (`1755`), UTF lead-byte bits (`1805-1806`).\n  - `FIRSTBITMAP` NULL: `abc` (FIRSTSET), `^a`+MULTILINE (STARTLINE), `.a` non-DOTALL (SSB_FAIL at `1720`), `\\C`, `(?R)`, `+NO_START_OPTIMIZE`.\n  - two-bit collapse ⇒ FIRSTSET+FIRSTCASELESS: `[Ww]ord`, `(word|WORD)`, `[aA]`. Verify the `UCD_CASESET(c) != 0 ⇒ goto DONE` guard (`2001`) with `[Kk]`+UCP.\n- **firstcu / firstcuflags / `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` / `PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS`** — set in `pcre2_compile.c:11148-11178` from the value threaded through `compile_branch`/`compile_regex`; caseless flag via `cb.fcc[firstcu] != firstcu` (`11160`) or `UCD_OTHERCASE` (`11169`).\n- **`find_firstassertedcu`** (`9280-9363`), used only when `firstcuflags >= REQ_NONE` (`11131`), and only adopted `if (assertedcuflags < REQ_NONE && assertedcu != reqcu)` (`11139`). Tests: `(?=abcde).+` (adopts 'a'), `(?=a)b?a` (must **not** adopt — `assertedcu == reqcu`), `(?=a)a.+`, `(?=abc)(?=abd)` (agreeing branches), `(?=abc)(?=xbc)` (disagree ⇒ 0).\n- **reqcu / `PCRE2_LASTSET` / `PCRE2_LASTCASELESS`** (`11198-11244`), incl. the 8-bit UTF minminlength guard `11206-11209`: `(overall_options & PCRE2_UTF)==0 || firstcuflags >= REQ_NONE || (firstcu & 0x80)==0 || (reqcu & 0x80)==0`.\n- **minlength** (`2053-2081`): computed only if `(re->flags & (PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY|PCRE2_HASACCEPT)) == 0 && re->top_backref <= 128`. `find_minlength` returns -1 for `\\C` in UTF / over-complex. Floor applied at `11269`: `if (re->minlength < minminlength) re->minlength = minminlength;` where `minminlength` = (firstcu?1:0) + (reqcu?1:0) (+1 if FIRSTMAPSET and 0, `11263-11264`). Capped at `UINT16_MAX`.\n  Tests: `abc`(3), `a*`(0 + MATCH_EMPTY), `(*ACCEPT)a`(0), `\\1{200}` with 200 groups (top_backref>128 ⇒ 0), `\\C`+UTF(→minminlength only), `(?R)`, `a{2,4}b`(3).\n- **maxlookbehind** = `cb.max_lookbehind` (`10975`), from `set_lookbehind_lengths` (`10047`) and `8378`.\n- **hascrorlf** = `PCRE2_HASCRORLF` in `re->flags`, set at `8474-8475` (literal `\\r`/`\\n`) and `pcre2_compile_class.c:1491,1508` (class member or range endpoint). Tests: `a\\rb`, `a\\nb`, `[\\r]`, `[\\x00-\\x0d]`, `\\x0d` (⇒ set — it goes through the literal path), `\\R` (⇒ not set), `\\r`+EXTRA_ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF (⇒ set, via LF).\n- **matchempty** = `PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY`, from `10972: if (regexrc < 0) re->flags |= PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY;` where `regexrc` is the `compile_regex` return (`-1` = may match empty, `+1` = must match ≥1 char, propagated at `8702: if (branch_return < 0) okreturn = -1;` and `6228: if (matched_char && !had_accept) okreturn = 1;`). Tests: ``(empty)``, `a*`, `a?`, `(?:)`, `(?=a)`, `\\b`, `^`, `(a){0}`, `(?(DEFINE)(a))` (DEFINE goes to `GROUP_PROCESS` not `..._NOTE_EMPTY`, `6798-6803`), `a`, `a+`, `[a]`, `(a|b)`.\n\n**`PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODETYPE` values** (`pcre2_pattern_info.c:149-151`): `1` if `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` (`abc`, `[Ww]ord`, `(?=abcde).+`); `2` if `PCRE2_STARTLINE` (`(?m)^a`, `^a`+MULTILINE, `.*a` non-DOTALL non-anchored — but note `.*a` also yields firstcu? no, `META_DOT` sets `firstcuflags = REQ_NONE` at `6276`); `0` otherwise (`\\da`, `[abc]x`, `.a`, `abc`+NO_START_OPTIMIZE, `^a` without MULTILINE ⇒ ANCHORED, no firstcu, STARTLINE gate fails at `11186`).\n**`LASTCODETYPE`** (`:195`): `1` iff `PCRE2_LASTSET` — `abc` (reqcu 'c'), `a.*b`; `0` — `a`, `abc`+ANCHORED (no REQ_VARY), `a*`, `(*ACCEPT)ab`, `[Ww]ord` if the study collapse cleared it (`2031-2034`).\n**`FIRSTBITMAP`** (`:159`): non-NULL iff `PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET`.\n\n---\n\n# 7. `_pcre2_check_escape` — full API and escape classes\n\n```c\nint PRIV(check_escape)(PCRE2_SPTR *ptrptr, PCRE2_SPTR ptrend, uint32_t *chptr,\n  int *errorcodeptr, uint32_t options, uint32_t xoptions, uint32_t bracount,\n  BOOL isclass, compile_block *cb);          /* pcre2_compile.c:1489-1492 */\n```\nEntry: `ptr` points *after* the `\\`. Exit: `*ptrptr` after the last code unit consumed (`EXIT:` at `2218`; `ESCAPE_FAILED_FORWARD:` at `2225` advances one char, plus `FORWARDCHARTEST` in UTF, for better error offsets).\n\n**Returns**\n- `0` ⇒ data character in `*chptr`.\n- `> 0` ⇒ one of `ESC_A=1, ESC_G, ESC_K, ESC_B, ESC_b, ESC_D, ESC_d, ESC_S, ESC_s, ESC_W, ESC_w, ESC_N, ESC_dum, ESC_C, ESC_P, ESC_p, ESC_R, ESC_H, ESC_h, ESC_V, ESC_v, ESC_X, ESC_Z, ESC_z, ESC_E, ESC_Q, ESC_g, ESC_k, ESC_ub` (`pcre2_internal.h:1607-1610`).\n- `< 0` ⇒ back reference to group `n` encoded as `-(n+1)`.\n- `*errorcodeptr` non-zero on error (and `escape`/`c` are then unreliable).\n\n**Dispatch** (`1517-1526`): `c < ESCAPES_FIRST(CHAR_0) || c > ESCAPES_LAST(CHAR_z)` ⇒ literal; else `i = escapes[c - ESCAPES_FIRST]`; `i > 0` ⇒ literal value `i`; `i < 0` ⇒ `escape = -i`; `i == 0` ⇒ the big `switch` at `1627`.\n\nTable (`379-419`): letters mapping to negative `ESC_*`: `A B C D E G H K N P Q R S V W X Z b d h k p s v w z`; positive literal values: `a`→BEL, `e`→ESC, `f`→FF, `n`→LF, `r`→CR, `t`→HT, plus punctuation `: ; < = > ? @ [ \\ ] ^ _ \\``. Zero (⇒ switch): `0-9 F I J L M O T U c g i j l m o q u x y`.\n\n`cb != NULL` side effects: `1546-1547` `if (escape == ESC_P || escape == ESC_p || escape == ESC_X) cb->external_flags |= PCRE2_HASBKPORX;`\n\n**`cb == NULL` (substitute) filter** (`1637-1646`): only digits, `c`, `o`, `x`, `g` allowed (else ERR3); `alt_bsux = FALSE` forced. `\\g<n>` returns `-(n+1)`; `\\g<name>` returns `ESC_g`.\n\n**Distinct escape classes and their option dependencies**\n\n| class | site | option dependence |\n|---|---|---|\n| non-alphanumeric literal (`\\.`, `\\\\`, `\\$`, `\\@`, `\\_`, …) | `1517` | none |\n| table literal `\\a \\e \\f \\n \\t` | `1527-1528` | none |\n| `\\r` | `1529-1531` | `EXTRA_ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF` ⇒ LF |\n| simple `ESC_*`: `\\A \\B \\b \\D \\d \\G \\H \\h \\K \\P \\p \\R \\S \\s \\V \\v \\W \\w \\X \\Z \\z \\C \\E \\Q` | `1534-1536` | `\\C` later gated by `PCRE2_NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` (in caller, `3664`) and by UTF-in-lookbehind (`9698`) |\n| `\\N` bare | `1534` | none |\n| `\\N{U+dddd}` | `1550-1578` | requires `PCRE2_UTF` and `!EBCDIC` (`1562-1567`) ⇒ jumps into `\\x{` code (`COME_FROM_NU`, `2054`); otherwise ERR93. In a class or `cb==NULL` ⇒ ERR37 (`1585-1589`) |\n| `\\N{2,3}` quantifier probe | `1594-1601` | not allowed in class / substitute (ERR37) |\n| `\\F \\l \\L` | `1631-1635` | always ERR37 |\n| `\\u` | `1649-1710` | `!alt_bsux` ⇒ ERR37. `EXTRA_ALT_BSUX` ⇒ braced form (`1656`), no-digit brace ⇒ `ESC_ub` unless `isclass` (then literal `u`). Else