{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ac53049c975232076","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012wNUABvdNNtP5U1rcbNPFT","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-tBNRGp-translated-rust/cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7/tasks/ac53049c975232076.output","summary":"# Configuration‑Surface Analysis (8‑bit, SUPPORT_UNICODE on, SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS on, no JIT, LINK_SIZE=2)\n\nActive preprocessor state for all six files (verified at `c_src/src/pcre2_intmodedep.h:232-249, 282-283`):\n`PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH==8`, `SUPPORT_UNICODE` defined ⇒ `SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS` defined, `MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` defined, `MAX_255(c)==TRUE`, `TABLE_GET(c,t,d)==t[c]`, `XCL_LIST==0x10`, `IMM2_SIZE==2`, `LINK_SIZE==2`, `GET/PUT` are 2‑byte. All `#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH != 8` / `== 16` / `== 32` blocks are **dead**; all `#ifdef SUPPORT_UNICODE` / `SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS` blocks are **live**; `#ifdef EBCDIC` dead.\n\n---\n\n# 1. `pcre2_pattern_convert` option surface — `pcre2_convert.c:1116-1237`\n\n## 1.1 Constants (`include/pcre2.h:201-207`)\n| Option | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF` | `0x01` |\n| `PCRE2_CONVERT_NO_UTF_CHECK` | `0x02` |\n| `PCRE2_CONVERT_POSIX_BASIC` | `0x04` |\n| `PCRE2_CONVERT_POSIX_EXTENDED` | `0x08` |\n| `PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB` | `0x10` |\n| `PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` | `0x30` (= `0x20 | GLOB`) |\n| `PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB_NO_STARSTAR` | `0x50` (= `0x40 | GLOB`) |\n\nDerived (`pcre2_convert.c:46-52`): `TYPE_OPTIONS = 0x1c`; `ALL_OPTIONS = 0x7f`.\n\n## 1.2 Validation order (mechanical)\n1. `:1129` `pattern==NULL && plength==0` ⇒ `pattern = null_str` (`{0xcd}`), i.e. **NULL + length 0 is legal**.\n2. `:1132` `pattern==NULL || bufflenptr==NULL` ⇒ `*bufflenptr=0` (only if non‑NULL), return `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`.\n3. `:1138-1144` `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` + `*bufflenptr=0` if **any** of:\n   * `(options & ~0x7f) != 0` (any bit ≥ `0x80`)\n   * `pattype & (~pattype+1) != pattype` (more than one bit of `0x1c` set)\n   * `pattype == 0`\n4. `:1146` `plength == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` (`~(PCRE2_SIZE)0`) ⇒ `plength = strlen(pattern)` — stops at first NUL.\n5. `:1147` `ccontext==NULL` ⇒ `PRIV(default_convert_context)`.\n6. `:1159-1168` if `PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF` **and not** `PCRE2_CONVERT_NO_UTF_CHECK`: `PRIV(valid_utf)`; on failure `*bufflenptr = erroroffset`, return the UTF error code (`PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR1..21`).\n\n## 1.3 Exhaustive VALID option matrix\nLegal set = **exactly one** type bit from `{0x04, 0x08, 0x10}` (after masking with `0x1c`) ∪ **any subset** of `{0x01, 0x02, 0x20, 0x40}`.\n\n| options | pattype | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `0x04` | BASIC | valid, `convert_posix(extended=FALSE)` |\n| `0x08` | EXTENDED | valid, `convert_posix(extended=TRUE)` |\n| `0x10` | GLOB | valid, `convert_glob(no_wildsep=F,no_starstar=F)` |\n| `0x30` (`GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR`) | GLOB | valid; `convert_glob` gets `0x20`; `no_wildsep=T`, `no_starstar=F` |\n| `0x50` (`GLOB_NO_STARSTAR`) | GLOB | valid; gets `0x40`; `no_wildsep=F`, `no_starstar=T` |\n| `0x70` (both glob mods) | GLOB | valid; gets `0x60`; `no_wildsep=T`, `no_starstar=T` |\n| any above `| 0x01` | — | valid + UTF (validity checked) |\n| any above `| 0x02` | — | valid, NO_UTF_CHECK; **legal without UTF** (bit simply unused) |\n| any above `| 0x03` | — | valid + UTF, check skipped (bad UTF then reaches converters) |\n| **`0x04|0x20`=0x24**, `0x04|0x40`=0x44, `0x04|0x60`=0x64 | BASIC | **valid**; glob‑mod bits are silently ignored by `convert_posix` |\n| same with `0x08` (`0x28/0x48/0x68`) | EXTENDED | **valid**, bits ignored |\n| `0x20` alone / `0x40` alone / `0x60` alone | 0 | `BADOPTION` (no type bit) |\n| `0x0c`, `0x14`, `0x18`, `0x1c`, `0x34` (=`0x04|0x30`), `0x54` | multi | `BADOPTION` |\n| `0x00` | 0 | `BADOPTION` |\n| `0x80`, `0x100`, `0xffffffff` … | — | `BADOPTION` (undefined bit) |\n\nNote `pattype = options & 0x1c`, so `0x30` ⇒ `0x10` (single bit, OK) and `0x50` ⇒ `0x10` (OK), but `POSIX_BASIC|GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR = 0x34` ⇒ `0x14` (two bits) ⇒ `BADOPTION`.\n\n`:1191` glob is called with `options & ~PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB`, i.e. `0x20`/`0x40` survive; `no_wildsep = (opt & 0x30)!=0`, `no_starstar = (opt & 0x50)!=0` (`:857-858`).\n\n---\n\n# 2. Two‑pass length/output logic — `pcre2_convert.c:1121-1237`\n\n| `buffptr` | `*buffptr` | `dummyrun` (`:1186`) | passes | `use_buffer` / `use_length` | `*bufflenptr` in | `*bufflenptr` out |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `NULL` | — | TRUE | 1 (returns at `:1213` because `buffptr==NULL`) | `dummy_buffer[100]` / 100 | ignored | required length **excluding** terminating NUL |\n| non‑NULL | `NULL` | pass1 TRUE, pass2 FALSE | 2 | pass1 dummy 100; pass2 allocated / `len+1` | ignored | final length excl. NUL; `*buffptr` = malloc'd buffer |\n| non‑NULL | non‑NULL | FALSE | 1 | `*buffptr` / `*bufflenptr` | **buffer capacity in code units** | used length excl. NUL |\n\n* `DUMMY_BUFFER_SIZE = 100` (`:54`). In a dummy run `convert_posix` resets `p = use_buffer` before each item (`:186`), so only one item + the 6‑unit `(*NUL)` prefix must fit; `convert_glob` never writes past `output_end` (`:413`, `:437`) and only counts.\n* Allocation `:1218-1219`: `sizeof(pcre2_memctl) + (*bufflenptr+1)*PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH` — note it multiplies by **8** (the width in bits), i.e. an 8× over‑allocation in 8‑bit mode. Preserve as‑is.\n* `pcre2_converted_pattern_free` (`:1250-1259`): NULL‑safe; otherwise reads the `pcre2_memctl` immediately **before** the returned pointer and calls `memctl->free`. Must only be called on a buffer allocated by the 2‑pass path (not on a caller buffer).\n* Buffer‑too‑small behaviour differs per converter:\n  * POSIX: `endp = p + use_length - 1` (`:157`) reserves 1 unit for the NUL; overflow ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` from `PUTCHARS` (`:77`) or `:242/:309/:339/:370`. Note `*bufflenptr` is left at its `:171` value = **input `plength`**, i.e. the \"error offset\" is always the whole input length for POSIX errors.\n  * GLOB: never overflows; detects short buffer at `:1082-1083` `!dummyrun && out.output_size != (out.output - use_buffer)` ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, then `:1088` `*bufflenptr = pattern - pattern_start` (= `plength`, since the loop ran to the end).\n* Success: POSIX `*bufflenptr = convlength` (`:381`) then writes the NUL at `p` (so the buffer must hold `convlength+1`). GLOB `*bufflenptr = out.output_size - 1` (`:1092`), NUL counted in `output_size`.\n* Zero‑length pattern: POSIX ⇒ length 6, output `\"(*NUL)\"`. GLOB (default opts) ⇒ length 8, output `\"(?s)\\A\\z\"`.\n\n---\n\n# 3. `pcre2_set_glob_separator` / `pcre2_set_glob_escape` and glob output\n\n## 3.1 Setters — `pcre2_context.c:528-554`\n* `pcre2_set_glob_separator(ccontext, sep)`: accepts **only** `/` (0x2F), `\\` (0x5C), `.` (0x2E). Anything else ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA`, context unchanged.\n* `pcre2_set_glob_escape(ccontext, esc)`: accepts `0` (= no escaping) or any byte in `globpunct` (`:537-545`) = the 32 ASCII punctuation chars `! \" # $ % & ' ( ) * + , - . / : ; < = > ? @ [ \\ ] ^ _ \\` { | } ~`. Rejects `esc > 255` and any non‑punct (letters, digits, space, control) ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA`.\n* Defaults (`pcre2_context.c:199-208`): non‑Windows `separator='/'`, `escape='\\\\'`.\n\n## 3.2 Derived flags in `convert_glob` (`pcre2_convert.c:846-905`)\n* `:868-873` if `utf && (separator >= 128 || escape >= 128)` ⇒ `*bufflenptr = 0`, `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`. (Unreachable via the setters, reachable only by direct struct manipulation.)\n* `:876` `with_escape = strchr(pcre2_escaped_literals, separator) != NULL`. `pcre2_escaped_literals` = `\\ ? * + | . ^ $ { } [ ] ( )` (`:94-99`). ⇒ **`with_escape` is FALSE for `/`, TRUE for `\\` and `.`**.\n* Prologue: always `\"(?s)\"` (`:883-887`). Then `is_start` (`:889-905`):\n  * `is_start = TRUE` unless `pattern[0]=='*'` **and** (`no_wildsep`, **or** (`!no_starstar && plength>1 && pattern[1]=='*'`)).\n  * If `is_start` ⇒ emit `\"\\A\"`.\n\n## 3.3 Top‑level constructs (`:907-1066`)\nTop‑level reads are **byte‑wise** (`:909 c = *pattern++`) — not UTF aware.\n\n### `*` (`:911-1033`)\n`is_start` recomputed as `pattern == pattern_start+1` (`:913`). If `in_atomic`, emit `)` and clear (`:915-919`).\n\n**Branch A — `**` (only when `!no_starstar` and next char is `*`), `:921-988`:**\n* `after_separator = is_start || (pattern[-2] == separator)` (`:923`).\n* Consume all further `*` (`:925-926`).\n* If now at end ⇒ `no_slash_z = TRUE`, `break` (no `\\z` appended). e.g. `\"a/**\"` ⇒ `(?s)\\Aa/`.\n* `after_starstar = TRUE` (`:934`).\n* `:936-938` if `after_separator && escape!=0 && *pattern==escape && pattern[1]==separator` ⇒ skip the escape byte.\n* If `is_start`:\n  * `*pattern != separator` ⇒ `continue`, **emit nothing** (`\"**abc\"` ⇒ `(?s)abc\\z`).\n  * else emit `\"(?:\\A|\"` + `[\\\\]`sep + `\")\"`, consume the separator (`\"**/abc\"` ⇒ `(?s)(?:\\A|/)abc\\z`).\n* Else (not at start):\n  * emit `\"(*COMMIT)\"` (`:959`)\n  * if `!after_separator || *pattern != separator` ⇒ emit `\".*?\"`, continue.\n  * else emit `\"(?:.*?\"` + `[\\\\]`sep + `\")??\"`, consume separator (`\"a/**/b\"` ⇒ `(?s)\\Aa/(*COMMIT)(?:.*?/)??b\\z`).\n\n**Branch B — single `*` (or `**` when `no_starstar`), `:990-1032`:**\n* Collapse runs of `*` (`:990-994`).\n* `no_wildsep`: if at end ⇒ `no_slash_z=TRUE`, `break`; else if `is_start` ⇒ `continue` (emit nothing).\n* If `!is_start`: `after_starstar` ⇒ emit `\"(?>\"`, `in_atomic=TRUE`; else emit `\"(*COMMIT)\"`.\n* Emit `\".\"` if `no_wildsep`, else `\"[^\"` + `[\\\\]`sep + `\"]\"` (`convert_glob_print_wildcard`, `:474-485`).\n* Emit `\"*?\"`, or `\"*+\"` if now at end of pattern (`:1027-1031`).\n\nConcrete: default opts ⇒ `\"*\"`→`(?s)\\A[^/]*+\\z`; `\"*a\"`→`(?s)\\A[^/]*?a\\z`; `\"a*\"`→`(?s)\\Aa(*COMMIT)[^/]*+\\z`. `no_wildsep`: `\"*\"`→`(?s)` (nothing else!); `\"*a\"`→`(?s).a…` — precisely: `is_start` true ⇒ `continue` ⇒ `(?s)a\\z`. `no_starstar`: `\"**\"`→`(?s)\\A[^/]*+\\z`.\n\n### `?` (`:1035-1042`)\n`no_wildsep` ⇒ `\".\"`; else `\"[^\"`+`[\\\\]`sep+`\"]\"`. No `is_start` interaction.\n\n### `[...]` (`:1044-1050`) ⇒ `convert_glob_parse_range` (see 3.4).\n\n### escape byte (`:1052-1060`)\nIf `escape != 0 && c == escape`: at end ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` (`*bufflenptr = offset`); else `c = *pattern++` and the char falls through to the literal path (so it is emitted with a `\\` if it is a PCRE2 metachar).\n\n### literal (`:1062-1065`)\n`if (c < 255 && strchr(pcre2_escaped_literals, c))` emit `\\`. **`c==0` matches `strchr`'s terminator ⇒ an embedded NUL is emitted as `\"\\<NUL>\"`.** `c==0xFF` fails `c<255` ⇒ emitted raw.\n\n### Epilogue (`:1068-1093`)\n`!no_slash_z` ⇒ `\"\\z\"`; `in_atomic` ⇒ `\")\"`; then `NUL`.\n\n## 3.4 `convert_glob_parse_range` — `pcre2_convert.c:636-804`\n* `:651-655` empty after `[` ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`.\n* `:657-685` leading `!` **or** `^` ⇒ negation: if nothing follows ⇒ `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`. Emits `\"[\"`,`\"^\"` then, **if `!no_wildsep`**, optional `\\` + separator; `convert_glob_write_str(out, len+1)`.\n  * **QUIRK (must be reproduced byte‑for‑byte):** when `no_wildsep` is set, `len` stays 2 but `len+1 = 3` bytes are written, so a **stale `out_str[2]`** is emitted. After the prologue `out_str` = `{'(','?','s',')'}` and, if `is_start`, `{'\\\\','A','s',')'}`. So `\"[!a]\"` with `GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` yields `(?s)\\A[^sa]\\z` (a spurious `s`). The stale byte depends on the last `convert_glob_write_str` before the class, so test several prefixes (`\"[!a]\"`, `\"*[!a]\"`, `\"?[!a]\"`, `\"a[!a]\"`).\n* `:686-687` non‑negated ⇒ emit just `\"[\"`.\n* `:692-700` a `]` as the very first class char ⇒ emit `\"\\]\"`, `has_prev_c=TRUE`, `prev_c=']'`. (`\"[]]\"`→`[\\]]`; `\"[!]]\"`→`[^/\\]]`.)\n* Main loop `:702-800` reads with `GETCHARINCTEST` ⇒ **UTF‑aware iff `PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF`**.\n  * `]` ⇒ emit `]`; then if `!is_negative && !no_wildsep && separator_seen` append `\"(?<!\"` + `[\\\\]`sep + `\")\"`; return 0.\n  * `[:name:]` (`:729-746`) ⇒ `convert_glob_parse_class` (`:499-551`): only lowercase a–z names, must be followed by `:]`; matched against `posix_classes` (`:110-124`) giving indices **1 alpha, 2 lower, 3 upper, 4 alnum, 5 ascii, 6 blank, 7 cntrl, 8 digit, 9 graph, 10 print, 11 punct, 12 space, 13 word, 14 xdigit**. On match the whole `[:name:]` is copied verbatim; `has_prev_c=FALSE`. If `!is_negative` and `convert_glob_char_in_class(idx, separator)` (`:563-621`, uses `PRIV(default_tables)+cbits_offset`) ⇒ `separator_seen=TRUE`. Unrecognized name ⇒ index 0 ⇒ falls through and `[` / `:` are treated as ordinary chars.\n  * `-` range (`:747-778`): requires `has_prev_c` and next char `!= ']'`. Emits `-`, reads the hi char; if at end ⇒ break ⇒ `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`. `escape` before the hi char is honoured (`:757-761`). `x-[:class:]` ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` (`:762-766`). `prev_c > c` ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` (`:768-772`). `prev_c < separator < c` ⇒ `separator_seen=TRUE`.\n  * plain char (`:779-791`): escape honoured (at end ⇒ break ⇒ `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`); `has_prev_c=TRUE`.\n  * `:793-795` `[`, `]`, `\\`, `-` are backslash‑escaped in the output. `:797` `c == separator` ⇒ `separator_seen`.\n  * Unterminated ⇒ `*from = pattern`, `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET` (`:802-803`).\n\n## 3.5 Separator/escape × output cross‑product to test\n| sep | with_escape | `?` (default) | `?` (no_wildsep) | `[!a]` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `/` | F | `[^/]` | `.` | `[^/a]` |\n| `.` | T | `[^\\.]` | `.` | `[^\\.a]` |\n| `\\` | T | `[^\\\\]` | `.` | `[^\\\\a]` |\n\n| escape | `\"a\\\\*b\"` (chars `a \\ * b`) | `\"\\\\\"` at end |\n|---|---|---|\n| `\\` (default) | `\\` consumed, `*` becomes literal ⇒ `a\\*b` | `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` |\n| `0` (none) | `\\` is a literal metachar ⇒ `\\\\` then wildcard for `*` | `\\\\` emitted, no error |\n| `` ` `` | `\\` is literal ⇒ `\\\\`, `*` still a wildcard | n/a |\n\nAlso test the `escape+separator` skip at `:936-938`: `\"**\\\\/x\"` with escape `\\` and sep `/`, and `\"/**\\\\/x\"`.\n\n---\n\n# 4. POSIX BASIC vs EXTENDED — `convert_posix`, `pcre2_convert.c:149-384`\n\nPrefix: always `\"(*NUL)\"` (`:172`, `STR_STAR_NUL` at `:64`).\nStates (`:68-69`): `POSIX_START_REGEX=0, POSIX_ANCHORED=1, POSIX_NOT_BRACKET=2, POSIX_CLASS_NOT_STARTED=3, POSIX_CLASS_STARTING=4, POSIX_CLASS_STARTED=5`.\n`extended = (pattype & PCRE2_CONVERT_POSIX_EXTENDED) != 0` (`:163`).\nChar read: `GETCHARLENTEST` (`:194`) ⇒ UTF‑aware iff `PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF`; `clength` 1–4.\n`sc = nextisliteral ? 0 : c` (`:199`) — `sc==0` forces the `default:` arm.\n\n## 4.1 Outside a class — per‑construct table\n| Input | BASIC (BR) output | EXTENDED (ER) output | Lines |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `\\` at end of pattern | `PCRE2_ERROR_END_BACKSLASH` | same | `:303` |\n| `\\(` | `(` , `lastspecial='('` | `\\(` (literal) | `:306-312` / `:304` |\n| `\\)` | `)` | `\\)` | same |\n| `\\{` | `{` | `\\{` | same |\n| `\\}` | `}` | `\\}` | same |\n| `\\1`..`\\9` | `\\1`..`\\9` (backref kept) | `1`..`9` (**backref lost**) | `:308` |\n| `\\0` | `0` (literal; `0` ∉ `posix_meta_escapes`) | `0` | `:306,313` |\n| `\\.` `\\*` `\\[` `\\^` `\\$` `\\\\` `\\?` `\\+` `\\|` | `\\.` … (escaped literal via `default`) | same | `:313`/`:304` → `:363-374` |\n| `\\` + NUL | raw NUL copied (`strchr` matches terminator), `lastspecial=0` | `\\<NUL>` | `:306` |\n| `(` | `\\(` **but `bracount++` anyway** | `(`, `bracount++`, state→NOT_BRACKET | `:322-341` |\n| `)` | `\\)` always | `bracount==0` ⇒ `\\)`; else `)`, `bracount--`, state unchanged | `:317-320` |\n| `?` `+` `{` `}` `\\|` | `\\?` `\\+` `\\{` `\\}` `\\|` | copied raw, state→NOT_BRACKET | `:326-341` |\n| `.` | `.` | `.` | `:334` |\n| `$` | `$` **unconditionally** (even mid‑pattern) | `$` | `:335` |\n| `*` | literal `\\*` if `posix_state < POSIX_NOT_BRACKET` (start of regex, or right after `^`) **or** `lastspecial=='('` (i.e. after `\\(`); else `*` | always `*` | `:343-351` |\n| `**`, `***` | 2nd and later `*` **dropped** (`lastspecial=='*'`) | same | `:344,351` |\n| `^` at start of pattern or after `\\(` | `^`, state→`POSIX_ANCHORED` | — | `:353-360` |\n| `^` elsewhere | `\\^` | `^` always (state unchanged) | `:353-361` |\n| `[` | `[`, state→CLASS_NOT_STARTED, `^` then `]` consumed if present | same | `:252-300` |\n| any other char ∈ `\\ ? * + \\| . ^ $ { } [ ] ( )` | `\\`+char | same | `:364-368` |\n| NUL byte (embedded) | `\\` + NUL (`strchr` matches terminator!) | same | `:364` |\n| byte `0xFF` | raw (`c<255` false) | same | `:364` |\n| other | raw copy, state→NOT_BRACKET, `lastspecial=0xff` | same | `:369-374` |\n\n`{n,m}`: BR needs `a\\{2,3\\}` ⇒ `a{2,3}`; BR `a{2,3}` ⇒ `a\\{2,3\\}`. ER `a{2,3}` ⇒ `a{2,3}`; ER `a\\{2,3\\}` ⇒ `a\\{2,3\\}`.\n\n## 4.2 Inside a class (`posix_state >= 3`) — `:204-246`\n* `]` ⇒ emit `]`, state→`POSIX_NOT_BRACKET`. Class end detection is purely positional (the `[`/`]` fix‑ups at `:285-299` handle `[^]` and `[]`).\n* State machine for `[:…:]`: `CLASS_NOT_STARTED` + `[` → `CLASS_STARTING`; `CLASS_STARTING` + `:` → `CLASS_STARTED`; `CLASS_STARTED` stays while `ISLOWER` (`:89` non‑EBCDIC `a`–`z`); on `:` with next `]` ⇒ emit `\":]\"`, consume `]`, `continue` (`:221-228`). **No name validation** — `[[:foo:]]` is copied verbatim; `posix_classes` (`:110-124`) is *not* consulted here (only glob uses it).\n* `\\` inside a class ⇒ emitted as `\\\\` (`:241` + `:243`), i.e. POSIX literal backslash.\n* Multi‑byte char copied via `memcpy(p, posix-clength, clength)` (`:243`).\n* Unterminated class ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET` (`:378-379`).\n\nTest set: `\"[]\"`→`[]`+`MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`; `\"[]]\"`→`(*NUL)[]]`; `\"[^]]\"`→`(*NUL)[^]]`; `\"[[:alpha:]]\"`→`(*NUL)[[:alpha:]]`; `\"[a\\\\]b]\"`→`(*NUL)[a\\\\]b]`; `\"[abc\"`→error.\n\n## 4.3 Error surface of `convert_posix`\n`PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `PCRE2_ERROR_END_BACKSLASH`, `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`. On **all** of these `*bufflenptr` == the **original `plength`** (`:171`), not the failing offset.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Input shapes (both converters)\n\n| Shape | POSIX | GLOB |\n|---|---|---|\n| `plength = 0` (or `pattern=NULL, plength=0`) | out `\"(*NUL)\"`, len 6 | out `\"(?s)\\A\\z\"`, len 8 |\n| `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` | `strlen` first; content after a NUL is invisible | same |\n| explicit length with embedded NUL | NUL emitted as `\\`+NUL (`:364`) → output contains a NUL; caller must use the returned length | same (`:1062`) |\n| UTF‑8 multibyte, **with** `CONVERT_UTF` | `GETCHARLENTEST` groups the char; code point ≥ 0x80 never equals a case label, `memcpy` copies all `clength` units ⇒ **byte‑identical to non‑UTF** | top level is byte‑wise regardless; **inside `[...]`** `GETCHARINCTEST` makes ranges code‑point based |\n| UTF‑8 multibyte, **without** `CONVERT_UTF` | byte‑wise; lead bytes 0xC2‑0xF4 and continuations 0x80‑0xBF are never metachars ⇒ same bytes out | `[à-é]` is byte‑wise ⇒ may hit `prev_c > c` ⇒ `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` |\n| invalid UTF‑8 + `CONVERT_UTF` (no `NO_UTF_CHECK`) | `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERRn`, `*bufflenptr = erroroffset` | same |\n| invalid UTF‑8 + `CONVERT_UTF|NO_UTF_CHECK` | undefined‑but‑deterministic: `GETUTF8LEN` may read past a truncated sequence | glob top level is byte‑safe; inside a class `GETCHARINCTEST` may over‑read |\n\n⇒ For POSIX, `CONVERT_UTF` changes **only** validation, never the output bytes.\n\n---\n\n# 6. `_pcre2_study` — what is computed and stored (`pcre2_study.c:1914-2084`)\n\nSignature `int PRIV(study)(pcre2_real_code *re)`; returns `0`, `1` (SSB_UNKNOWN — unreachable), `2` (missing bracket), `3` (unknown opcode).\n\nCaller gate (`pcre2_compile.c:11122`): the whole first‑CU/req‑CU/study block runs only when `PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE` is set. `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` / `pcre2_set_optimize(PCRE2_START_OPTIMIZE_OFF)` / `(*NO_START_OPT)` clears it ⇒ **study never runs**, no bitmap, `minlength` stays 0.\n\n## 6.1 Fields it touches\n* `re->start_bitmap[32]` — built in place by `set_start_bits` (`SET_BIT` at `:56`) even on paths that later fail.\n* `re->flags |= PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` **or** `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` (+ `PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS`), `re->first_codeunit` (`:2030-2041`).\n* May **clear** `PCRE2_LASTSET|PCRE2_LASTCASELESS` and zero `re->last_codeunit` (`:2031-2034`) when the collapsed first CU equals the required last CU (patterns like `/[Aa]a/`, `/a*a/`).\n* `re->minlength` (`:2078`), clamped to `UINT16_MAX`.\n* `firstcu/firstcuflags/reqcu/reqcuflags` themselves are **compile‑time locals** in `pcre2_compile.c` (`REQ_UNSET=0xffffffff`, `REQ_NONE=0xfffffffe`, `REQ_CASELESS=0x1`, `REQ_VARY=0x2`, `pcre2_compile.c:261-264`) and are turned into `re->flags`/`re->first_codeunit`/`re->last_codeunit` at `pcre2_compile.c:11148-11244` **before** `PRIV(study)` is called. Study only *overrides* the first CU when the bitmap collapses.\n\n## 6.2 Gates\n* `:1930` `set_start_bits` runs only if `(re->flags & (PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_STARTLINE)) == 0`.\n* `:2053-2054` `find_minlength` runs only if `(re->flags & (PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY|PCRE2_HASACCEPT)) == 0` **and** `re->top_backref <= MAX_CACHE_BACKREF (128)`.\n  * `PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY` set when the pattern can match empty (`pcre2_compile.c:10972`).\n  * `PCRE2_HASACCEPT` set when `(*ACCEPT)` present (`pcre2_compile.c:10981`) — also forces `reqcuflags=REQ_NONE`.\n  * ⇒ **129 or more capture groups referenced by backreference** (`top_backref > 128`) disables minlength.\n\n## 6.3 Bitmap collapse loop (`:1950-2042`) — distinct outcomes\nOnly when `set_start_bits` returned `SSB_DONE`:\n1. Any 8‑bit slot with **>1 bit** set ⇒ `goto DONE` ⇒ `PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` (`:1964-1965`).\n2. In UTF mode, a set bit with `c > 127` ⇒ `goto DONE` ⇒ `FIRSTMAPSET` (`:1990-1992`). **This is the key UTF difference:** e.g. `/[Ww]ord/` non‑UTF collapses to a caseless first CU, but any pattern whose bitmap includes a UTF lead byte cannot collapse.\n3. Exactly 1 bit total ⇒ `re->first_codeunit = a`, `PCRE2_FIRSTSET`.\n4. Exactly 2 bits, and they are case partners ⇒ `PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS`. Partner test (`:1996-2006`): `d = re->tables[fcc_offset + c]`; if `utf||ucp` then `UCD_CASESET(c)!=0` ⇒ `goto DONE` (multi‑case set), and `c>127` ⇒ `d = UCD_OTHERCASE(c)`; require `d == a`.\n5. 3+ bits ⇒ `goto DONE` ⇒ `FIRSTMAPSET` (`:2019`).\n6. `a < 0` (bitmap all zero, `SSB_DONE`) ⇒ `flags` stays `PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` ⇒ FIRSTMAPSET with an empty bitmap.\nPost‑study (`pcre2_compile.c:11263-11269`): `FIRSTMAPSET` forces `minminlength ≥ 1`, and `re->minlength = max(re->minlength, minminlength)`.\n\n## 6.4 `find_minlength` (`pcre2_study.c:101-767`) — opcode groups and driving shapes\nArgs: `(re, code, startcode, utf, recurses, countptr, backref_cache)`. Returns `-1` (`\\C` in UTF / `(*ACCEPT)` / `*countptr > 1000`), `-2` (missing bracket), `-3` (unlisted opcode), else the min length **in characters**.\n\n| Group (lines) | Opcodes | Effect / driving shape |\n|---|---|---|\n| `:121` | `OP_SBRA..OP_SCOND` at group head | **return 0** immediately (\"could be empty\" group) |\n| `:125` | `OP_CBRA`,`OP_CBRAPOS` | skip `IMM2_SIZE` |\n| `:129` | — | `(*countptr)++ > 1000` ⇒ **‑1** (complexity cap) |\n| `:141-145` | — | `branchlength >= UINT16_MAX` ⇒ clamp and jump to `nextbranch` |\n| `:150-164` | `OP_COND`,`OP_SCOND` | one‑branch condition (incl. `(?(DEFINE)…)`) adds **0**; two‑branch ⇒ treated as non‑capture |\n| `:166-177` | `OP_BRA` wrapping `OP_RECURSE`+`OP_KET` | `once_fudge = 1+LINK_SIZE`, process the recurse at this level (repeated `(?1)` cases) |\n| `:180-192` | `OP_ONCE`,`OP_SCRIPT_RUN`,`OP_SBRA`,`OP_BRAPOS`,`OP_SBRAPOS`, `OP_BRA` | recurse; add `d` |\n| `:199-214` | `OP_CBRA/SCBRA/CBRAPOS/SCBRAPOS` | cached by `recno` in `prev_cap_recno/prev_cap_d`, **unless** `PCRE2_DUPCAPUSED` (`(?\\|…)` present, `pcre2_compile.c:5016`) |\n| `:220-222` | `OP_ACCEPT`,`OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT` | **‑1** (dead path — `PCRE2_HASACCEPT` gate) |\n| `:230-243` | `OP_ALT`,`OP_KET`,`OP_KETRMAX/RMIN/RPOS`,`OP_END` | branch end: `length = min(length, branchlength)` unless `had_recurse`; `length==0` ⇒ early return; reset `branchlength=0`, `had_recurse=FALSE` per alternative |\n| `:247-254` | `OP_ASSERT`,`OP_ASSERT_NOT`,`OP_ASSERTBACK`,`OP_ASSERTBACK_NOT`,`OP_ASSERT_NA`,`OP_ASSERT_SCS`,`OP_ASSERTBACK_NA` | skipped entirely (contribute 0) |\n| `:259-281` | `OP_REVERSE`,`OP_VREVERSE`,`OP_CREF`,`OP_DNCREF`,`OP_RREF`,`OP_DNRREF`,`OP_FALSE`,`OP_TRUE`,`OP_CALLOUT`,`OP_SOD`,`OP_SOM`,`OP_EOD`,`OP_EODN`,`OP_CIRC`,`OP_CIRCM`,`OP_DOLL`,`OP_DOLLM`,`OP_NOT_WORD_BOUNDARY`,`OP_WORD_BOUNDARY`,`OP_NOT_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY`,`OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY` | +0 |\n| `:283-285` | `OP_CALLOUT_STR` | skip by `GET(cc, 1+2*LINK_SIZE)` |\n| `:289-296` | `OP_BRAZERO`,`OP_BRAMINZERO`,`OP_BRAPOSZERO`,`OP_SKIPZERO` | whole group skipped, +0 (`{0}`, `{0,n}`, `?` on a group) |\n| `:300-321` | `OP_CHAR/CHARI/NOT/NOTI` + all `PLUS` variants (`PLUS,PLUSI,MINPLUS,MINPLUSI,POSPLUS,POSPLUSI,NOTPLUS…NOTPOSPLUSI`) | **+1**; in UTF skip `GET_EXTRALEN` |\n| `:323-328` | `OP_TYPEPLUS`,`OP_TYPEMINPLUS`,`OP_TYPEPOSPLUS` | **+1**; step 4 if `\\p`/`\\P`, else 2 |\n| `:333-342` | `OP_EXACT/EXACTI/NOTEXACT/NOTEXACTI` | **+ GET2** (chars, not code units) |\n| `:344-348` | `OP_TYPEEXACT` | **+ GET2**; +2 more if `\\p`/`\\P` |\n| `:352-372` | `OP_PROP`,`OP_NOTPROP`,`OP_NOT_DIGIT`,`OP_DIGIT`,`OP_NOT_WHITESPACE`,`OP_WHITESPACE`,`OP_NOT_WORDCHAR`,`OP_WORDCHAR`,`OP_ANY`,`OP_ALLANY`,`OP_EXTUNI`,`OP_HSPACE`,`OP_NOT_HSPACE`,`OP_VSPACE`,`OP_NOT_VSPACE` | **+1** |\n| `:377-380` | `OP_ANYNL` (`\\R`) | **+1** (CRLF is 2 but 1 is a valid lower bound) |\n| `:386-392` | `OP_ANYBYTE` (`\\C`) | **utf ⇒ return ‑1**; else +1 |\n| `:397-413` | `OP_TYPESTAR/MINSTAR/QUERY/MINQUERY/POSSTAR/POSQUERY` and `OP_TYPEUPTO/MINUPTO/POSUPTO` | +0; `\\p`/`\\P` adds 2 to the step |\n| `:417-458` | `OP_CLASS`,`OP_NCLASS`,`OP_XCLASS`,`OP_ECLASS` then the `OP_CR*` suffix | `CRPLUS/CRMINPLUS/CRPOSPLUS` ⇒ +1; `CRSTAR/CRMINSTAR/CRQUERY/CRMINQUERY/CRPOSSTAR/CRPOSQUERY` ⇒ +0; `CRRANGE/CRMINRANGE/CRPOSRANGE` ⇒ **+GET2** (the min); no suffix ⇒ +1. `XCLASS`/`ECLASS` advance by `GET(cc,1)` |\n| `:477-542` | `OP_DNREF`,`OP_DNREFI` | if `dupcapused` **or** `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF` ⇒ `d=0`; else min over all same‑named groups (each via `find_bracket`, cached); `cs==NULL` ⇒ **‑2** |\n| `:547-594` | `OP_REF`,`OP_REFI` | cache lookup; `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF` ⇒ `d=0`; simple recursion (`cs < cc < ce`) or mutual recursion (found in `recurses` chain) ⇒ `had_recurse=TRUE`, `d=0`; `cs==NULL` ⇒ **‑2** |\n| `:598-637` | `REPEAT_BACK_REFERENCE` | `min` from the `OP_CR*` suffix (0 / 1 / `GET2`); overflow‑safe `branchlength += min*d`, clamped to `UINT16_MAX` |\n| `:643-675` | `OP_RECURSE` | cached by `recno` in `prev_recurse_recno/_d`; simple/mutual recursion ⇒ `had_recurse=TRUE`, adds nothing; `once_fudge` consumed here |\n| `:685-728` | all `UPTO/STAR/QUERY` char forms and their `I`/`NOT` variants | +0; UTF extralen skip |\n| `:732-738` | `OP_MARK`,`OP_COMMIT_ARG`,`OP_PRUNE_ARG`,`OP_SKIP_ARG`,`OP_THEN_ARG` | +0, skip `+ cc[1]` |\n| `:742-750` | `OP_CLOSE`,`OP_COMMIT`,`OP_FAIL`,`OP_PRUNE`,`OP_SET_SOM`,`OP_SKIP`,`OP_THEN` | +0 |\n| `:756-758` | anything else | **‑3** |\n\nNote `MAX_CACHE_BACKREF = 128` (`:52`), cache invalidation loop at `:531`/`:590`.\nDistinct minlength drivers to test: alternation min (`/ab|cdef/` ⇒ 2), recursion‑ignored branch (`/(a|b(?1))/`), backref multiplication (`/(abc)\\1{3}/` ⇒ 12), `{0}` group, `(?(DEFINE)…)`, `\\C` in UTF (⇒ minlength stays 0), `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF`, `(?|…)` dup captures, `top_backref = 129`.\n\n---\n\n# 7. `set_start_bits` — `pcre2_study.c:1092-1894`\n\nSignature `static int set_start_bits(pcre2_real_code *re, PCRE2_SPTR code, BOOL utf, BOOL ucp, int *depthptr)`. Returns `SSB_FAIL=0, SSB_DONE=1, SSB_CONTINUE=2, SSB_UNKNOWN=3, SSB_TOODEEP=4` (`:60`).\n`table_limit = utf ? 16 : 32` (`:1100`) — the crucial UTF switch for `set_type_bits`/`set_nottype_bits`.\n`*depthptr > 1000` ⇒ `SSB_TOODEEP` (`:1106`).\n\n## 7.1 Return‑value semantics\n* `SSB_DONE` — found a **mandatory** starter in every branch. Only this value at the outermost call makes the map usable.\n* `SSB_CONTINUE` — set at `:1373` on `OP_ALT` (branch had only optional starters) and returned at `:1377-1381` on any `OP_KET/KETRMAX/KETRMIN/KETRPOS`. At top level this means **map dropped**; inside a nested group it makes the caller keep scanning after the group (`:1357-1361`).\n* `SSB_FAIL` / `SSB_UNKNOWN` / `SSB_TOODEEP` propagate immediately (`:1362`).\n\n## 7.2 Opcodes that immediately return `SSB_FAIL` (`:1136-1208`) — these are the \"bitmap abandoned\" triggers\n`OP_ACCEPT, OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT, OP_ALLANY, OP_ANY, OP_ANYBYTE, OP_CIRCM, OP_CLOSE, OP_COMMIT, OP_COMMIT_ARG, OP_COND, OP_CREF, OP_FALSE, OP_TRUE, OP_DNCREF, OP_DNREF, OP_DNREFI, OP_DNRREF, OP_DOLL, OP_DOLLM, OP_END, OP_EOD, OP_EODN, OP_EXTUNI, OP_FAIL, OP_MARK, OP_NOT, OP_NOTEXACT, OP_NOTEXACTI, OP_NOTI, OP_NOTMINPLUS(I), OP_NOTMINQUERY(I), OP_NOTMINSTAR(I), OP_NOTMINUPTO(I), OP_NOTPLUS(I), OP_NOTPOSPLUS(I), OP_NOTPOSQUERY(I), OP_NOTPOSSTAR(I), OP_NOTPOSUPTO(I), OP_NOTPROP, OP_NOTQUERY(I), OP_NOTSTAR(I), OP_NOTUPTO(I), OP_NOT_HSPACE, OP_NOT_VSPACE, OP_PRUNE, OP_PRUNE_ARG, OP_RECURSE, OP_REF, OP_REFI, OP_REVERSE, OP_VREVERSE, OP_RREF, OP_SCOND, OP_SET_SOM, OP_SKIP, OP_SKIP_ARG, OP_SOD, OP_SOM, OP_THEN, OP_THEN_ARG`.\nPlus `default: return SSB_UNKNOWN` (`:1131`), `OP_ECLASS ⇒ SSB_FAIL` (`:1719-1720`), and `OP_TYPE*` whose type is `OP_ANY`/`OP_ALLANY`/unknown ⇒ `SSB_FAIL` (`:1620-1623`).\n\n## 7.3 Bit‑setting branches\n| Lines | Opcodes | Bits set | `try_next` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `:1213-1215` | `OP_CIRC` | none, skip | continue |\n| `:1222-1240` | `OP_PROP` with `tcode[1]==PT_CLIST` | for each c in `ucd_caseless_sets[tcode[2]]`, UTF ⇒ first byte of `ord2utf(c)`; else `c>0xff?0xff:c` | stop |\n| `:1222` | `OP_PROP` with any other `PT_*` | — | `SSB_FAIL` |\n| `:1244-1249` | `\\b \\B` (`OP_WORD_BOUNDARY`, `OP_NOT_WORD_BOUNDARY`, `OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY`, `OP_NOT_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY`) | none | continue |\n| `:1256-1333` | `OP_ASSERT`, `OP_ASSERT_NA` | look past the assertion, skipping nested assertions/`\\b`/callouts (`:1264-1299`); if the next significant op ∈ {`OP_PROP(PT_CLIST)`, `OP_ANYNL`, `OP_CHAR`, `OP_CHARI`, `OP_EXACT`, `OP_EXACTI`, `OP_HSPACE`, `OP_MINPLUS(I)`, `OP_PLUS(I)`, `OP_POSPLUS(I)`, `OP_VSPACE`, `OP_DIGIT`, `OP_NOT_DIGIT`, `OP_WORDCHAR`, `OP_NOT_WORDCHAR`, `OP_WHITESPACE`, `OP_NOT_WHITESPACE`} ⇒ `tcode = ncode; continue` (skip the assertion); otherwise fall into the group case | — |\n| `:1342-1363` | `OP_BRA/SBRA/CBRA/SCBRA/BRAPOS/SBRAPOS/CBRAPOS/SCBRAPOS/ONCE/SCRIPT_RUN` | recurse; `SSB_DONE`⇒stop, `SSB_CONTINUE`⇒skip group and keep going, else propagate | — |\n| `:1385-1391` | `OP_CALLOUT`, `OP_CALLOUT_STR` | none | continue |\n| `:1396-1403` | `OP_ASSERT_NOT`, `OP_ASSERTBACK`, `OP_ASSERTBACK_NOT`, `OP_ASSERTBACK_NA`, `OP_ASSERT_SCS` | skipped | continue |\n| `:1407-1414` | `OP_BRAZERO`, `OP_BRAMINZERO`, `OP_BRAPOSZERO` | recurse into the group (bits added) then continue past it; `FAIL/UNKNOWN/TOODEEP` propagate, `CONTINUE`/`DONE` both continue | continue |\n| `:1418-1422` | `OP_SKIPZERO` | group skipped, no bits | continue |\n| `:1426-1433` | `OP_STAR/MINSTAR/POSSTAR/QUERY/MINQUERY/POSQUERY` | `set_table_bit(caseless=FALSE)` | continue |\n| `:1435-1442` | same + `I` | `set_table_bit(caseless=TRUE)` | continue |\n| `:1446-1456` | `OP_UPTO/MINUPTO/POSUPTO` (+`I`) | `set_table_bit` at `tcode+1+IMM2_SIZE` | continue |\n| `:1460-1469` | `OP_EXACT`, `OP_CHAR`, `OP_PLUS`, `OP_MINPLUS`, `OP_POSPLUS` | `set_table_bit(FALSE)` | **stop** |\n| `:1471-1480` | `OP_EXACTI`, `OP_CHARI`, `OP_PLUSI`, `OP_MINPLUSI`, `OP_POSPLUSI` | `set_table_bit(TRUE)` | **stop** |\n| `:1488-1519` | `OP_HSPACE` | `HT`, `SPACE`; **utf ⇒ 0xC2,0xE1,0xE2,0xE3**; **non‑utf ⇒ NBSP (0xA0)** | stop |\n| `:1521-1553` | `OP_ANYNL`, `OP_VSPACE` | `LF,VT,FF,CR`; **utf ⇒ 0xC2,0xE2**; non‑utf ⇒ `NEL (0x85)` | stop |\n| `:1560-1588` | `OP_NOT_DIGIT/DIGIT/NOT_WHITESPACE/WHITESPACE/NOT_WORDCHAR/WORDCHAR` | `set_type_bits`/`set_nottype_bits(cbit_*, table_limit)` | stop |\n| `:1593-1601` | `OP_TYPEPLUS/TYPEMINPLUS/TYPEPOSPLUS`, `OP_TYPEEXACT` | pointer fudge only, re‑dispatch on the single type | continue |\n| `:1606-1714` | `OP_TYPEUPTO/MINUPTO/POSUPTO/STAR/MINSTAR/POSSTAR/QUERY/MINQUERY/POSQUERY` | dispatch on `tcode[1]`: `OP_ANY`/`OP_ALLANY`/default ⇒ **SSB_FAIL**; `HSPACE`/`ANYNL`/`VSPACE`/`(NOT_)DIGIT`/`(NOT_)WHITESPACE`/`(NOT_)WORDCHAR` same bit sets as above | continue |\n| `:1719-1720` | `OP_ECLASS` | — | **SSB_FAIL** |\n| `:1731-1786` | `OP_XCLASS` | see 7.4 | — |\n| `:1801-1811` | `OP_NCLASS` | **utf ⇒ `start_bitmap[24] \\|= 0xf0` (0xC4‑0xC8) and `memset(bitmap+25,0xff,7)` (0xC9‑0xFF)**; non‑utf identical to `OP_CLASS` | falls through |\n| `:1818-1885` | `OP_CLASS` | copy `classmap`: **utf ⇒ bytes 0‑15 copied verbatim, then for each set bit c in 128..255 set `((c>>6)\\|0xC0)` and jump `c = (c&0xC0)+0x40-1`** (`:1838-1850`); non‑utf ⇒ all 32 bytes OR'd (`:1856`). Then the `OP_CR*` suffix: `CRSTAR/CRMINSTAR/CRQUERY/CRMINQUERY/CRPOSSTAR/CRPOSQUERY` ⇒ continue; `CRRANGE/CRMINRANGE/CRPOSRANGE` ⇒ continue **iff `GET2(tcode,1)==0`**, else stop; default ⇒ stop | — |\n\n### `set_table_bit` (`:788-850`)\nSets the bit for the first code unit. UTF ⇒ consumes the rest of the char via `GETUTF8INC` when `c >= 0xc0`. Caseless: if `utf||ucp` ⇒ `c = UCD_OTHERCASE(c)` and (utf) set `ord2utf(c)[0]`, else if `c<256` set `c`; if **neither** utf nor ucp ⇒ `SET_BIT(re->tables[fcc_offset + c])`.\n\n### `set_type_bits` / `set_nottype_bits` (`:873-923`)\n* Positive, `table_limit==16` (utf): copies the low 16 bytes, then for every c in 128..255 whose cbit is set, sets `ord2utf(c)[0]`.\n* Negative, `table_limit==16` (utf): copies the negated low 16 bytes, then **`start_bitmap[24..31] = 0xff`** (all bytes ≥ 0xC0).\n* Non‑utf (`table_limit==32`): plain 32‑byte OR / negated‑OR.\n\n## 7.4 `OP_XCLASS` UTF handling (`:1731-1786`) and `study_char_list` (`:942-1054`)\n* `xclassflags = tcode[1+LINK_SIZE]`. **`SSB_FAIL` if `(flags & XCL_HASPROP) != 0` or `(flags & (XCL_MAP|XCL_NOT)) == XCL_NOT`** (negative XCLASS with no map).\n* `classmap = (flags & XCL_MAP) ? tcode+1+LINK_SIZE+1 : NULL`.\n* If `utf && !(flags & XCL_NOT)`: `p = tcode+1+LINK_SIZE+1+(classmap?32:0)`; if `*p >= XCL_LIST (0x10)` ⇒ `study_char_list` (binary‑packed 16/32‑bit range lists, `XCL_CHAR_LIST_LOW_16_*`, `XCL_BEGIN_WITH_RANGE`, `XCL_ITEM_COUNT_MASK`, `XCL_CHAR_END/SHIFT`), else walk `XCL_SINGLE`/`XCL_RANGE`/`XCL_END` setting UTF‑8 lead‑byte bits (`:1760-1785`); `default` ⇒ `SSB_UNKNOWN`. Then `goto HANDLE_CLASSMAP`.\n* Negative XCLASS **with** a map falls through to the `OP_NCLASS` code (setting 0xC4‑0xFF in UTF) then the classmap merge.\n\n## 7.5 Patterns that drop the bitmap (test list)\n`/a/` (FIRSTSET before study ⇒ study skipped), `/^a/m` (STARTLINE ⇒ skipped), `/.a/` (`OP_ANY` ⇒ FAIL), `/\\Ca/` (utf, `OP_ANYBYTE` ⇒ FAIL), `/\\X/` (`OP_EXTUNI` ⇒ FAIL), `/(?1)x/`+`(x)` (`OP_RECURSE` ⇒ FAIL), `/(a)\\1/` (`OP_REF` ⇒ FAIL), `/(?(1)a|b)/` (`OP_COND` ⇒ FAIL), `/(*MARK:x)a/` (`OP_MARK` ⇒ FAIL), `/[^\\x{100}]/` in UTF with no map (`XCL_NOT` w/o `XCL_MAP` ⇒ FAIL), `/[\\p{L}\\x{100}]/` (`XCL_HASPROP` ⇒ FAIL), any `[…]` built with set operators (`OP_ECLASS` ⇒ FAIL), `/a?/` alone (`OP_QUERY` then `OP_KET` ⇒ CONTINUE at top ⇒ dropped), `/a*b|/` (`OP_ALT` ⇒ CONTINUE), 1001‑deep nesting (`SSB_TOODEEP`).\n\n---\n\n# 8. `_pcre2_auto_possessify` — `pcre2_auto_possess.c:1171-1414`\n\nSignature `int PRIV(auto_possessify)(PCRE2_UCHAR *code, const compile_block *cb)`; returns 0 or `-1` (opcode ≥ `OP_TABLE_LENGTH`, unreachable). **Mutates the compiled code.**\n`utf = (cb->external_options & PCRE2_UTF) != 0`, `ucp = (… & PCRE2_UCP) != 0` (`:1179-1180`). `rec_limit = 1000` (`:1178`), decremented in `compare_opcodes` (`:566`) — exhaustion ⇒ `FALSE` (leave alone).\n\n## 8.1 Enable/disable\n`pcre2_compile.c:11084`: runs iff `(optim_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_AUTO_POSSESS) != 0`. Cleared by `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS` (`0x4000`) at `pcre2_compile.c:10410-10411`, by `pcre2_set_optimize(ctx, PCRE2_AUTO_POSSESS_OFF /*=65*/)`, and by the in‑pattern `(*NO_AUTO_POSSESS)` (`pcre2_compile.c:10570`). ⇒ zero rewrites, everything stays `OP_STAR`/`OP_MINSTAR`/…\n\n## 8.2 What gets rewritten\n**Single‑char iterators** (`:1194-1240`), `c ∈ [OP_STAR, OP_TYPEPOSUPTO]`, base‑normalized via `get_repeat_base` (`:296-305`) to one of `OP_STAR / OP_STARI / OP_NOTSTAR / OP_NOTSTARI / OP_TYPESTAR`. Only considered when the normalized `c <= OP_MINUPTO` (i.e. greedy or lazy, never already‑possessive) — `end = NULL` otherwise. `list[1] = (c==OP_STAR||OP_PLUS||OP_QUERY||OP_UPTO)` = \"greedy\".\nRewrites (`:1204-1237`), all `*code += delta`:\n`OP_STAR|OP_MINSTAR → OP_POSSTAR`, `OP_PLUS|OP_MINPLUS → OP_POSPLUS`, `OP_QUERY|OP_MINQUERY → OP_POSQUERY`, `OP_UPTO|OP_MINUPTO → OP_POSUPTO`. The delta preserves the `I`/`NOT`/`TYPE` family.\n**Class iterators** (`:1241-1293`): `OP_CLASS`, `OP_NCLASS`, `OP_XCLASS`, `OP_ECLASS` followed by `OP_CRSTAR..OP_CRMINRANGE`; `list[1] = (c & 1) == 0` (even `OP_CR*` opcodes are the \"can be empty\" ones). Rewrites `CRSTAR|CRMINSTAR→CRPOSSTAR`, `CRPLUS|CRMINPLUS→CRPOSPLUS`, `CRQUERY|CRMINQUERY→CRPOSQUERY`, `CRRANGE|CRMINRANGE→CRPOSRANGE`.\nNote: `OP_CRPOS*` are outside `[OP_CRSTAR, OP_CRMINRANGE]` so already‑possessive classes are skipped.\n\n## 8.3 `get_chr_property_list` — `:330-524`\n`list[0]` = normalized opcode, `list[1]` = \"can match empty\", `list[2..7]` opcode‑specific (`MAX_LIST = 8`, `:53`).\n| Accepted opcodes | `list[2..]` |\n|---|---|\n| `:391-409` `OP_NOT_DIGIT, OP_DIGIT, OP_NOT_WHITESPACE, OP_WHITESPACE, OP_NOT_WORDCHAR, OP_WORDCHAR, OP_ANY, OP_ALLANY, OP_ANYNL, OP_NOT_HSPACE, OP_HSPACE, OP_NOT_VSPACE, OP_VSPACE, OP_EXTUNI, OP_EODN, OP_EOD, OP_DOLL, OP_DOLLM` | nothing |\n| `:411-416` `OP_CHAR, OP_NOT` | `[2]=chr` (`GETCHARINCTEST` — UTF aware), `[3]=NOTACHAR` |\n| `:418-441` `OP_CHARI, OP_NOTI` → normalized to `OP_CHAR/OP_NOT` | `[2]=chr`, `[3]=othercase`: `chr<128 \\|\\| (chr<256 && !utf && !ucp)` ⇒ `fcc[chr]`, else `UCD_OTHERCASE(chr)`; if equal ⇒ `[3]=NOTACHAR` else `[4]=NOTACHAR` |\n| `:444-478` `OP_PROP, OP_NOTPROP` | non‑`PT_CLIST`: `[2]=ptype`, `[3]=pdata`. `PT_CLIST`: expanded into `list[2..]` from `ucd_caseless_sets`, `list[0]` becomes `OP_CHAR`/`OP_NOT` — so a caseless multi‑case char behaves as a small char list |\n| `:481-520` `OP_NCLASS, OP_CLASS, OP_XCLASS, OP_ECLASS` | `[2] = end-code` (offset back to the bitmap/xclass body), `[3] = end-class_end`; `list[1]` from the `OP_CR*` suffix (`CRSTAR/CRMINSTAR/CRQUERY/CRMINQUERY/CRPOSSTAR/CRPOSQUERY`⇒TRUE, `CRPLUS/CRMINPLUS/CRPOSPLUS`⇒FALSE, `CRRANGE/…`⇒`GET2(end,1)==0`) |\n| everything else | `return NULL` ⇒ **not possessifiable** |\n\n## 8.4 `compare_opcodes` — `:547-1148`\nRight‑hand context walk:\n* skip `OP_CALLOUT` / `OP_CALLOUT_STR` (`:584-594`); `OP_ALT` ⇒ jump to end of group (`:598-602`).\n* `OP_END` (`:612`) ⇒ `return base_list[1] != 0` (**greedy iterator at end of pattern ⇒ possessify; lazy ⇒ never**).\n* `OP_KET`, `OP_KETRPOS` (`:623-688`): `base_list[1]==0` ⇒ FALSE. Then by the opening bracket:\n  * `OP_CBRA/SCBRA/CBRAPOS/SCBRAPOS` ⇒ FALSE if `cb->had_recurse` (any recursion in the pattern).\n  * `OP_SCRIPT_RUN` ⇒ FALSE unless `base_list[0]` is `OP_CHAR`/`OP_CHARI`.\n  * `OP_ASSERT`, `OP_ASSERT_NOT`, `OP_ONCE` ⇒ `return !entered_a_group`.\n  * `OP_ASSERTBACK`, `OP_ASSERTBACK_NOT` ⇒ FALSE if **any** branch starts with `OP_VREVERSE` (variable‑length lookbehind); else `!entered_a_group`.\n  * `OP_ASSERT_NA`, `OP_ASSERTBACK_NA` ⇒ FALSE.\n  * `OP_KETRMAX` / `OP_KETRMIN` are **not** in this switch ⇒ they reach `get_chr_property_list`, return NULL ⇒ FALSE.\n* `OP_ONCE`, `OP_BRA`, `OP_CBRA` (`:692-710`): recurse for every non‑final branch, set `entered_a_group = TRUE`.\n* `OP_BRAZERO`, `OP_BRAMINZERO` (`:712-729`): only if followed by `OP_BRA/OP_CBRA/OP_ONCE`; recurse past the group.\n\nComparison arms:\n1. **char list vs anything** (`:747-756`, executed at `:987-1141`): iterate every char of the small list against `list_ptr[0]`. Returns FALSE on any overlap. Handled right‑hand ops: `OP_CHAR`, `OP_NOT`, `OP_DIGIT`, `OP_NOT_DIGIT`, `OP_WHITESPACE`, `OP_NOT_WHITESPACE`, `OP_WORDCHAR` (note `chr < 255`, not 256 — asymmetry at `:1035`), `OP_NOT_WORDCHAR`, `OP_HSPACE`, `OP_NOT_HSPACE`, `OP_ANYNL`/`OP_VSPACE`, `OP_NOT_VSPACE`, `OP_DOLL`/`OP_EODN` (CR, LF, VT, FF, NEL, 0x2028, 0x2029), `OP_EOD` (always OK), `OP_PROP`/`OP_NOTPROP` via `check_char_prop`, `OP_NCLASS` (`chr>255` ⇒ FALSE), `OP_CLASS` (`chr>255` ⇒ no overlap), `OP_XCLASS` via `PRIV(xclass)(…, cb->start_code, utf)`, `OP_ECLASS` via `PRIV(eclass)`; anything else ⇒ FALSE. Then `list[1]==0` ⇒ TRUE, else keep scanning.\n2. **bitset vs bitset/type** (`:760-856`): triggered when either side is `OP_CLASS`, **or (8‑bit only) `!utf` and either side is `OP_NCLASS`** (`:761-764`, `:768`). Right side may be `OP_CLASS`/`OP_NCLASS` (direct 32‑byte AND), `OP_XCLASS` (FALSE if `XCL_HASPROP`; if no `XCL_MAP` ⇒ `list[1]==0 ? (XCL_NOT==0) : continue`), or `OP_(NOT_)DIGIT/WHITESPACE/WORDCHAR` using `cb->cbits + cbit_*` with `invert_bits`. Byte‑wise 32‑byte AND (or AND‑NOT); any non‑zero ⇒ FALSE.\n3. **property/table** (`:861-982`): if `leftop ∈ {OP_PROP, OP_NOTPROP}`: `rightop == OP_EOD` ⇒ TRUE; `rightop ∈ {OP_PROP, OP_NOTPROP}` ⇒ `n = propposstab[base_list[2]][list[2]]` (`:127-143`, `PT_TABSIZE = PT_ANY = 13`) and cases 0–17 (`:895-965`) using `catposstab[7][30]` (`:152-161`) and `posspropstab[3][4]` (`:174-178`). Else ⇒ `autoposstab[leftop-OP_NOT_DIGIT][rightop-OP_NOT_DIGIT]` with `FIRST_AUTOTAB_OP=OP_NOT_DIGIT`, `LAST_AUTOTAB_LEFT_OP=OP_EXTUNI`, `LAST_AUTOTAB_RIGHT_OP=OP_DOLLM` (`pcre2_internal.h:1634-1636`) — 17 rows × 21 cols (`:75-94`).\n\n### `autoposstab` (rows = repeated/left, cols = following/right)\nRow/col order (from `pcre2_internal.h:1648-1672`): `\\D \\d \\S \\s \\W \\w . .+(ALLANY) \\C \\P \\p \\R \\H \\h \\V \\v \\X` then extra cols `\\Z \\z $ $M`. The `1` entries (exhaustive from `:77-93`):\n* `\\D`: `\\d`, `\\z`\n* `\\d`: `\\D`, `\\s`, `\\W`, `\\R`, `\\h`, `\\v`, `\\Z`, `\\z`, `$`, `$M`\n* `\\S`: `\\s`, `\\R`, `\\h`, `\\v`, `\\Z`, `\\z`, `$`, `$M`\n* `\\s`: `\\d`, `\\S`, `\\w`, `\\z`\n* `\\W`: `\\d`, `\\w`, `\\z`\n* `\\w`: `\\s`, `\\W`, `\\R`, `\\h`, `\\v`, `\\Z`, `\\z`, `$`, `$M`\n* `.`: `\\R`, `\\z`\n* `.+`(ALLANY), `\\C`, `\\X`: `\\z` only\n* `\\P`, `\\p`: all zero (handled by `propposstab`)\n* `\\R`: `\\d`, `\\s`, `\\w`, `.`, `\\h`, `\\z`\n* `\\H`: `\\h`, `\\z`\n* `\\h`: `\\d`, `\\S`, `\\w`, `\\R`, `\\H`, `\\v`, `\\z`\n* `\\V`: `\\R`, `\\v`, `\\z`\n* `\\v`: `\\d`, `\\S`, `\\w`, `\\h`, `\\V`, `\\z`\n\n## 8.5 Effect of the four options\n| Option | Mechanism |\n|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_UTF` | (a) `utf` param to `GETCHARINCTEST` in `get_chr_property_list` (`:413`, `:421`) so `list[2]` is a code point not a byte; (b) `chr<128` gate for `fcc` vs `UCD_OTHERCASE` (`:425-428`); (c) at `:763`/`:768` `OP_NCLASS` is only treated as a bitset when **not** UTF; (d) `xclass`/`eclass` calls get `utf` (`:1118`, `:1126`); (e) the `MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` extralen skip at `:1348-1409` |\n| `PCRE2_UCP` | only at `:425` — with UCP (even without UTF), a 128‑255 char's other case comes from `UCD_OTHERCASE` instead of `fcc`, changing `list[3]` and hence overlap decisions for caseless Latin‑1 |\n| `PCRE2_CASELESS` | selects `OP_CHARI`/`OP_NOTI`/`OP_STARI`… at compile time ⇒ `get_chr_property_list` produces a **2‑element** char list (`chr`, othercase) instead of 1, so overlaps are more likely ⇒ fewer possessifications. Also makes multi‑case chars compile to `OP_PROP/PT_CLIST` (`pcre2_compile.c:6374-6398`) which expands to an n‑element char list |\n| `PCRE2_EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT` | **not referenced in this file.** It acts earlier, in `pcre2_compile.c:6384-6389` and `:6421-6426`: a `UCD_CASESET` whose first member is `< 128` is ignored ⇒ the item compiles to plain `OP_CHARI`/`OP_NOTI` instead of `OP_PROP/PT_CLIST`, so `get_chr_property_list` yields a 2‑element list instead of the full caseless set. Observable difference: `/(?i)k+\\x{212a}/` vs `/(?i:(?r)k)+\\x{212a}/` |\n\n## 8.6 Test matrix\nPossessified: `/\\d+\\D/`, `/\\d+\\Z/`, `/a+b/`, `/[a-z]+[0-9]/`, `/\\w+\\s/`, `/a*$/` (via `$`⇒`\\d` row? use `/\\d*$/`), `/x+\\z/`, `/a++/` already, `/(?>a+)b/`, `/(?=a+b)/`.\nLeft alone: `/a+a/`, `/a+\\w/`, `/\\d+\\d/`, `/(a+)\\1/` (had_recurse? use `/(?1)|(a+b)/`), `/a+?b/` (lazy), `/(a+)b/` with `(?1)` present, `/(?<=a+)b/` variable lookbehind, `/(*script_run:\\d+x)/` with non‑char base, `/[\\p{L}]+x/` (XCL_HASPROP), any `OP_ECLASS`.\n\n---\n\n# 9. `pcre2_xclass.c`\n\n## 9.1 `_pcre2_xclass`\n```c\nBOOL PRIV(xclass)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR data, const uint8_t *char_lists_end, BOOL utf)\n```\n(`:66-67`; exported as `_pcre2_xclass_8`.) `data` points at the **flag code unit** of the XCLASS payload (i.e. `opcode+1+LINK_SIZE`). `char_lists_end` = `(const uint8_t *)re + re->code_start` at match time / `cb->start_code` at compile time.\n\n* `:75-78` **8‑bit: `utf` is unconditionally forced to `TRUE`.** The `utf` argument is therefore inert in this build.\n* `:71` `not_negated = (*data & XCL_NOT) == 0` — negation is the `XCL_NOT (0x01)` flag.\n* `:82-88` if `XCL_MAP (0x02)`: `c < 256` ⇒ **return the raw bitmap bit** (negation already baked into the map by the compiler — do *not* apply `not_negated`); otherwise skip 32 code units.\n* `:93-263` property list, while `*data == XCL_PROP (3) || XCL_NOTPROP (4)`; `isprop = (*data == XCL_PROP)`; each item is 3 units (`tag`, `ptype`, `pdata`), advanced by `data += 2` after the tag consume (`:101`, `:260`). All `PT_*` branches:\n\n| `PT_` | Test (`:106-248`) |\n|---|---|\n| `PT_LAMP` | `chartype ∈ {Lu, Ll, Lt}` |\n| `PT_GC` | `data[1] == ucp_gentype[chartype]` |\n| `PT_PC` | `data[1] == chartype` |\n| `PT_SC` | `data[1] == prop->script` |\n| `PT_SCX` | `data[1]==script \\|\\| MAPBIT(ucd_script_sets + UCD_SCRIPTX_PROP, data[1])` |\n| `PT_ALNUM` | gentype ∈ {L, N} |\n| `PT_SPACE`, `PT_PXSPACE` | `HSPACE_CASES`/`VSPACE_CASES` (HT, SP, NBSP, 0x1680, 0x180E, 0x2000‑0x200A, 0x202F, 0x205F, 0x3000; LF, VT, FF, CR, NEL, 0x2028, 0x2029) ⇒ match; else gentype == Z |\n| `PT_WORD` | gentype ∈ {L, N} or chartype ∈ {Mn, Pc} — **note: uses `Mn`/`Pc`, unlike `check_char_prop` which uses `c == '_'`** |\n| `PT_UCNC` | `c < 0xa0` ⇒ `c ∈ {'$','@','`'}`; else `c < 0xd800 \\|\\| c > 0xdfff` |\n| `PT_BIDICL` | `UCD_BIDICLASS_PROP == data[1]` |\n| `PT_BOOL` | `MAPBIT(ucd_boolprop_sets + UCD_BPROPS_PROP, data[1])` |\n| `PT_PXGRAPH` | `gentype != Z && (gentype != C \\|\\| (chartype == Cf && c != 0x061C && c != 0x180E && (c < 0x2066 \\|\\| c > 0x2069)))` — XCLASS‑only |\n| `PT_PXPRINT` | `chartype != Zl && chartype != Zp && (gentype != C \\|\\| (chartype == Cf && c != 0x061C && (c < 0x2066 \\|\\| c > 0x2069)))` — XCLASS‑only |\n| `PT_PXPUNCT` | `gentype == P \\|\\| (c < 128 && gentype == S)` — XCLASS‑only |\n| `PT_PXXDIGIT` | `[0-9A-Fa-f]` ∪ `0xFF10-0xFF19` ∪ `0xFF21-0xFF26` ∪ `0xFF41-0xFF46` |\n| `default` | unreachable ⇒ FALSE |\n\nEach match returns `not_negated`; no early false — the loop just continues.\n* `:269-308` **legacy list form** (`*data < XCL_LIST` i.e. `< 0x10`): sequence of `XCL_SINGLE(1)`/`XCL_RANGE(2)` items terminated by `XCL_END(0)`, chars encoded with `GETCHARINC` when `utf`. Items are **sorted**, so `c <= x` allows early exit (`:288`, `:304`). Falling off the end ⇒ `!not_negated`.\n* `:310-440` **packed char‑list form**. 8‑bit: `type = (data[0]<<8) | data[1]`, `data += 2`; `next_char = char_lists_end - (GET(data,0) << 1)`; `type &= XCL_TYPE_MASK (0xfff)`, `XCL_TYPE_BIT_LEN = 3`, `XCL_ITEM_COUNT_MASK = 3`, `XCL_BEGIN_WITH_RANGE = 0x4`, `XCL_CHAR_END = 0x1`, `XCL_CHAR_SHIFT = 1`. Sub‑lists: `c >= XCL_CHAR_LIST_HIGH_16_START (0x8000)` skips the low‑16 list (`:325-337`); `c < XCL_CHAR_LIST_LOW_32_START (0x10000)` ⇒ 16‑bit binary search (`:339-375`); else 32‑bit search (`:377-440`). Empty list or `c` below the first entry ⇒ `((type & XCL_BEGIN_WITH_RANGE) != 0) == not_negated`. The `#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 32` block (`:394-408`) is dead here.\n\nInput‑configuration axes for `xclass`: `XCL_NOT` × `XCL_MAP` × `XCL_HASPROP` × {legacy item list, packed char list} × `c<256` / `256≤c<0x8000` / `0x8000≤c<0x10000` / `c≥0x10000`.\n\n## 9.2 `_pcre2_eclass` — `:461-545`\n```c\nBOOL PRIV(eclass)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR data_start, PCRE2_SPTR data_end,\n                  const uint8_t *char_lists_end, BOOL utf)\n```\n* `flags = *ptr++`; `ECL_MAP (0x01)`. `c < 256` **and** `ECL_MAP` ⇒ return the bitmap bit directly and **never evaluate the expression** (`:478-485`); otherwise skip 32 units and evaluate.\n* RPN evaluation on a **32‑bit register used as a bit stack** (`stack`, LSB = top), `stack_depth` tracked only for assertions:\n  * `ECL_AND (1)`: `stack = (stack >> 1) & (stack | ~1u)` — pops 2, pushes AND. Requires depth ≥ 2.\n  * `ECL_OR (2)`: `stack = (stack >> 1) | (stack & 1u)`.\n  * `ECL_XOR (3)`: `stack = (stack >> 1) ^ (stack & 1u)`.\n  * `ECL_NOT (4)`: `stack ^= 1u` (in place, depth ≥ 1).\n  * `ECL_XCLASS (5)`: `matched = PRIV(xclass)(c, ptr+1+LINK_SIZE, char_lists_end, utf)`; `ptr += GET(ptr,1)`; `stack = (stack<<1) | matched`.\n  * anything else ⇒ FALSE (unreachable).\n* Terminates when `ptr >= data_end`; asserts `stack_depth == 1`; returns `(stack & 1) != 0`. **Max nesting depth 32 operands** is implicit (silently overflows beyond that — the compiler is responsible for the bound).\n* Differences vs `xclass`: takes an explicit `data_end`; `ECL_MAP` instead of `XCL_MAP`; no negation flag (negation is the `ECL_NOT` operator); no direct property items (only nested `ECL_XCLASS` leaves); `ECL_ANY (6)` / `ECL_NONE (7)` are compile‑time only and must never appear.\n\n## 9.3 `_pcre2_update_classbits` — `pcre2_compile_class.c:751-866` (not in `pcre2_xclass.c`)\n```c\nvoid PRIV(update_classbits)(uint32_t ptype, uint32_t pdata, BOOL negated, uint8_t *classbits)\n```\nCompile‑time mirror of `xclass`'s property tests, restricted to `c ∈ [0,256)`, ORing bits into a 32‑byte map.\n* `ptype == PT_ANY` and `!negated` ⇒ `memset(classbits, 0xff, 32)`; `PT_ANY` + negated ⇒ no change.\n* Same `PT_*` arms, with three deliberate divergences from `PRIV(xclass)`: `PT_UCNC` uses `c >= 0xa0` (no surrogate carve‑out); `PT_PXGRAPH`/`PT_PXPRINT` omit the 0x061C/0x180E/0x2066‑0x2069 exceptions (all > 255); `PT_PXXDIGIT` omits the fullwidth ranges. `default:` asserts `PT_PXXDIGIT`. The file header comment at `pcre2_xclass.c:69` and `pcre2_compile_class.c:754` note they must be kept in sync.\n\n---\n\n# 10. `_pcre2_script_run` — `pcre2_script_run.c:83-341`\n\n```c\nBOOL PRIV(script_run)(PCRE2_SPTR ptr, PCRE2_SPTR endptr, BOOL utf)\n```\n`utf` feeds `GETCHARINCTEST` (`:100`, `:332`) ⇒ with `utf==FALSE` the subject is read **byte‑wise** (code points 0‑255 only). Called from `pcre2_match.c:6481` (`OP_SCRIPT_RUN`, `ptr = P->eptr`, `endptr = Feptr`). Without `SUPPORT_UNICODE` it is a `return TRUE` stub (`:335-340`) — not this build.\n\nStates (`:72-78`): `SCRIPT_UNSET, SCRIPT_MAP, SCRIPT_HANPENDING, SCRIPT_HANHIRAKATA, SCRIPT_HANBOPOMOFO, SCRIPT_HANHANGUL`. `UCD_MAPSIZE = ucp_Unknown/32+1`, `FULL_MAPSIZE = ucp_Script_Count/32+1` (`:80-81`).\n\nBranches:\n1. `:99` `ptr >= endptr` ⇒ **TRUE** (empty).\n2. `:100-101` read first char; `ptr >= endptr` ⇒ **TRUE** (single char — *any* char, including `ucp_Unknown`).\n3. Per char (`:124-333`):\n   * `:132` `script == ucp_Unknown` ⇒ **FALSE**.\n   * `:138` the script/extension block is **skipped entirely** when `UCD_SCRIPTX_PROP(ucd) == 0 && (script == ucp_Inherited || script == ucp_Common)` — such chars are accepted with anything and do not change state.\n   * `:148-150` build `map` = copy of `ucd_script_sets + UCD_SCRIPTX_PROP` (first `UCD_MAPSIZE` words), zero the rest, and `MAPSET(map, script)` unless script is Common or Inherited.\n   * `SCRIPT_UNSET` (`:159-184`): `Han` ⇒ `HANPENDING`; `Hiragana`/`Katakana` ⇒ `HANHIRAKATA`; `Bopomofo` ⇒ `HANBOPOMOFO`; `Hangul` ⇒ `HANHANGUL`; otherwise `require_map = map`, state `SCRIPT_MAP`.\n   * `SCRIPT_HANPENDING` (`:203-223`): another `Han` ⇒ no change. Otherwise build `chspecial` from `FOUND_BOPOMOFO 1 / FOUND_HIRAGANA 2 / FOUND_KATAKANA 4 / FOUND_HANGUL 8` (`:198-201`); `chspecial == 0` ⇒ **FALSE**; `== FOUND_BOPOMOFO` ⇒ `HANBOPOMOFO`; `== (HIRAGANA|KATAKANA)` ⇒ `HANHIRAKATA`; any other combination ⇒ stay `HANPENDING`.\n   * `SCRIPT_HANHIRAKATA` (`:228-231`): FALSE unless `MAPBIT(Han)+MAPBIT(Hiragana)+MAPBIT(Katakana) != 0`.\n   * `SCRIPT_HANBOPOMOFO` (`:233-235`): FALSE unless `Han` or `Bopomofo` bit set.\n   * `SCRIPT_HANHANGUL` (`:237-239`): FALSE unless `Han` or `Hangul` bit set.\n   * `SCRIPT_MAP` (`:244-288`): FALSE unless `require_map & map` is non‑zero in some word; then, if the char's script is `Han`/`Hiragana`/`Katakana`/`Bopomofo`/`Hangul`, **switch to the corresponding HAN* state**; otherwise `require_map &= map` (intersection narrows).\n4. Digit consistency (`:302-327`): only for `ucd->chartype == ucp_Nd`. `c <= ucd_digit_sets[1]` (`0x39`) ⇒ `digitset = 1` (ASCII fast path); else binary chop over `ucd_digit_sets[1..77]` (`pcre2_ucd.c:216-228`, 77 sets: 0x39, 0x669, 0x6F9, …, 0x1FBF9) yielding the index of the set's '9'. First `Nd` sets `require_digitset`; a later `Nd` with a different index ⇒ **FALSE**. Note `0x1D7D7/0x1D7E1/0x1D7EB/0x1D7F5/0x1D7FF` are distinct sets **within the same (Common) script**, so mixed math‑digit styles fail.\n5. `:331` end reached ⇒ **TRUE**.\n\nSubject shapes to test: `\"\"`, `\"A\"`, single `ucp_Unknown` char (TRUE), two `ucp_Unknown` (FALSE), `\"ab\"` (TRUE), Latin+Cyrillic (FALSE), Latin + combining mark (Inherited, TRUE), Han+Han, Han+Hiragana (TRUE), Han+Bopomofo (TRUE), Han+Hangul (TRUE), Hiragana+Bopomofo (FALSE), Bopomofo then Hangul (FALSE), Han then a char in `Bopomofo+Hangul+Han+Hiragana+Katakana` (stays HANPENDING), `\"1٢\"` ASCII+Arabic‑Indic digits (FALSE), `\"١٢\"` same set (TRUE), `\"0\" + U+1D7CE`‑style mixed math digits (FALSE), Common punctuation between two scripts, `utf=FALSE` with bytes ≥ 0x80.\n\n---\n\n# 11. `_pcre2_extuni` — `pcre2_extuni.c:92-155`\n\n```c\nPCRE2_SPTR PRIV(extuni)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR eptr, PCRE2_SPTR start_subject,\n                        PCRE2_SPTR end_subject, BOOL utf, int *xcount)\n```\n`c` = the **already‑consumed** first character; `eptr` = position of the *next* character. Returns the pointer after the cluster. `xcount` (nullable) is **incremented** per extra character consumed (`:151`). A `#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` stub returning NULL exists at `:56-67` (dead here).\n\nTable: `PRIV(ucp_gbtable)[lgb] & (1u << rgb)` non‑zero ⇒ **no break** (`pcre2_tables.c:203-223`, `ESZ = Extend|SpacingMark|ZWJ`). `ucp_gb*` indices (`pcre2_ucp.h:204-218`): `CR 0, LF 1, Control 2, Extend 3, Prepend 4, SpacingMark 5, L 6, V 7, T 8, LV 9, LVT 10, Regional_Indicator 11, Other 12, ZWJ 13, Extended_Pictographic 14`.\n\nRow contents (drives the branch table):\n| lgb | joins with rgb ∈ |\n|---|---|\n| CR | LF only |\n| LF, Control | nothing (always break) |\n| Extend, SpacingMark, Other, Extended_Pictographic | Extend, SpacingMark, ZWJ |\n| Prepend | ESZ + Prepend, L, V, T, LV, LVT, Other, Regional_Indicator |\n| L | ESZ + L, V, LV, LVT |\n| V, LV | ESZ + V, T |\n| T, LVT | ESZ + T |\n| Regional_Indicator | Regional_Indicator only (**note: not ESZ**) |\n| ZWJ | ESZ + Extended_Pictographic |\n\nLoop body (`:99-152`):\n1. `:103` `if (!utf) c = *eptr; else GETCHARLEN(c, eptr, len);` — `len` is 1 in non‑UTF, 1‑4 in UTF.\n2. `:105` table lookup; 0 ⇒ break.\n3. `:110-111` **ZWJ ⇒ Extended_Pictographic** is allowed **only if `was_ep_ZWJ`** (the ZWJ itself was preceded by Extended_Pictographic, possibly with `Extend`s in between). Otherwise break.\n4. `:116-138` **RI ⇒ RI**: walk backwards from `eptr-1` (with `BACKCHAR` when `utf`, `:120`, `:128-130`), counting consecutive preceding RIs while `bptr > start_subject`; **odd `ricount` ⇒ break**. This makes the result depend on `start_subject`, i.e. on how much subject precedes the match start.\n5. `:143` `was_ep_ZWJ = (lgb == Extended_Pictographic && rgb == ZWJ)`.\n6. `:148` `if (rgb != Extend || lgb != Extended_Pictographic) lgb = rgb;` — **`lgb` is *not* updated when Extend follows Extended_Pictographic**, so any number of Extends may precede a joining ZWJ.\n7. `:150-151` advance `eptr += len`; `*xcount += 1` if non‑NULL.\n\nSubject shapes per branch:\n* `eptr == end_subject` at entry ⇒ returns `eptr` unchanged, `xcount` untouched.\n* `\"\\r\\n\"` ⇒ joins (CR→LF). `\"\\n\\r\"`, `\"\\nX\"` ⇒ break immediately.\n* `\"a\" + U+0301` (Other→Extend) ⇒ joins; chain of Extends ⇒ all joined.\n* `\"a\" + U+0903` (SpacingMark) ⇒ joins. `\"a\" + U+200D` (ZWJ) ⇒ joins.\n* Prepend: U+0600 + `\"a\"` ⇒ joins.\n* Hangul: `L+V`, `L+LV`, `LV+T`, `LVT+T` join; `V+L`, `T+V` break.\n* Emoji ZWJ: `U+1F468 U+200D U+1F469` ⇒ one cluster (needs `was_ep_ZWJ`); `\"a\" U+200D U+1F469` ⇒ breaks before the pictographic. `U+1F468 U+0301 U+200D U+1F469` ⇒ still one cluster (rule 6 keeps `lgb == Extended_Pictographic`).\n* Regional indicators: 2 RIs ⇒ one cluster; 3 RIs ⇒ 2+1 (odd count breaks); crucially, matching starting **mid‑flag** changes the answer, so test `start_subject` offsets, and both `utf=TRUE` (BACKCHAR path) and `utf=FALSE`.\n* `utf == FALSE`: `c = *eptr` so only 0‑255 grapheme‑break classes are reachable (`CR, LF, Control, Extend (0xAD?), Other`), `len` always 1, `BACKCHAR` skipped.\n\n---\n\n## Cross‑cutting notes for test authors\n1. **`pcre2_convert.c:684`** writes one byte too many for a negated glob class when `GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` is set; the extra byte is stale `out_str[2]`. Reproduce bit‑exactly.\n2. **`pcre2_convert.c:364` and `:1062`** treat `c == 0` as \"in `pcre2_escaped_literals`\" because `strchr` matches the terminator ⇒ embedded NULs are emitted as `\\`+NUL. Same at `:306` for `posix_meta_escapes`.\n3. **`pcre2_convert.c:171`** means every `convert_posix` error reports `*bufflenptr == input plength`, never a real offset; `convert_glob` errors report `pattern - pattern_start`, except the separator/escape ≥ 128 error which reports 0.\n4. **`pcre2_study.c:1990-1992`** is the only place where 8‑bit UTF prevents the bitmap→first‑CU collapse; `pcre2_study.c:1100` (`table_limit`) and the `SET_BIT(0xC2/0xE1/0xE2/0xE3)` blocks are the other UTF‑only bit patterns.\n5. **`pcre2_auto_possess.c:1035`** uses `chr < 255` for `OP_WORDCHAR` where the neighbouring cases use `chr < 256` — an intentional‑looking asymmetry worth an explicit test at `chr == 255`.\n6. **`pcre2_xclass.c:77`** forces `utf = TRUE` in 8‑bit, so the `utf` argument of `_pcre2_xclass`/`_pcre2_eclass` cannot be exercised in this configuration.\n7. `PT_WORD` differs between `pcre2_xclass.c:158-164` (`Mn`/`Pc`) and `pcre2_auto_possess.c:253-256` (`c == '_'`) — differential test around U+203F (Pc) and U+0300 (Mn).","usage":{"total_tokens":159075,"tool_uses":46,"duration_ms":789306},"uuid":"f0baeca6-c113-476f-9539-67c4bc8e31c0","session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_his3krc7zb5ahskhhy2r2fedgglaiozh2vqv3famyl4i7ypa2g7q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_011TD9CbcqPAJhuNa6yNvffE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_compile_match.rs","content":"// Phase B — the compile pipeline and both matchers, driven end to end the way\n// a real consumer does: build a compile context, set the options, compile, then\n// run the full match with a match context.\n//\n// The compiled bytecode is compared BYTE FOR BYTE, which is a far stronger\n// check than comparing match results alone: it transitively validates every\n// internal that only runs during compilation (the parser, `_pcre2_study_8`,\n// `_pcre2_auto_possessify_8`, `_pcre2_check_escape_8`, the class compilers, the\n// capture-group/name-table helpers), none of which can be called directly\n// without fabricating an internal `compile_block`.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::{c_int, c_void};\nuse std::ptr;\n\n/// One compile configuration: option bits plus compile-context state.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct Cfg {\n    pub name: &'static str,\n    pub opts: u32,\n    pub xopts: u32,\n    pub newline: u32,\n    pub bsr: u32,\n    pub varlookbehind: u32,\n    pub parens_limit: u32,\n    pub optimize: u32,\n    pub own_tables: bool,\n}\n\nimpl Cfg {\n    const fn new(name: &'static str, opts: u32, xopts: u32) -> Cfg {\n        Cfg {\n            name,\n            opts,\n            xopts,\n            newline: 0,\n            bsr: 0,\n            varlookbehind: 0,\n            parens_limit: 0,\n            optimize: u32::MAX,\n            own_tables: false,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// The configuration axes the C actually branches on, crossed.\nfn configs() -> Vec<Cfg> {\n    let mut v = vec![\n        Cfg::new(\"default\", 0, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"CASELESS\", PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"MULTILINE\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DOTALL\", PCRE2_DOTALL, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"EXTENDED\", PCRE2_EXTENDED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"EXTENDED_MORE\", PCRE2_EXTENDED | PCRE2_EXTENDED_MORE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UNGREEDY\", PCRE2_UNGREEDY, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DUPNAMES\", PCRE2_DUPNAMES, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_AUTO_CAPTURE\", PCRE2_NO_AUTO_CAPTURE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_AUTO_POSSESS\", PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\", PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR\", PCRE2_NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ANCHORED\", PCRE2_ANCHORED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ENDANCHORED\", PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ANCHORED|ENDANCHORED\", PCRE2_ANCHORED | PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DOLLAR_ENDONLY|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"FIRSTLINE\", PCRE2_FIRSTLINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_CIRCUMFLEX|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_BSUX\", PCRE2_ALT_BSUX, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_VERBNAMES\", PCRE2_ALT_VERBNAMES, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALLOW_EMPTY_CLASS\", PCRE2_ALLOW_EMPTY_CLASS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF\", PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"LITERAL\", PCRE2_LITERAL, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"LITERAL|CASELESS\", PCRE2_LITERAL | PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"AUTO_CALLOUT\", PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS\", PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        // --- UTF / UCP axis, the biggest behaviour switch in the library\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UCP\", PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|CASELESS\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP|CASELESS\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|MATCH_INVALID_UTF\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP|DOTALL|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_DOTALL | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        // --- EXTRA options\n        Cfg::new(\"X:CASELESS_RESTRICT\", PCRE2_CASELESS, PCRE2_EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT),\n        Cfg::new(\n            \"UTF|UCP|CASELESS + X:CASELESS_RESTRICT\",\n            PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_CASELESS,\n            PCRE2_EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT,\n        ),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:TURKISH_CASING\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_CASELESS, PCRE2_EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_BSD\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSD),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_BSS\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSS),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_BSW\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSW),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_POSIX\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_POSIX),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_DIGIT\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_DIGIT),\n        Cfg::new(\n            \"X:ASCII_all|UCP|UTF\",\n            PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_UTF,\n            PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSD | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSS | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSW\n                | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_POSIX | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_DIGIT,\n        ),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:MATCH_WORD\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_WORD),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:MATCH_LINE\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_LINE),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:MATCH_LINE|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_LINE),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ALT_BSUX\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALT_BSUX | PCRE2_ALT_BSUX * 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_BSUX + X:ALT_BSUX\", PCRE2_ALT_BSUX, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALT_BSUX),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ALLOW_SURROGATE_ESCAPES|UTF\", PCRE2_UTF, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_SURROGATE_ESCAPES),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:PYTHON_OCTAL\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_PYTHON_OCTAL),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:NO_BS0\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_NO_BS0),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:NEVER_CALLOUT\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_NEVER_CALLOUT),\n    ];\n    // --- newline convention axis (affects ., $, \\R, \\N and the CRLF scan)\n    for nl in [\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CR,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_LF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANYCRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_NUL,\n    ] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"MULTILINE + newline\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0);\n        c.newline = nl;\n        v.push(c);\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF|MULTILINE + newline\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0);\n        c.newline = nl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- \\R convention axis\n    for bsr in [PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE, PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"bsr\", 0, 0);\n        c.bsr = bsr;\n        v.push(c);\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF + bsr\", PCRE2_UTF, 0);\n        c.bsr = bsr;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- optimization directives (auto-possessify / start optimize on+off)\n    for opt in [\n        PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_NONE,\n        PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_FULL,\n        PCRE2_AUTO_POSSESS_OFF,\n        PCRE2_START_OPTIMIZE_OFF,\n    ] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"optimize\", 0, 0);\n        c.optimize = opt;\n        v.push(c);\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP + optimize\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0);\n        c.optimize = opt;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- variable lookbehind limit\n    for vl in [1u32, 2, 255] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"max_varlookbehind\", 0, 0);\n        c.varlookbehind = vl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- parens nest limit (drives PARENTHESES_NEST_TOO_DEEP)\n    for pl in [1u32, 3, 250] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"parens_nest_limit\", 0, 0);\n        c.parens_limit = pl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- locale tables built by pcre2_maketables (vs the built-in defaults)\n    let mut c = Cfg::new(\"own tables (pcre2_maketables)\", 0, 0);\n    c.own_tables = true;\n    v.push(c);\n    let mut c = Cfg::new(\"own tables + CASELESS\", PCRE2_CASELESS, 0);\n    c.own_tables = true;\n    v.push(c);\n    v\n}\n\n/// A compile context configured per `Cfg`, plus the tables it owns.\nstruct Ctx {\n    ccontext: Ptr,\n    tables: *const u8,\n}\n\nunsafe fn make_ctx(api: &Api, cfg: &Cfg) -> Ctx {\n    let cc = (api.compile_context_create)(ptr::null_mut());\n    assert!(!cc.is_null(), \"[{}] compile_context_create failed\", api.name);\n    if cfg.newline != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_newline)(cc, cfg.newline), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.bsr != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_bsr)(cc, cfg.bsr), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.varlookbehind != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_max_varlookbehind)(cc, cfg.varlookbehind), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.parens_limit != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_parens_nest_limit)(cc, cfg.parens_limit), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.xopts != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_compile_extra_options)(cc, cfg.xopts), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.optimize != u32::MAX {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_optimize)(cc, cfg.optimize), 0);\n    }\n    let mut tables = ptr::null();\n    if cfg.own_tables {\n        tables = (api.maketables)(ptr::null_mut());\n        assert!(!tables.is_null(), \"[{}] maketables failed\", api.name);\n        assert_eq!((api.set_character_tables)(cc, tables), 0);\n    }\n    Ctx { ccontext: cc, tables }\n}\n\nunsafe fn free_ctx(api: &Api, c: Ctx) {\n    (api.compile_context_free)(c.ccontext);\n    if !c.tables.is_null() {\n        (api.maketables_free)(ptr::null_mut(), c.tables);\n    }\n}\n\n/// Compile `pat` under `cfg` in both libraries.  Asserts the two agree on\n/// success/failure, on the error code and error offset, and (on success) that\n/// the produced bytecode is byte-identical.  Returns the two code objects.\nunsafe fn compile_both(p: &Pair, pat: &[u8], len: Sz, cfg: &Cfg, d: &mut Diffs) -> Option<(Ptr, Ptr)> {\n    let cc = make_ctx(&p.c, cfg);\n    let rc = make_ctx(&p.r, cfg);\n    let (mut eca, mut ecb) = (0 as c_int, 0 as c_int);\n    let (mut eoa, mut eob) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n    let a = (p.c.compile)(pat.as_ptr(), len, cfg.opts, &mut eca, &mut eoa, cc.ccontext);\n    let b = (p.r.compile)(pat.as_ptr(), len, cfg.opts, &mut ecb, &mut eob, rc.ccontext);\n    free_ctx(&p.c, cc);\n    free_ctx(&p.r, rc);\n\n    let tag = format!(\"compile({}) cfg[{}]\", show(pat), cfg.name);\n    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} null?\"), a.is_null(), b.is_null());\n    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} errorcode\"), eca, ecb);\n    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} erroroffset\"), eoa, eob);\n    if a.is_null() || b.is_null() {\n        if !a.is_null() {\n            (p.c.code_free)(a);\n        }\n        if !b.is_null() {\n            (p.r.code_free)(b);\n        }\n        return None;\n    }\n    assert_code_eq(a, b, &tag);\n    d.checked += 1;\n    Some((a, b))\n}\n\n// ============================================== compile: bytecode + info\n\n// CONFIGS rows: every Cfg x every pattern -> identical bytecode and identical\n// pattern_info for all 27 info ids.\n#[test]\nfn compile_bytecode_and_info_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let cfgs = configs();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    for cfg in &cfgs {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let b = pat.as_bytes();\n            // both explicit length and PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED\n            for &len in &[b.len(), PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED] {\n                if len == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED && b.contains(&0) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                unsafe {\n                    if let Some((a, bb)) = compile_both(p, b, len, cfg, &mut d) {\n                        compare_all_info(p, a, bb, &format!(\"{} cfg[{}]\", show(b), cfg.name), &mut d);\n                        (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                        (p.r.code_free)(bb);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    println!(\"compile configs={} patterns={}\", cfgs.len(), PATTERNS.len());\n    d.finish(\"compile: all Cfg x all PATTERNS x {explicit len, ZERO_TERMINATED}\");\n}\n\n/// `pcre2_pattern_info` for every info id, using the right result width.\nunsafe fn compare_all_info(p: &Pair, a: Ptr, b: Ptr, tag: &str, d: &mut Diffs) {\n    // uint32_t results\n    for what in [\n        PCRE2_INFO_ARGOPTIONS,\n        PCRE2_INFO_ALLOPTIONS,\n        PCRE2_INFO_EXTRAOPTIONS,\n        PCRE2_INFO_BACKREFMAX,\n        PCRE2_INFO_BSR,\n        PCRE2_INFO_CAPTURECOUNT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODEUNIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODETYPE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_HASCRORLF,\n        PCRE2_INFO_JCHANGED,\n        PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODEUNIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODETYPE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MATCHEMPTY,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MATCHLIMIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MAXLOOKBEHIND,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MINLENGTH,\n        PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_NEWLINE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_DEPTHLIMIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_HASBACKSLASHC,\n        PCRE2_INFO_HEAPLIMIT,\n    ] {\n        let (mut va, mut vb) = (0xDEAD_BEEFu32, 0xDEAD_BEEFu32);\n        let ra = (p.c.pattern_info)(a, what, &mut va as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        let rb = (p.r.pattern_info)(b, what, &mut vb as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] rc {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] val {tag}\"), va, vb);\n    }\n    // PCRE2_SIZE results\n    for what in [PCRE2_INFO_SIZE, PCRE2_INFO_FRAMESIZE, PCRE2_INFO_JITSIZE] {\n        let (mut va, mut vb) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n        let ra = (p.c.pattern_info)(a, what, &mut va as *mut usize as Ptr);\n        let rb = (p.r.pattern_info)(b, what, &mut vb as *mut usize as Ptr);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] rc {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] val {tag}\"), va, vb);\n    }\n    // FIRSTBITMAP: pointer to a 32-byte table (or NULL)\n    {\n        let (mut pa, mut pb) = (ptr::null::<u8>(), ptr::null::<u8>());\n        let ra = (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBITMAP, &mut pa as *mut _ as Ptr);\n        let rb = (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBITMAP, &mut pb as *mut _ as Ptr);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[FIRSTBITMAP] rc {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[FIRSTBITMAP] null {tag}\"), pa.is_null(), pb.is_null());\n        if !pa.is_null() && !pb.is_null() {\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"info[FIRSTBITMAP] bytes {tag}\"),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(pa, 32).to_vec(),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(pb, 32).to_vec(),\n            );\n        }\n    }\n    // NAMETABLE: name_count entries of name_entry_size bytes\n    {\n        let (mut na, mut nb) = (0u32, 0u32);\n        (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT, &mut na as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT, &mut nb as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        let (mut sa, mut sb) = (0u32, 0u32);\n        (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE, &mut sa as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE, &mut sb as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        if na == nb && sa == sb && na > 0 {\n            let (mut ta, mut tb) = (ptr::null::<u8>(), ptr::null::<u8>());\n            (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_NAMETABLE, &mut ta as *mut _ as Ptr);\n            (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_NAMETABLE, &mut tb as *mut _ as Ptr);\n            let n = (na * sa) as usize;\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"info[NAMETABLE] {tag}\"),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(ta, n).to_vec(),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(tb, n).to_vec(),\n            );\n            // and the by-name lookups over that table\n            for i in 0..na {\n                let ent = ta.add((i * sa) as usize);\n                let name = ent.add(2); // 2-byte group number, then NUL-term name\n                d.eq(\n                    &format!(\"substring_number_from_name #{i} {tag}\"),\n                    (p.c.substring_number_from_name)(a, name),\n                    (p.r.substring_number_from_name)(b, name),\n                );\n                let (mut f1, mut l1) = (ptr::null(), ptr::null());\n                let (mut f2, mut l2) = (ptr::null(), ptr::null());\n                let ra = (p.c.substring_nametable_scan)(a, name, &mut f1, &mut l1);\n                let rb = (p.r.substring_nametable_scan)(b, name, &mut f2, &mut l2);\n                d.eq(&format!(\"nametable_scan rc #{i} {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n                if ra >= 0 && rb >= 0 {\n                    d.eq(\n                        &format!(\"nametable_scan span #{i} {tag}\"),\n                        (f1 as usize - ta as usize, l1 as usize - ta as usize),\n                        (f2 as usize - tb as usize, l2 as usize - tb as usize),\n                    );\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ============================================================ code_copy\n\n// CONFIGS row: pcre2_code_copy / pcre2_code_copy_with_tables must reproduce a\n// pattern that is byte-identical to the original and to the other library's.\n#[test]\nfn code_copy_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let cfgs = configs();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    for cfg in cfgs.iter().take(34) {\n        for pat in PATTERNS.iter().step_by(3) {\n            let b = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                if let Some((a, bb)) = compile_both(p, b, b.len(), cfg, &mut d) {\n                    let tag = format!(\"{} cfg[{}]\", show(b), cfg.name);\n                    let ca = (p.c.code_copy)(a);\n                    let cb = (p.r.code_copy)(bb);\n                    assert!(!ca.is_null() && !cb.is_null(), \"code_copy failed {tag}\");\n                    assert_code_eq(ca, cb, &format!(\"code_copy {tag}\"));\n                    assert_code_eq(a, ca, &format!(\"code_copy vs original (C) {tag}\"));\n                    let ta = (p.c.code_copy_with_tables)(a);\n                    let tb = (p.r.code_copy_with_tables)(bb);\n                    assert!(!ta.is_null() && !tb.is_null(), \"code_copy_with_tables failed {tag}\");\n                    assert_code_eq(ta, tb, &format!(\"code_copy_with_tables {tag}\"));\n                    d.checked += 2;\n                    (p.c.code_free)(ca);\n                    (p.r.code_free)(cb);\n                    (p.c.code_free)(ta);\n                    (p.r.code_free)(tb);\n                    (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                    (p.r.code_free)(bb);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_code_copy_8 / pcre2_code_copy_with_tables_8 over Cfg x patterns\");\n}\n\n// ================================================================= matching\n\n/// Runs `pcre2_match` in both libraries and compares rc, ovector, startchar,\n/// mark, and the derived match-data accessors.\nunsafe fn cmp_match(\n    p: &Pair,\n    a: Ptr,\n    b: Ptr,\n    subj: &[u8],\n    len: Sz,\n    start: Sz,\n    mopts: u32,\n    ovecsize: u32,\n    mctx: (Ptr, Ptr),\n    tag: &str,\n    d: &mut Diffs,\n) {\n    let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(ovecsize, ptr::null_mut());\n    let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(ovecsize, ptr::null_mut());\n    let ra = (p.c.do_match)(a, subj.as_ptr(), len, start, mopts, mda, mctx.0);\n    let rb = (p.r.do_match)(b, subj.as_ptr(), len, start, mopts, mdb, mctx.1);\n    let oa = read_match_out(&p.c, mda, ra);\n    let ob = read_match_out(&p.r, mdb, rb);\n    d.eq(tag, oa, ob);\n    d.eq(\n        &format!(\"{tag} :: ovector_count\"),\n        (p.c.get_ovector_count)(mda),\n        (p.r.get_ovector_count)(mdb),\n    );\n    d.eq(\n        &format!(\"{tag} :: match_data_size\"),\n        (p.c.get_match_data_size)(mda),\n        (p.r.get_match_data_size)(mdb),\n    );\n    d.eq(\n        &format!(\"{tag} :: heapframes_size\"),\n        (p.c.get_match_data_heapframes_size)(mda),\n        (p.r.get_match_data_heapframes_size)(mdb),\n    );\n    // substring accessors over the result\n    if ra > 0 && rb > 0 {\n        for i in 0..(ra.max(rb) as u32 + 1) {\n            let (mut la, mut lb) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"{tag} :: substring_length_bynumber({i}) rc\"),\n                (p.c.substring_length_bynumber)(mda, i, &mut la),\n                (p.r.substring_length_bynumber)(mdb, i, &mut lb),\n            );\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_length_bynumber({i}) len\"), la, lb);\n            let mut ba = [0u8; 256];\n            let mut bb = [0u8; 256];\n            let (mut ca, mut cb) = (ba.len(), bb.len());\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"{tag} :: substring_copy_bynumber({i}) rc\"),\n                (p.c.substring_copy_bynumber)(mda, i, ba.as_mut_ptr(), &mut ca),\n                (p.r.substring_copy_bynumber)(mdb, i, bb.as_mut_ptr(), &mut cb),\n            );\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_copy_bynumber({i}) out\"), (ba, ca), (bb, cb));\n            let (mut pa, mut pb) = (ptr::null_mut::<u8>(), ptr::null_mut::<u8>());\n            let (mut na, mut nb) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n            let ga = (p.c.substring_get_bynumber)(mda, i, &mut pa, &mut na);\n            let gb = (p.r.substring_get_bynumber)(mdb, i, &mut pb, &mut nb);\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_get_bynumber({i}) rc\"), ga, gb);\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_get_bynumber({i}) len\"), na, nb);\n            if ga == 0 && gb == 0 {\n                d.eq(\n                    &format!(\"{tag} :: substring_get_bynumber({i}) bytes\"),\n                    std::slice::from_raw_parts(pa, na + 1).to_vec(),\n                    std::slice::from_raw_parts(pb, nb + 1).to_vec(),\n                );\n            }\n            if !pa.is_null() {\n                (p.c.substring_free)(pa);\n            }\n            if !pb.is_null() {\n                (p.r.substring_free)(pb);\n            }\n        }\n        // whole-list variant\n        let (mut la, mut lb) = (ptr::null_mut(), ptr::null_mut());\n        let (mut sa, mut sb) = (ptr::null_mut(), ptr::null_mut());\n        let ra2 = (p.c.substring_list_get)(mda, &mut la, &mut sa);\n        let rb2 = (p.r.substring_list_get)(mdb, &mut lb, &mut sb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_list_get rc\"), ra2, rb2);\n        if ra2 == 0 && rb2 == 0 {\n            let n = ra.max(rb) as usize + 1;\n            for i in 0..n {\n                let (x, y) = (*la.add(i), *lb.add(i));\n                let (nx, ny) = (*sa.add(i), *sb.add(i));\n                d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: list[{i}] len\"), nx, ny);\n                if nx == ny {\n                    d.eq(\n                        &format!(\"{tag} :: list[{i}] bytes\"),\n                        std::slice::from_raw_parts(x, nx).to_vec(),\n                        std::slice::from_raw_parts(y, ny).to_vec(),\n                    );\n                }\n            }\n            (p.c.substring_list_free)(la);\n            (p.r.substring_list_free)(lb);\n        }\n    }\n    (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n    (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n}\n\n/// Match options crossed over the axes `pcre2_match` branches on.\nconst MOPTS: &[(u32, &str)] = &[\n    (0, \"none\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTBOL, \"NOTBOL\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTEOL, \"NOTEOL\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTBOL | PCRE2_NOTEOL, \"NOTBOL|NOTEOL\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY, \"NOTEMPTY\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, \"NOTEMPTY_ATSTART\"),\n    (PCRE2_ANCHORED, \"ANCHORED\"),\n    (PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, \"ENDANCHORED\"),\n    (PCRE2_ANCHORED | PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, \"ANCHORED|ENDANCHORED\"),\n    (PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT, \"PARTIAL_SOFT\"),\n    (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD, \"PARTIAL_HARD\"),\n    (PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, \"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\"),\n    (PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK, \"NO_UTF_CHECK\"),\n    (PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT, \"COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT\"),\n    (PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK, \"DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK\"),\n    (PCRE2_NO_JIT, \"NO_JIT\"),\n];\n\n/// Compile configurations used for matching (a representative spread; the full\n/// set is covered by the bytecode test above).\nfn match_cfgs() -> Vec<Cfg> {\n    let all = configs();\n    let names = [\n        \"default\",\n        \"CASELESS\",\n        \"MULTILINE\",\n        \"DOTALL\",\n        \"UNGREEDY\",\n        \"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\",\n        \"NO_AUTO_POSSESS\",\n        \"ANCHORED\",\n        \"ENDANCHORED\",\n        \"FIRSTLINE\",\n        \"MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF\",\n        \"AUTO_CALLOUT\",\n        \"UTF\",\n        \"UCP\",\n        \"UTF|UCP\",\n        \"UTF|CASELESS\",\n        \"UTF|UCP|CASELESS\",\n        \"UTF|MATCH_INVALID_UTF\",\n        \"UTF|UCP|DOTALL|MULTILINE\",\n        \"X:CASELESS_RESTRICT\",\n        \"X:TURKISH_CASING\",\n        \"X:ASCII_all|UCP|UTF\",\n        \"X:MATCH_WORD\",\n        \"X:MATCH_LINE\",\n        \"own tables (pcre2_maketables)\",\n    ];\n    let mut v: Vec<Cfg> = all\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|c| names.contains(&c.name))\n        .cloned()\n        .collect();\n    // plus each newline convention with MULTILINE, and both \\R conventions\n    for nl in [\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CR,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_LF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANYCRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_NUL,\n    ] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"MULTILINE + newline\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0);\n        c.newline = nl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    for bsr in [PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE, PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF + bsr\", PCRE2_UTF, 0);\n        c.bsr = bsr;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    v\n}\n\n// CONFIGS rows: pcre2_match over (compile cfg) x (pattern) x (subject) x\n// (match options) x (startoffset) x (ovector size).\n#[test]\nfn match_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(100);\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    // Bound the run: deterministic limits so both libraries hit them alike.\n    let mca = unsafe { (p.c.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    let mcb = unsafe { (p.r.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    unsafe {\n        for (m, v) in [(&p.c, mca), (&p.r, mcb)] {\n            assert_eq!((m.set_match_limit)(v, 20_000), 0);\n            assert_eq!((m.set_depth_limit)(v, 2_000), 0);\n            assert_eq!((m.set_heap_limit)(v, 200), 0);\n        }\n    }\n    for cfg in &match_cfgs() {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    // a random slice of the option/offset/ovector axes per\n                    // (pattern, subject) keeps the run bounded while still\n                    // covering every axis many thousands of times overall\n                    for _ in 0..3 {\n                        let (mo, mn) = MOPTS[rng.below(MOPTS.len())];\n                        let start = if sb.is_empty() { 0 } else { rng.below(sb.len() + 1) };\n                        let ovec = *rng.pick(&[0u32, 1, 2, 4, 16, 64]);\n                        let len = if rng.chance(4) && !sb.contains(&0) {\n                            PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED\n                        } else {\n                            sb.len()\n                        };\n                        let tag = format!(\n                            \"match {} cfg[{}] subj={} start={} mopts={} ovec={} len={}\",\n                            show(pb),\n                            cfg.name,\n                            show(sb),\n                            start,\n                            mn,\n                            ovec,\n                            if len == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED { \"ZT\".into() } else { len.to_string() }\n                        );\n                        cmp_match(p, a, b, sb, len, start, mo, ovec, (mca, mcb), &tag, &mut d);\n                    }\n                }\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    unsafe {\n        (p.c.match_context_free)(mca);\n        (p.r.match_context_free)(mcb);\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_match_8: match_cfgs x PATTERNS x SUBJECTS x MOPTS x startoffset x ovector size\");\n}\n\n// CONFIGS rows: pcre2_dfa_match over the same axes, plus DFA_SHORTEST,\n// DFA_RESTART and workspace sizes.\n#[test]\nfn dfa_match_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(200);\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    let mca = unsafe { (p.c.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    let mcb = unsafe { (p.r.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    unsafe {\n        for (m, v) in [(&p.c, mca), (&p.r, mcb)] {\n            assert_eq!((m.set_match_limit)(v, 20_000), 0);\n            assert_eq!((m.set_depth_limit)(v, 2_000), 0);\n        }\n    }\n    let dfa_opts: &[(u32, &str)] = &[\n        (0, \"none\"),\n        (PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST, \"DFA_SHORTEST\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTBOL, \"NOTBOL\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTEOL, \"NOTEOL\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY, \"NOTEMPTY\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, \"NOTEMPTY_ATSTART\"),\n        (PCRE2_ANCHORED, \"ANCHORED\"),\n        (PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, \"ENDANCHORED\"),\n        (PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT, \"PARTIAL_SOFT\"),\n        (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD, \"PARTIAL_HARD\"),\n        (PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, \"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\"),\n        (PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK, \"NO_UTF_CHECK\"),\n        (PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT, \"COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT\"),\n    ];\n    for cfg in &match_cfgs() {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    for _ in 0..3 {\n                        let (mo, mn) = dfa_opts[rng.below(dfa_opts.len())];\n                        let start = if sb.is_empty() { 0 } else { rng.below(sb.len() + 1) };\n                        let ovec = *rng.pick(&[0u32, 1, 2, 4, 16]);\n                        // include a deliberately tiny workspace to reach\n                        // PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE identically\n                        let wsn = *rng.pick(&[20usize, 100, 1000]);\n                        let mut wa = vec![0 as c_int; wsn];\n                        let mut wb = vec![0 as c_int; wsn];\n                        let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(ovec, ptr::null_mut());\n                        let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(ovec, ptr::null_mut());\n                        let ra = (p.c.dfa_match)(\n                            a, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), start, mo, mda, mca, wa.as_mut_ptr(), wsn,\n                        );\n                        let rb = (p.r.dfa_match)(\n                            b, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), start, mo, mdb, mcb, wb.as_mut_ptr(), wsn,\n                        );\n                        let tag = format!(\n                            \"dfa_match {} cfg[{}] subj={} start={} opts={} ovec={} ws={}\",\n                            show(pb), cfg.name, show(sb), start, mn, ovec, wsn\n                        );\n                        d.eq(&tag, read_match_out(&p.c, mda, ra), read_match_out(&p.r, mdb, rb));\n                        (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n                        (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n                    }\n                }\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    unsafe {\n        (p.c.match_context_free)(mca);\n        (p.r.match_context_free)(mcb);\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_dfa_match_8: match_cfgs x PATTERNS x SUBJECTS x dfa options x workspace sizes\");\n}\n\n// CONFIGS row: pcre2_next_match_8 — iterating the alternative match ends that\n// pcre2_dfa_match records in the ovector.\n#[test]\nfn next_match_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    let cfgs = match_cfgs();\n    for cfg in cfgs.iter().take(20) {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    let mut ws_a = vec![0 as c_int; 1000];\n                    let mut ws_b = vec![0 as c_int; 1000];\n                    let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                    let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                    let ra = (p.c.dfa_match)(\n                        a, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, 0, mda, ptr::null_mut(), ws_a.as_mut_ptr(), 1000,\n                    );\n                    let rb = (p.r.dfa_match)(\n                        b, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, 0, mdb, ptr::null_mut(), ws_b.as_mut_ptr(), 1000,\n                    );\n                    let tag = format!(\"next_match {} cfg[{}] subj={}\", show(pb), cfg.name, show(sb));\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} dfa rc\"), ra, rb);\n                    // walk the whole iterator to exhaustion in both\n                    let mut steps_a = Vec::new();\n                    let mut steps_b = Vec::new();\n                    loop {\n                        let (mut o, mut f) = (usize::MAX, 0u32);\n                        let rc = (p.c.next_match)(mda, &mut o, &mut f);\n                        steps_a.push((rc, o, f));\n                        if rc <= 0 || steps_a.len() > 40 {\n                            break;\n                        }\n                    }\n                    loop {\n                        let (mut o, mut f) = (usize::MAX, 0u32);\n                        let rc = (p.r.next_match)(mdb, &mut o, &mut f);\n                        steps_b.push((rc, o, f));\n                        if rc <= 0 || steps_b.len() > 40 {\n                            break;\n                        }\n                    }\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} next_match sequence\"), steps_a, steps_b);\n                    (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n                    (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n                }\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_next_match_8: full iteration after pcre2_dfa_match over cfgs x patterns x subjects\");\n}\n\n// =========================================================== callouts\n\nstatic mut CALLOUT_LOG: Vec<u8> = Vec::new();\n\n/// Records the fields of every callout block so the two libraries' callout\n/// sequences can be compared exactly.  Layout mirrors `pcre2_callout_block`.\n#[repr(C)]\nstruct CalloutBlock {\n    version: u32,\n    callout_number: u32,\n    capture_top: u32,\n    capture_last: u32,\n    offset_vector: *const Sz,\n    mark: Sptr,\n    subject: Sptr,\n    subject_length: Sz,\n    start_match: Sz,\n    current_position: Sz,\n    pattern_position: Sz,\n    next_item_length: Sz,\n    callout_string_offset: Sz,\n    callout_string_length: Sz,\n    callout_string: Sptr,\n    callout_flags: u32,\n}\n\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn record_callout(blk: *mut c_void, _data: *mut c_void) -> c_int {\n    let b = &*(blk as *const CalloutBlock);\n    let log = &mut *ptr::addr_of_mut!(CALLOUT_LOG);\n    for v in [\n        b.version as u64,\n        b.callout_number as u64,\n        b.capture_top as u64,\n        b.capture_last as u64,\n        b.subject_length as u64,\n        b.start_match as u64,\n        b.current_position as u64,\n        b.pattern_position as u64,\n        b.next_item_length as u64,\n        b.callout_string_offset as u64,\n        b.callout_string_length as u64,\n        b.callout_flags as u64,\n        b.mark.is_null() as u64,\n    ] {\n        log.extend_from_slice(&v.to_le_bytes());\n    }\n    if !b.callout_string.is_null() {\n        log.extend_from_slice(std::slice::from_raw_parts(\n            b.callout_string,\n            b.callout_string_length,\n        ));\n    }\n    0\n}\n\n// CONFIGS rows: match-time callouts, with AUTO_CALLOUT and with explicit\n// (?C) / (?C1) / (?C{str}) callouts — the whole callout sequence must match.\n#[test]\nfn callouts_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    let cal_pats: &[&str] = &[\n        \"a(?C)b\",\n        \"a(?C1)b\",\n        \"a(?C255)b\",\n        \"a(?C{txt})b\",\n        \"(?C0)a(?C1)b(?C2)c\",\n        \"(a)(?C)(b)\",\n        \"\\\\d+(?C9)\\\\w*\",\n        \"(?:a(?C)|b(?C))+\",\n        \"^(?C)a*(?C)$\",\n    ];\n    for cfg in [\n        Cfg::new(\"default\", 0, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"AUTO_CALLOUT\", PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|AUTO_CALLOUT\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n    ] {\n        // AUTO_CALLOUT applies to every pattern, so use the full corpus there\n        let pats: Vec<&str> = if cfg.opts & PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT != 0 {\n            PATTERNS.iter().copied().collect()\n        } else {\n            cal_pats.iter().copied().collect()\n        };\n        for pat in pats {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), &cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                // pcre2_callout_enumerate walks the compiled pattern\n                {\n                    CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                    let ea = (p.c.callout_enumerate)(a, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut());\n                    let la = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                    CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                    let eb = (p.r.callout_enumerate)(b, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut());\n                    let lb = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"callout_enumerate rc {}\", show(pb)), ea, eb);\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"callout_enumerate log {}\", show(pb)), la, lb);\n                }\n                let mca = (p.c.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut());\n                let mcb = (p.r.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut());\n                assert_eq!((p.c.set_callout)(mca, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut()), 0);\n                assert_eq!((p.r.set_callout)(mcb, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut()), 0);\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    for &(mo, mn) in &[(0u32, \"none\"), (PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, \"NO_START_OPT\")] {\n                        let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                        let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                        CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                        let ra = (p.c.do_match)(a, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, mo, mda, mca);\n                        let la = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                        CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                        let rb = (p.r.do_match)(b, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, mo, mdb, mcb);\n                        let lb = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                        let tag =\n                            format!(\"callout match {} cfg[{}] subj={} {}\", show(pb), cfg.name, show(sb), mn);\n                        d.eq(&tag, read_match_out(&p.c, mda, ra), read_match_out(&p.r, mdb, rb));\n                        d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: callout log\"), la, lb);\n                        (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n                        (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n                    }\n                }\n                (p.c.match_context_free)(mca);\n                (p.r.match_context_free)(mcb);\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"callouts: explicit (?C..) and AUTO_CALLOUT, pcre2_callout_enumerate_8 + match-time sequence\");\n}\n\n// ================================================== bytecode-level internals\n\n/// Finds the unique occurrence of `op` in a compiled pattern's bytecode.\n/// Returns the byte offset from the bytecode start, or None if not unique.\nunsafe fn unique_op(code: Ptr, op: u8) -> Option<usize> {\n    let start = bytecode_ptr(code);\n    let n = code_blocksize(code) - (start as usize - code as usize);\n    let by = std::slice::from_raw_parts(start, n);\n    let mut found = None;\n    for i in 0..n.saturating_sub(3) {\n        if by[i] != op {\n            continue;\n        }\n        let link = ((by[i + 1] as usize) << 8) | by[i + 2] as usize; // LINK_SIZE == 2\n        if link >= 4 && i + link <= n {\n            if found.is_some() {\n                return None; // ambiguous\n            }\n            found = Some(i);\n        }\n    }\n    found\n}\n\nconst OP_XCLASS: u8 = 112;\nconst OP_ECLASS: u8 = 113;\n\n// CONFIGS row: _pcre2_xclass_8 and _pcre2_eclass_8 driven over every code point\n// class boundary, using real XCLASS/ECLASS bytecode produced by the compiler.\n#[test]\nfn xclass_and_eclass_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    // patterns that produce exactly one wide/extended class\n    let xpats: &[(&str, u32, u32)] = &[\n        (\"[\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{200}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[^\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{200}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\x{100}\\\\x{300}\\\\x{500}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[a-c\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{200}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{L}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\P{L}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{Greek}\\\\p{Nd}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{Lu}a-f]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{10ffff}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[[:alpha:]\\\\x{100}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"(?[\\\\p{L} & \\\\p{Greek}])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"(?[\\\\p{L} -- [a-z]])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"(?[[a-z] | \\\\p{Nd}])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"(?[\\\\p{L} ^ \\\\p{Lu}])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{Xan}\\\\x{2000}-\\\\x{2fff}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n    ];\n    // code points at and around every interesting boundary, plus a sweep\n    let mut cps: Vec<u32> = vec![\n        0, 1, 0x40, 0x41, 0x5a, 0x61, 0x7a, 0x7f, 0x80, 0xff, 0x100, 0x101, 0x1ff, 0x200, 0x201,\n        0x2ff, 0x300, 0x37f, 0x386, 0x3b1, 0x400, 0x2000, 0x2028, 0x2fff, 0xffff, 0x10000,\n        0x10ffff,\n    ];\n    for i in 0..2000u32 {\n        cps.push(i * 137 % 0x11_0000);\n    }\n    for &(pat, opts, xopts) in xpats {\n        let mut cfg = Cfg::new(\"xclass\", opts, xopts);\n        cfg.name = \"xclass probe\";\n        let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n        unsafe {\n            let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), &cfg, &mut d) else {\n                continue;\n            };\n            let sa = bytecode_ptr(a);\n            let sb = bytecode_ptr(b);\n            for (op, is_e) in [(OP_XCLASS, false), (OP_ECLASS, true)] {\n                let Some(off) = unique_op(a, op) else { continue };\n                assert_eq!(Some(off), unique_op(b, op), \"opcode offset differs for {pat}\");\n                for utf in [0 as Bool, 1] {\n                    for &c in &cps {\n                        let da = sa.add(off + 3); // skip opcode + LINK_SIZE\n                        let db = sb.add(off + 3);\n                        if is_e {\n                            let link = {\n                                let by = std::slice::from_raw_parts(sa.add(off), 3);\n                                ((by[1] as usize) << 8) | by[2] as usize\n                            };\n                            d.eq(\n                                &format!(\"eclass({c:#x}, {pat}, utf={utf})\"),\n                                (p.c.p_eclass)(c, da, sa.add(off + link), sa, utf),\n                                (p.r.p_eclass)(c, db, sb.add(off + link), sb, utf),\n                            );\n                        } else {\n                            d.eq(\n                                &format!(\"xclass({c:#x}, {pat}, utf={utf})\"),\n                                (p.c.p_xclass)(c, da, sa, utf),\n                                (p.r.p_xclass)(c, db, sb, utf),\n                            );\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            (p.c.code_free)(a);\n            (p.r.code_free)(b);\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"_pcre2_xclass_8 / _pcre2_eclass_8: real XCLASS/ECLASS bytecode x ~2000 code points x utf\");\n}\n\n// CONFIGS row: _pcre2_find_bracket_8 over real bytecode, for every group\n// number present plus out-of-range and negative numbers.\n#[test]\nfn find_bracket_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    for cfg in [\n        Cfg::new(\"default\", 0, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DUPNAMES\", PCRE2_DUPNAMES, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_AUTO_CAPTURE\", PCRE2_NO_AUTO_CAPTURE, 0),\n    ] {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), &cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                let (sa, sb) = (bytecode_ptr(a), bytecode_ptr(b));\n                let mut top = 0u32;\n                (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_CAPTURECOUNT, &mut top as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n                for utf in [0 as Bool, 1] {\n                    for num in -3i32..=(top as i32 + 3) {\n                        let ra = (p.c.p_find_bracket)(sa, utf, num);\n                        let rb = (p.r.p_find_bracket)(sb, utf, num);\n                        d.eq(\n                            &format!(\"find_bracket({} cfg[{}] n={num} utf={utf})\", show(pb), cfg.name),\n                            if ra.is_null() { None } else { Some(ra as usize - sa as usize) },\n                            if rb.is_null() { None } else { Some(rb as usize - sb as usize) },\n                        );\n                    }\n                }\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"_pcre2_find_bracket_8: real bytecode x group numbers -3..top+3 x utf on/off\");\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10579,"cache_read_input_tokens":148260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10579,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7","uuid":"d04faa72-dc1a-4562-927c-7c7ecf8b54fc","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:27:37.287Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011TD9CbcqPAJhuNa6yNvffE","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_compile_match.rs (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7","uuid":"7fcb8cba-5cde-42a3-9988-07a3efa90247","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:27:37.298Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_compile_match.rs","content":"// Phase B — the compile pipeline and both matchers, driven end to end the way\n// a real consumer does: build a compile context, set the options, compile, then\n// run the full match with a match context.\n//\n// The compiled bytecode is compared BYTE FOR BYTE, which is a far stronger\n// check than comparing match results alone: it transitively validates every\n// internal that only runs during compilation (the parser, `_pcre2_study_8`,\n// `_pcre2_auto_possessify_8`, `_pcre2_check_escape_8`, the class compilers, the\n// capture-group/name-table helpers), none of which can be called directly\n// without fabricating an internal `compile_block`.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::{c_int, c_void};\nuse std::ptr;\n\n/// One compile configuration: option bits plus compile-context state.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct Cfg {\n    pub name: &'static str,\n    pub opts: u32,\n    pub xopts: u32,\n    pub newline: u32,\n    pub bsr: u32,\n    pub varlookbehind: u32,\n    pub parens_limit: u32,\n    pub optimize: u32,\n    pub own_tables: bool,\n}\n\nimpl Cfg {\n    const fn new(name: &'static str, opts: u32, xopts: u32) -> Cfg {\n        Cfg {\n            name,\n            opts,\n            xopts,\n            newline: 0,\n            bsr: 0,\n            varlookbehind: 0,\n            parens_limit: 0,\n            optimize: u32::MAX,\n            own_tables: false,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// The configuration axes the C actually branches on, crossed.\nfn configs() -> Vec<Cfg> {\n    let mut v = vec![\n        Cfg::new(\"default\", 0, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"CASELESS\", PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"MULTILINE\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DOTALL\", PCRE2_DOTALL, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"EXTENDED\", PCRE2_EXTENDED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"EXTENDED_MORE\", PCRE2_EXTENDED | PCRE2_EXTENDED_MORE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UNGREEDY\", PCRE2_UNGREEDY, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DUPNAMES\", PCRE2_DUPNAMES, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_AUTO_CAPTURE\", PCRE2_NO_AUTO_CAPTURE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_AUTO_POSSESS\", PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\", PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR\", PCRE2_NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ANCHORED\", PCRE2_ANCHORED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ENDANCHORED\", PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ANCHORED|ENDANCHORED\", PCRE2_ANCHORED | PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DOLLAR_ENDONLY|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"FIRSTLINE\", PCRE2_FIRSTLINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_CIRCUMFLEX|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_BSUX\", PCRE2_ALT_BSUX, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_VERBNAMES\", PCRE2_ALT_VERBNAMES, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALLOW_EMPTY_CLASS\", PCRE2_ALLOW_EMPTY_CLASS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF\", PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"LITERAL\", PCRE2_LITERAL, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"LITERAL|CASELESS\", PCRE2_LITERAL | PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"AUTO_CALLOUT\", PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS\", PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        // --- UTF / UCP axis, the biggest behaviour switch in the library\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UCP\", PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|CASELESS\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP|CASELESS\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_CASELESS, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|MATCH_INVALID_UTF\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP|DOTALL|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_DOTALL | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0),\n        // --- EXTRA options\n        Cfg::new(\"X:CASELESS_RESTRICT\", PCRE2_CASELESS, PCRE2_EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT),\n        Cfg::new(\n            \"UTF|UCP|CASELESS + X:CASELESS_RESTRICT\",\n            PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_CASELESS,\n            PCRE2_EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT,\n        ),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:TURKISH_CASING\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_CASELESS, PCRE2_EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_BSD\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSD),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_BSS\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSS),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_BSW\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSW),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_POSIX\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_POSIX),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ASCII_DIGIT\", PCRE2_UCP, PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_DIGIT),\n        Cfg::new(\n            \"X:ASCII_all|UCP|UTF\",\n            PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_UTF,\n            PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSD | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSS | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_BSW\n                | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_POSIX | PCRE2_EXTRA_ASCII_DIGIT,\n        ),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:MATCH_WORD\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_WORD),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:MATCH_LINE\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_LINE),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:MATCH_LINE|MULTILINE\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_LINE),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ALT_BSUX\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALT_BSUX | PCRE2_ALT_BSUX * 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"ALT_BSUX + X:ALT_BSUX\", PCRE2_ALT_BSUX, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALT_BSUX),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:ALLOW_SURROGATE_ESCAPES|UTF\", PCRE2_UTF, PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_SURROGATE_ESCAPES),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:PYTHON_OCTAL\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_PYTHON_OCTAL),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:NO_BS0\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_NO_BS0),\n        Cfg::new(\"X:NEVER_CALLOUT\", 0, PCRE2_EXTRA_NEVER_CALLOUT),\n    ];\n    // --- newline convention axis (affects ., $, \\R, \\N and the CRLF scan)\n    for nl in [\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CR,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_LF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANYCRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_NUL,\n    ] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"MULTILINE + newline\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0);\n        c.newline = nl;\n        v.push(c);\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF|MULTILINE + newline\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0);\n        c.newline = nl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- \\R convention axis\n    for bsr in [PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE, PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"bsr\", 0, 0);\n        c.bsr = bsr;\n        v.push(c);\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF + bsr\", PCRE2_UTF, 0);\n        c.bsr = bsr;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- optimization directives (auto-possessify / start optimize on+off)\n    for opt in [\n        PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_NONE,\n        PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_FULL,\n        PCRE2_AUTO_POSSESS_OFF,\n        PCRE2_START_OPTIMIZE_OFF,\n    ] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"optimize\", 0, 0);\n        c.optimize = opt;\n        v.push(c);\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP + optimize\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0);\n        c.optimize = opt;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- variable lookbehind limit\n    for vl in [1u32, 2, 255] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"max_varlookbehind\", 0, 0);\n        c.varlookbehind = vl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- parens nest limit (drives PARENTHESES_NEST_TOO_DEEP)\n    for pl in [1u32, 3, 250] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"parens_nest_limit\", 0, 0);\n        c.parens_limit = pl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    // --- locale tables built by pcre2_maketables (vs the built-in defaults)\n    let mut c = Cfg::new(\"own tables (pcre2_maketables)\", 0, 0);\n    c.own_tables = true;\n    v.push(c);\n    let mut c = Cfg::new(\"own tables + CASELESS\", PCRE2_CASELESS, 0);\n    c.own_tables = true;\n    v.push(c);\n    v\n}\n\n/// A compile context configured per `Cfg`, plus the tables it owns.\nstruct Ctx {\n    ccontext: Ptr,\n    tables: *const u8,\n}\n\nunsafe fn make_ctx(api: &Api, cfg: &Cfg) -> Ctx {\n    let cc = (api.compile_context_create)(ptr::null_mut());\n    assert!(!cc.is_null(), \"[{}] compile_context_create failed\", api.name);\n    if cfg.newline != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_newline)(cc, cfg.newline), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.bsr != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_bsr)(cc, cfg.bsr), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.varlookbehind != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_max_varlookbehind)(cc, cfg.varlookbehind), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.parens_limit != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_parens_nest_limit)(cc, cfg.parens_limit), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.xopts != 0 {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_compile_extra_options)(cc, cfg.xopts), 0);\n    }\n    if cfg.optimize != u32::MAX {\n        assert_eq!((api.set_optimize)(cc, cfg.optimize), 0);\n    }\n    let mut tables = ptr::null();\n    if cfg.own_tables {\n        tables = (api.maketables)(ptr::null_mut());\n        assert!(!tables.is_null(), \"[{}] maketables failed\", api.name);\n        assert_eq!((api.set_character_tables)(cc, tables), 0);\n    }\n    Ctx { ccontext: cc, tables }\n}\n\nunsafe fn free_ctx(api: &Api, c: Ctx) {\n    (api.compile_context_free)(c.ccontext);\n    if !c.tables.is_null() {\n        (api.maketables_free)(ptr::null_mut(), c.tables);\n    }\n}\n\n/// Compile `pat` under `cfg` in both libraries.  Asserts the two agree on\n/// success/failure, on the error code and error offset, and (on success) that\n/// the produced bytecode is byte-identical.  Returns the two code objects.\nunsafe fn compile_both(p: &Pair, pat: &[u8], len: Sz, cfg: &Cfg, d: &mut Diffs) -> Option<(Ptr, Ptr)> {\n    let cc = make_ctx(&p.c, cfg);\n    let rc = make_ctx(&p.r, cfg);\n    let (mut eca, mut ecb) = (0 as c_int, 0 as c_int);\n    let (mut eoa, mut eob) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n    let a = (p.c.compile)(pat.as_ptr(), len, cfg.opts, &mut eca, &mut eoa, cc.ccontext);\n    let b = (p.r.compile)(pat.as_ptr(), len, cfg.opts, &mut ecb, &mut eob, rc.ccontext);\n    free_ctx(&p.c, cc);\n    free_ctx(&p.r, rc);\n\n    let tag = format!(\"compile({}) cfg[{}]\", show(pat), cfg.name);\n    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} null?\"), a.is_null(), b.is_null());\n    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} errorcode\"), eca, ecb);\n    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} erroroffset\"), eoa, eob);\n    if a.is_null() || b.is_null() {\n        if !a.is_null() {\n            (p.c.code_free)(a);\n        }\n        if !b.is_null() {\n            (p.r.code_free)(b);\n        }\n        return None;\n    }\n    assert_code_eq(a, b, &tag);\n    d.checked += 1;\n    Some((a, b))\n}\n\n// ============================================== compile: bytecode + info\n\n// CONFIGS rows: every Cfg x every pattern -> identical bytecode and identical\n// pattern_info for all 27 info ids.\n#[test]\nfn compile_bytecode_and_info_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let cfgs = configs();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    for cfg in &cfgs {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let b = pat.as_bytes();\n            // both explicit length and PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED\n            for &len in &[b.len(), PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED] {\n                if len == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED && b.contains(&0) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                unsafe {\n                    if let Some((a, bb)) = compile_both(p, b, len, cfg, &mut d) {\n                        compare_all_info(p, a, bb, &format!(\"{} cfg[{}]\", show(b), cfg.name), &mut d);\n                        (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                        (p.r.code_free)(bb);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    println!(\"compile configs={} patterns={}\", cfgs.len(), PATTERNS.len());\n    d.finish(\"compile: all Cfg x all PATTERNS x {explicit len, ZERO_TERMINATED}\");\n}\n\n/// `pcre2_pattern_info` for every info id, using the right result width.\nunsafe fn compare_all_info(p: &Pair, a: Ptr, b: Ptr, tag: &str, d: &mut Diffs) {\n    // uint32_t results\n    for what in [\n        PCRE2_INFO_ARGOPTIONS,\n        PCRE2_INFO_ALLOPTIONS,\n        PCRE2_INFO_EXTRAOPTIONS,\n        PCRE2_INFO_BACKREFMAX,\n        PCRE2_INFO_BSR,\n        PCRE2_INFO_CAPTURECOUNT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODEUNIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODETYPE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_HASCRORLF,\n        PCRE2_INFO_JCHANGED,\n        PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODEUNIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODETYPE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MATCHEMPTY,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MATCHLIMIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MAXLOOKBEHIND,\n        PCRE2_INFO_MINLENGTH,\n        PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_NEWLINE,\n        PCRE2_INFO_DEPTHLIMIT,\n        PCRE2_INFO_HASBACKSLASHC,\n        PCRE2_INFO_HEAPLIMIT,\n    ] {\n        let (mut va, mut vb) = (0xDEAD_BEEFu32, 0xDEAD_BEEFu32);\n        let ra = (p.c.pattern_info)(a, what, &mut va as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        let rb = (p.r.pattern_info)(b, what, &mut vb as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] rc {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] val {tag}\"), va, vb);\n    }\n    // PCRE2_SIZE results\n    for what in [PCRE2_INFO_SIZE, PCRE2_INFO_FRAMESIZE, PCRE2_INFO_JITSIZE] {\n        let (mut va, mut vb) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n        let ra = (p.c.pattern_info)(a, what, &mut va as *mut usize as Ptr);\n        let rb = (p.r.pattern_info)(b, what, &mut vb as *mut usize as Ptr);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] rc {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[{what}] val {tag}\"), va, vb);\n    }\n    // FIRSTBITMAP: pointer to a 32-byte table (or NULL)\n    {\n        let (mut pa, mut pb) = (ptr::null::<u8>(), ptr::null::<u8>());\n        let ra = (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBITMAP, &mut pa as *mut _ as Ptr);\n        let rb = (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBITMAP, &mut pb as *mut _ as Ptr);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[FIRSTBITMAP] rc {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"info[FIRSTBITMAP] null {tag}\"), pa.is_null(), pb.is_null());\n        if !pa.is_null() && !pb.is_null() {\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"info[FIRSTBITMAP] bytes {tag}\"),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(pa, 32).to_vec(),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(pb, 32).to_vec(),\n            );\n        }\n    }\n    // NAMETABLE: name_count entries of name_entry_size bytes\n    {\n        let (mut na, mut nb) = (0u32, 0u32);\n        (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT, &mut na as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT, &mut nb as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        let (mut sa, mut sb) = (0u32, 0u32);\n        (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE, &mut sa as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE, &mut sb as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n        if na == nb && sa == sb && na > 0 {\n            let (mut ta, mut tb) = (ptr::null::<u8>(), ptr::null::<u8>());\n            (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_NAMETABLE, &mut ta as *mut _ as Ptr);\n            (p.r.pattern_info)(b, PCRE2_INFO_NAMETABLE, &mut tb as *mut _ as Ptr);\n            let n = (na * sa) as usize;\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"info[NAMETABLE] {tag}\"),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(ta, n).to_vec(),\n                std::slice::from_raw_parts(tb, n).to_vec(),\n            );\n            // and the by-name lookups over that table\n            for i in 0..na {\n                let ent = ta.add((i * sa) as usize);\n                let name = ent.add(2); // 2-byte group number, then NUL-term name\n                d.eq(\n                    &format!(\"substring_number_from_name #{i} {tag}\"),\n                    (p.c.substring_number_from_name)(a, name),\n                    (p.r.substring_number_from_name)(b, name),\n                );\n                let (mut f1, mut l1) = (ptr::null(), ptr::null());\n                let (mut f2, mut l2) = (ptr::null(), ptr::null());\n                let ra = (p.c.substring_nametable_scan)(a, name, &mut f1, &mut l1);\n                let rb = (p.r.substring_nametable_scan)(b, name, &mut f2, &mut l2);\n                d.eq(&format!(\"nametable_scan rc #{i} {tag}\"), ra, rb);\n                if ra >= 0 && rb >= 0 {\n                    d.eq(\n                        &format!(\"nametable_scan span #{i} {tag}\"),\n                        (f1 as usize - ta as usize, l1 as usize - ta as usize),\n                        (f2 as usize - tb as usize, l2 as usize - tb as usize),\n                    );\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ============================================================ code_copy\n\n// CONFIGS row: pcre2_code_copy / pcre2_code_copy_with_tables must reproduce a\n// pattern that is byte-identical to the original and to the other library's.\n#[test]\nfn code_copy_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let cfgs = configs();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    for cfg in cfgs.iter().take(34) {\n        for pat in PATTERNS.iter().step_by(3) {\n            let b = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                if let Some((a, bb)) = compile_both(p, b, b.len(), cfg, &mut d) {\n                    let tag = format!(\"{} cfg[{}]\", show(b), cfg.name);\n                    let ca = (p.c.code_copy)(a);\n                    let cb = (p.r.code_copy)(bb);\n                    assert!(!ca.is_null() && !cb.is_null(), \"code_copy failed {tag}\");\n                    assert_code_eq(ca, cb, &format!(\"code_copy {tag}\"));\n                    assert_code_eq(a, ca, &format!(\"code_copy vs original (C) {tag}\"));\n                    let ta = (p.c.code_copy_with_tables)(a);\n                    let tb = (p.r.code_copy_with_tables)(bb);\n                    assert!(!ta.is_null() && !tb.is_null(), \"code_copy_with_tables failed {tag}\");\n                    assert_code_eq(ta, tb, &format!(\"code_copy_with_tables {tag}\"));\n                    d.checked += 2;\n                    (p.c.code_free)(ca);\n                    (p.r.code_free)(cb);\n                    (p.c.code_free)(ta);\n                    (p.r.code_free)(tb);\n                    (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                    (p.r.code_free)(bb);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_code_copy_8 / pcre2_code_copy_with_tables_8 over Cfg x patterns\");\n}\n\n// ================================================================= matching\n\n/// Runs `pcre2_match` in both libraries and compares rc, ovector, startchar,\n/// mark, and the derived match-data accessors.\nunsafe fn cmp_match(\n    p: &Pair,\n    a: Ptr,\n    b: Ptr,\n    subj: &[u8],\n    len: Sz,\n    start: Sz,\n    mopts: u32,\n    ovecsize: u32,\n    mctx: (Ptr, Ptr),\n    tag: &str,\n    d: &mut Diffs,\n) {\n    let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(ovecsize, ptr::null_mut());\n    let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(ovecsize, ptr::null_mut());\n    let ra = (p.c.do_match)(a, subj.as_ptr(), len, start, mopts, mda, mctx.0);\n    let rb = (p.r.do_match)(b, subj.as_ptr(), len, start, mopts, mdb, mctx.1);\n    let oa = read_match_out(&p.c, mda, ra);\n    let ob = read_match_out(&p.r, mdb, rb);\n    d.eq(tag, oa, ob);\n    d.eq(\n        &format!(\"{tag} :: ovector_count\"),\n        (p.c.get_ovector_count)(mda),\n        (p.r.get_ovector_count)(mdb),\n    );\n    d.eq(\n        &format!(\"{tag} :: match_data_size\"),\n        (p.c.get_match_data_size)(mda),\n        (p.r.get_match_data_size)(mdb),\n    );\n    d.eq(\n        &format!(\"{tag} :: heapframes_size\"),\n        (p.c.get_match_data_heapframes_size)(mda),\n        (p.r.get_match_data_heapframes_size)(mdb),\n    );\n    // substring accessors over the result\n    if ra > 0 && rb > 0 {\n        for i in 0..(ra.max(rb) as u32 + 1) {\n            let (mut la, mut lb) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"{tag} :: substring_length_bynumber({i}) rc\"),\n                (p.c.substring_length_bynumber)(mda, i, &mut la),\n                (p.r.substring_length_bynumber)(mdb, i, &mut lb),\n            );\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_length_bynumber({i}) len\"), la, lb);\n            let mut ba = [0u8; 256];\n            let mut bb = [0u8; 256];\n            let (mut ca, mut cb) = (ba.len(), bb.len());\n            d.eq(\n                &format!(\"{tag} :: substring_copy_bynumber({i}) rc\"),\n                (p.c.substring_copy_bynumber)(mda, i, ba.as_mut_ptr(), &mut ca),\n                (p.r.substring_copy_bynumber)(mdb, i, bb.as_mut_ptr(), &mut cb),\n            );\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_copy_bynumber({i}) out\"), (ba, ca), (bb, cb));\n            let (mut pa, mut pb) = (ptr::null_mut::<u8>(), ptr::null_mut::<u8>());\n            let (mut na, mut nb) = (usize::MAX, usize::MAX);\n            let ga = (p.c.substring_get_bynumber)(mda, i, &mut pa, &mut na);\n            let gb = (p.r.substring_get_bynumber)(mdb, i, &mut pb, &mut nb);\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_get_bynumber({i}) rc\"), ga, gb);\n            d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_get_bynumber({i}) len\"), na, nb);\n            if ga == 0 && gb == 0 {\n                d.eq(\n                    &format!(\"{tag} :: substring_get_bynumber({i}) bytes\"),\n                    std::slice::from_raw_parts(pa, na + 1).to_vec(),\n                    std::slice::from_raw_parts(pb, nb + 1).to_vec(),\n                );\n            }\n            if !pa.is_null() {\n                (p.c.substring_free)(pa);\n            }\n            if !pb.is_null() {\n                (p.r.substring_free)(pb);\n            }\n        }\n        // whole-list variant\n        let (mut la, mut lb) = (ptr::null_mut(), ptr::null_mut());\n        let (mut sa, mut sb) = (ptr::null_mut(), ptr::null_mut());\n        let ra2 = (p.c.substring_list_get)(mda, &mut la, &mut sa);\n        let rb2 = (p.r.substring_list_get)(mdb, &mut lb, &mut sb);\n        d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: substring_list_get rc\"), ra2, rb2);\n        if ra2 == 0 && rb2 == 0 {\n            let n = ra.max(rb) as usize + 1;\n            for i in 0..n {\n                let (x, y) = (*la.add(i), *lb.add(i));\n                let (nx, ny) = (*sa.add(i), *sb.add(i));\n                d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: list[{i}] len\"), nx, ny);\n                if nx == ny {\n                    d.eq(\n                        &format!(\"{tag} :: list[{i}] bytes\"),\n                        std::slice::from_raw_parts(x, nx).to_vec(),\n                        std::slice::from_raw_parts(y, ny).to_vec(),\n                    );\n                }\n            }\n            (p.c.substring_list_free)(la);\n            (p.r.substring_list_free)(lb);\n        }\n    }\n    (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n    (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n}\n\n/// Match options crossed over the axes `pcre2_match` branches on.\nconst MOPTS: &[(u32, &str)] = &[\n    (0, \"none\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTBOL, \"NOTBOL\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTEOL, \"NOTEOL\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTBOL | PCRE2_NOTEOL, \"NOTBOL|NOTEOL\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY, \"NOTEMPTY\"),\n    (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, \"NOTEMPTY_ATSTART\"),\n    (PCRE2_ANCHORED, \"ANCHORED\"),\n    (PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, \"ENDANCHORED\"),\n    (PCRE2_ANCHORED | PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, \"ANCHORED|ENDANCHORED\"),\n    (PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT, \"PARTIAL_SOFT\"),\n    (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD, \"PARTIAL_HARD\"),\n    (PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, \"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\"),\n    (PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK, \"NO_UTF_CHECK\"),\n    (PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT, \"COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT\"),\n    (PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK, \"DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK\"),\n    (PCRE2_NO_JIT, \"NO_JIT\"),\n];\n\n/// Compile configurations used for matching (a representative spread; the full\n/// set is covered by the bytecode test above).\nfn match_cfgs() -> Vec<Cfg> {\n    let all = configs();\n    let names = [\n        \"default\",\n        \"CASELESS\",\n        \"MULTILINE\",\n        \"DOTALL\",\n        \"UNGREEDY\",\n        \"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\",\n        \"NO_AUTO_POSSESS\",\n        \"ANCHORED\",\n        \"ENDANCHORED\",\n        \"FIRSTLINE\",\n        \"MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF\",\n        \"AUTO_CALLOUT\",\n        \"UTF\",\n        \"UCP\",\n        \"UTF|UCP\",\n        \"UTF|CASELESS\",\n        \"UTF|UCP|CASELESS\",\n        \"UTF|MATCH_INVALID_UTF\",\n        \"UTF|UCP|DOTALL|MULTILINE\",\n        \"X:CASELESS_RESTRICT\",\n        \"X:TURKISH_CASING\",\n        \"X:ASCII_all|UCP|UTF\",\n        \"X:MATCH_WORD\",\n        \"X:MATCH_LINE\",\n        \"own tables (pcre2_maketables)\",\n    ];\n    let mut v: Vec<Cfg> = all\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|c| names.contains(&c.name))\n        .cloned()\n        .collect();\n    // plus each newline convention with MULTILINE, and both \\R conventions\n    for nl in [\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CR,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_LF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANYCRLF,\n        PCRE2_NEWLINE_NUL,\n    ] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"MULTILINE + newline\", PCRE2_MULTILINE, 0);\n        c.newline = nl;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    for bsr in [PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE, PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF] {\n        let mut c = Cfg::new(\"UTF + bsr\", PCRE2_UTF, 0);\n        c.bsr = bsr;\n        v.push(c);\n    }\n    v\n}\n\n// CONFIGS rows: pcre2_match over (compile cfg) x (pattern) x (subject) x\n// (match options) x (startoffset) x (ovector size).\n#[test]\nfn match_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(100);\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    // Bound the run: deterministic limits so both libraries hit them alike.\n    let mca = unsafe { (p.c.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    let mcb = unsafe { (p.r.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    unsafe {\n        for (m, v) in [(&p.c, mca), (&p.r, mcb)] {\n            assert_eq!((m.set_match_limit)(v, 20_000), 0);\n            assert_eq!((m.set_depth_limit)(v, 2_000), 0);\n            assert_eq!((m.set_heap_limit)(v, 200), 0);\n        }\n    }\n    for cfg in &match_cfgs() {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    // a random slice of the option/offset/ovector axes per\n                    // (pattern, subject) keeps the run bounded while still\n                    // covering every axis many thousands of times overall\n                    for _ in 0..3 {\n                        let (mo, mn) = MOPTS[rng.below(MOPTS.len())];\n                        let start = if sb.is_empty() { 0 } else { rng.below(sb.len() + 1) };\n                        let ovec = *rng.pick(&[0u32, 1, 2, 4, 16, 64]);\n                        let len = if rng.chance(4) && !sb.contains(&0) {\n                            PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED\n                        } else {\n                            sb.len()\n                        };\n                        let tag = format!(\n                            \"match {} cfg[{}] subj={} start={} mopts={} ovec={} len={}\",\n                            show(pb),\n                            cfg.name,\n                            show(sb),\n                            start,\n                            mn,\n                            ovec,\n                            if len == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED { \"ZT\".into() } else { len.to_string() }\n                        );\n                        cmp_match(p, a, b, sb, len, start, mo, ovec, (mca, mcb), &tag, &mut d);\n                    }\n                }\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    unsafe {\n        (p.c.match_context_free)(mca);\n        (p.r.match_context_free)(mcb);\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_match_8: match_cfgs x PATTERNS x SUBJECTS x MOPTS x startoffset x ovector size\");\n}\n\n// CONFIGS rows: pcre2_dfa_match over the same axes, plus DFA_SHORTEST,\n// DFA_RESTART and workspace sizes.\n#[test]\nfn dfa_match_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(200);\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    let mca = unsafe { (p.c.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    let mcb = unsafe { (p.r.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut()) };\n    unsafe {\n        for (m, v) in [(&p.c, mca), (&p.r, mcb)] {\n            assert_eq!((m.set_match_limit)(v, 20_000), 0);\n            assert_eq!((m.set_depth_limit)(v, 2_000), 0);\n        }\n    }\n    let dfa_opts: &[(u32, &str)] = &[\n        (0, \"none\"),\n        (PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST, \"DFA_SHORTEST\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTBOL, \"NOTBOL\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTEOL, \"NOTEOL\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY, \"NOTEMPTY\"),\n        (PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, \"NOTEMPTY_ATSTART\"),\n        (PCRE2_ANCHORED, \"ANCHORED\"),\n        (PCRE2_ENDANCHORED, \"ENDANCHORED\"),\n        (PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT, \"PARTIAL_SOFT\"),\n        (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD, \"PARTIAL_HARD\"),\n        (PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, \"NO_START_OPTIMIZE\"),\n        (PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK, \"NO_UTF_CHECK\"),\n        (PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT, \"COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT\"),\n    ];\n    for cfg in &match_cfgs() {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    for _ in 0..3 {\n                        let (mo, mn) = dfa_opts[rng.below(dfa_opts.len())];\n                        let start = if sb.is_empty() { 0 } else { rng.below(sb.len() + 1) };\n                        let ovec = *rng.pick(&[0u32, 1, 2, 4, 16]);\n                        // include a deliberately tiny workspace to reach\n                        // PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE identically\n                        let wsn = *rng.pick(&[20usize, 100, 1000]);\n                        let mut wa = vec![0 as c_int; wsn];\n                        let mut wb = vec![0 as c_int; wsn];\n                        let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(ovec, ptr::null_mut());\n                        let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(ovec, ptr::null_mut());\n                        let ra = (p.c.dfa_match)(\n                            a, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), start, mo, mda, mca, wa.as_mut_ptr(), wsn,\n                        );\n                        let rb = (p.r.dfa_match)(\n                            b, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), start, mo, mdb, mcb, wb.as_mut_ptr(), wsn,\n                        );\n                        let tag = format!(\n                            \"dfa_match {} cfg[{}] subj={} start={} opts={} ovec={} ws={}\",\n                            show(pb), cfg.name, show(sb), start, mn, ovec, wsn\n                        );\n                        d.eq(&tag, read_match_out(&p.c, mda, ra), read_match_out(&p.r, mdb, rb));\n                        (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n                        (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n                    }\n                }\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    unsafe {\n        (p.c.match_context_free)(mca);\n        (p.r.match_context_free)(mcb);\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_dfa_match_8: match_cfgs x PATTERNS x SUBJECTS x dfa options x workspace sizes\");\n}\n\n// CONFIGS row: pcre2_next_match_8 — iterating the alternative match ends that\n// pcre2_dfa_match records in the ovector.\n#[test]\nfn next_match_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    let cfgs = match_cfgs();\n    for cfg in cfgs.iter().take(20) {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    let mut ws_a = vec![0 as c_int; 1000];\n                    let mut ws_b = vec![0 as c_int; 1000];\n                    let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                    let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                    let ra = (p.c.dfa_match)(\n                        a, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, 0, mda, ptr::null_mut(), ws_a.as_mut_ptr(), 1000,\n                    );\n                    let rb = (p.r.dfa_match)(\n                        b, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, 0, mdb, ptr::null_mut(), ws_b.as_mut_ptr(), 1000,\n                    );\n                    let tag = format!(\"next_match {} cfg[{}] subj={}\", show(pb), cfg.name, show(sb));\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} dfa rc\"), ra, rb);\n                    // walk the whole iterator to exhaustion in both\n                    let mut steps_a = Vec::new();\n                    let mut steps_b = Vec::new();\n                    loop {\n                        let (mut o, mut f) = (usize::MAX, 0u32);\n                        let rc = (p.c.next_match)(mda, &mut o, &mut f);\n                        steps_a.push((rc, o, f));\n                        if rc <= 0 || steps_a.len() > 40 {\n                            break;\n                        }\n                    }\n                    loop {\n                        let (mut o, mut f) = (usize::MAX, 0u32);\n                        let rc = (p.r.next_match)(mdb, &mut o, &mut f);\n                        steps_b.push((rc, o, f));\n                        if rc <= 0 || steps_b.len() > 40 {\n                            break;\n                        }\n                    }\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} next_match sequence\"), steps_a, steps_b);\n                    (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n                    (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n                }\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"pcre2_next_match_8: full iteration after pcre2_dfa_match over cfgs x patterns x subjects\");\n}\n\n// =========================================================== callouts\n\nstatic mut CALLOUT_LOG: Vec<u8> = Vec::new();\n\n/// Records the fields of every callout block so the two libraries' callout\n/// sequences can be compared exactly.  Layout mirrors `pcre2_callout_block`.\n#[repr(C)]\nstruct CalloutBlock {\n    version: u32,\n    callout_number: u32,\n    capture_top: u32,\n    capture_last: u32,\n    offset_vector: *const Sz,\n    mark: Sptr,\n    subject: Sptr,\n    subject_length: Sz,\n    start_match: Sz,\n    current_position: Sz,\n    pattern_position: Sz,\n    next_item_length: Sz,\n    callout_string_offset: Sz,\n    callout_string_length: Sz,\n    callout_string: Sptr,\n    callout_flags: u32,\n}\n\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn record_callout(blk: *mut c_void, _data: *mut c_void) -> c_int {\n    let b = &*(blk as *const CalloutBlock);\n    let log = &mut *ptr::addr_of_mut!(CALLOUT_LOG);\n    for v in [\n        b.version as u64,\n        b.callout_number as u64,\n        b.capture_top as u64,\n        b.capture_last as u64,\n        b.subject_length as u64,\n        b.start_match as u64,\n        b.current_position as u64,\n        b.pattern_position as u64,\n        b.next_item_length as u64,\n        b.callout_string_offset as u64,\n        b.callout_string_length as u64,\n        b.callout_flags as u64,\n        b.mark.is_null() as u64,\n    ] {\n        log.extend_from_slice(&v.to_le_bytes());\n    }\n    if !b.callout_string.is_null() {\n        log.extend_from_slice(std::slice::from_raw_parts(\n            b.callout_string,\n            b.callout_string_length,\n        ));\n    }\n    0\n}\n\n// CONFIGS rows: match-time callouts, with AUTO_CALLOUT and with explicit\n// (?C) / (?C1) / (?C{str}) callouts — the whole callout sequence must match.\n#[test]\nfn callouts_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    let cal_pats: &[&str] = &[\n        \"a(?C)b\",\n        \"a(?C1)b\",\n        \"a(?C255)b\",\n        \"a(?C{txt})b\",\n        \"(?C0)a(?C1)b(?C2)c\",\n        \"(a)(?C)(b)\",\n        \"\\\\d+(?C9)\\\\w*\",\n        \"(?:a(?C)|b(?C))+\",\n        \"^(?C)a*(?C)$\",\n    ];\n    for cfg in [\n        Cfg::new(\"default\", 0, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"AUTO_CALLOUT\", PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|AUTO_CALLOUT\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF|UCP\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n    ] {\n        // AUTO_CALLOUT applies to every pattern, so use the full corpus there\n        let pats: Vec<&str> = if cfg.opts & PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT != 0 {\n            PATTERNS.iter().copied().collect()\n        } else {\n            cal_pats.iter().copied().collect()\n        };\n        for pat in pats {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), &cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                // pcre2_callout_enumerate walks the compiled pattern\n                {\n                    CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                    let ea = (p.c.callout_enumerate)(a, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut());\n                    let la = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                    CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                    let eb = (p.r.callout_enumerate)(b, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut());\n                    let lb = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"callout_enumerate rc {}\", show(pb)), ea, eb);\n                    d.eq(&format!(\"callout_enumerate log {}\", show(pb)), la, lb);\n                }\n                let mca = (p.c.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut());\n                let mcb = (p.r.match_context_create)(ptr::null_mut());\n                assert_eq!((p.c.set_callout)(mca, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut()), 0);\n                assert_eq!((p.r.set_callout)(mcb, Some(record_callout), ptr::null_mut()), 0);\n                for subj in SUBJECTS {\n                    let sb = subj.as_bytes();\n                    for &(mo, mn) in &[(0u32, \"none\"), (PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, \"NO_START_OPT\")] {\n                        let mda = (p.c.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                        let mdb = (p.r.match_data_create)(16, ptr::null_mut());\n                        CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                        let ra = (p.c.do_match)(a, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, mo, mda, mca);\n                        let la = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                        CALLOUT_LOG.clear();\n                        let rb = (p.r.do_match)(b, sb.as_ptr(), sb.len(), 0, mo, mdb, mcb);\n                        let lb = CALLOUT_LOG.clone();\n                        let tag =\n                            format!(\"callout match {} cfg[{}] subj={} {}\", show(pb), cfg.name, show(sb), mn);\n                        d.eq(&tag, read_match_out(&p.c, mda, ra), read_match_out(&p.r, mdb, rb));\n                        d.eq(&format!(\"{tag} :: callout log\"), la, lb);\n                        (p.c.match_data_free)(mda);\n                        (p.r.match_data_free)(mdb);\n                    }\n                }\n                (p.c.match_context_free)(mca);\n                (p.r.match_context_free)(mcb);\n                (p.c.code_free)(a);\n                (p.r.code_free)(b);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"callouts: explicit (?C..) and AUTO_CALLOUT, pcre2_callout_enumerate_8 + match-time sequence\");\n}\n\n// ================================================== bytecode-level internals\n\n/// Finds the unique occurrence of `op` in a compiled pattern's bytecode.\n/// Returns the byte offset from the bytecode start, or None if not unique.\nunsafe fn unique_op(code: Ptr, op: u8) -> Option<usize> {\n    let start = bytecode_ptr(code);\n    let n = code_blocksize(code) - (start as usize - code as usize);\n    let by = std::slice::from_raw_parts(start, n);\n    let mut found = None;\n    for i in 0..n.saturating_sub(3) {\n        if by[i] != op {\n            continue;\n        }\n        let link = ((by[i + 1] as usize) << 8) | by[i + 2] as usize; // LINK_SIZE == 2\n        if link >= 4 && i + link <= n {\n            if found.is_some() {\n                return None; // ambiguous\n            }\n            found = Some(i);\n        }\n    }\n    found\n}\n\nconst OP_XCLASS: u8 = 112;\nconst OP_ECLASS: u8 = 113;\n\n// CONFIGS row: _pcre2_xclass_8 and _pcre2_eclass_8 driven over every code point\n// class boundary, using real XCLASS/ECLASS bytecode produced by the compiler.\n#[test]\nfn xclass_and_eclass_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    // patterns that produce exactly one wide/extended class\n    let xpats: &[(&str, u32, u32)] = &[\n        (\"[\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{200}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[^\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{200}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\x{100}\\\\x{300}\\\\x{500}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[a-c\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{200}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{L}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\P{L}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{Greek}\\\\p{Nd}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{Lu}a-f]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\x{100}-\\\\x{10ffff}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"[[:alpha:]\\\\x{100}]\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        (\"(?[\\\\p{L} & \\\\p{Greek}])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"(?[\\\\p{L} -- [a-z]])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"(?[[a-z] | \\\\p{Nd}])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"(?[\\\\p{L} ^ \\\\p{Lu}])\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP | PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, 0),\n        (\"[\\\\p{Xan}\\\\x{2000}-\\\\x{2fff}]\", PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_UCP, 0),\n    ];\n    // code points at and around every interesting boundary, plus a sweep\n    let mut cps: Vec<u32> = vec![\n        0, 1, 0x40, 0x41, 0x5a, 0x61, 0x7a, 0x7f, 0x80, 0xff, 0x100, 0x101, 0x1ff, 0x200, 0x201,\n        0x2ff, 0x300, 0x37f, 0x386, 0x3b1, 0x400, 0x2000, 0x2028, 0x2fff, 0xffff, 0x10000,\n        0x10ffff,\n    ];\n    for i in 0..2000u32 {\n        cps.push(i * 137 % 0x11_0000);\n    }\n    for &(pat, opts, xopts) in xpats {\n        let mut cfg = Cfg::new(\"xclass\", opts, xopts);\n        cfg.name = \"xclass probe\";\n        let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n        unsafe {\n            let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), &cfg, &mut d) else {\n                continue;\n            };\n            let sa = bytecode_ptr(a);\n            let sb = bytecode_ptr(b);\n            for (op, is_e) in [(OP_XCLASS, false), (OP_ECLASS, true)] {\n                let Some(off) = unique_op(a, op) else { continue };\n                assert_eq!(Some(off), unique_op(b, op), \"opcode offset differs for {pat}\");\n                for utf in [0 as Bool, 1] {\n                    for &c in &cps {\n                        let da = sa.add(off + 3); // skip opcode + LINK_SIZE\n                        let db = sb.add(off + 3);\n                        if is_e {\n                            let link = {\n                                let by = std::slice::from_raw_parts(sa.add(off), 3);\n                                ((by[1] as usize) << 8) | by[2] as usize\n                            };\n                            d.eq(\n                                &format!(\"eclass({c:#x}, {pat}, utf={utf})\"),\n                                (p.c.p_eclass)(c, da, sa.add(off + link), sa, utf),\n                                (p.r.p_eclass)(c, db, sb.add(off + link), sb, utf),\n                            );\n                        } else {\n                            d.eq(\n                                &format!(\"xclass({c:#x}, {pat}, utf={utf})\"),\n                                (p.c.p_xclass)(c, da, sa, utf),\n                                (p.r.p_xclass)(c, db, sb, utf),\n                            );\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            (p.c.code_free)(a);\n            (p.r.code_free)(b);\n        }\n    }\n    d.finish(\"_pcre2_xclass_8 / _pcre2_eclass_8: real XCLASS/ECLASS bytecode x ~2000 code points x utf\");\n}\n\n// CONFIGS row: _pcre2_find_bracket_8 over real bytecode, for every group\n// number present plus out-of-range and negative numbers.\n#[test]\nfn find_bracket_identical() {\n    let p = pair();\n    let mut d = Diffs::new();\n    for cfg in [\n        Cfg::new(\"default\", 0, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"UTF\", PCRE2_UTF, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"DUPNAMES\", PCRE2_DUPNAMES, 0),\n        Cfg::new(\"NO_AUTO_CAPTURE\", PCRE2_NO_AUTO_CAPTURE, 0),\n    ] {\n        for pat in PATTERNS {\n            let pb = pat.as_bytes();\n            unsafe {\n                let Some((a, b)) = compile_both(p, pb, pb.len(), &cfg, &mut d) else {\n                    continue;\n                };\n                let (sa, sb) = (bytecode_ptr(a), bytecode_ptr(b));\n                let mut top = 0u32;\n                (p.c.pattern_info)(a, PCRE2_INFO_CAPTURECOUNT, &mut top as *mut u32 as Ptr);\n                for utf in [0 as Bool, 1] {\n                    for num in -3i32..=(top as i32 + 3) {\n                        let ra = (p.c.p_find_bracket)(sa, utf, num);\n                        let rb = (p.r.p_find_bracket)(sb, utf, num);\n      