hy it is unreachable, plus an assertion that C and Rust agree on the nearest reachable input.\n\n## Rules\n- Fix `src/*.rs` if (and only if) you find a genuine C-vs-Rust divergence; rebuild with `cargo build --release`. Report every such fix precisely. Do NOT touch `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT weaken or delete an assertion to make a failure go away.\n- Run `timeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_c_compile -- --test-threads=1` and iterate until it passes.\n- If the process dies with no message, the Rust `.so` panicked (`panic = \"abort\"`); isolate with `--exact <testname>`.\n\n## Final report must state\n- the exact command you ran and its final PASS output,\n- `grep -o 'rows: &\\[[0-9, ]*\\]' tests/phase_c_compile.rs | grep -o '[0-9]\\+' | sort -n -u | wc -l` and confirmation that the covered set is exactly 1..221,\n- every `src/*.rs` fix you made (file, what was wrong, what the C does),\n- every `ERRORS.md` cell you corrected and why.","uuid":"311186a9-6f4e-4fbb-84c2-9e6a55a2a7ea","session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7"}
