apacity\n    expect: i32,            // documented return code\n}\n```\n\nThe `pcre2_substitute` replacement mini-language is the densest part of this section. Make sure you cover each distinct trigger separately:\n- the 9 distinct `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPLACEMENT` (-35) branches,\n- the 8 distinct `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE` (-57) branches,\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE` (-58),\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSTITUTION` (-59), `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSPATTERN` (-60),\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOMANYREPLACE` (-61),\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING` (-49) / `PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` (-50) / `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` (-55) and how `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNKNOWN_UNSET` / `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNSET_EMPTY` change them,\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (-48) and the `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_OVERFLOW_LENGTH` variant (buffer too small: with and without the flag; assert the returned required length matches),\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE` (-69) and `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOLARGEREPLACE` (-70),\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` (-75), `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` (-76),\n- the six `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` consistency checks: `PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSPATTERN` (-71), `DIFFSUBSSUBJECT` (-72), `DIFFSUBSOFFSET` (-73), `DIFFSUBSOPTIONS` (-74) — build a match_data with one (pattern, subject, offset, options) and then call substitute with a DIFFERENT one,\n- generic boundaries: NULL `code`, NULL `subject` with non-zero length, NULL `replacement`, NULL `outlengthptr`, NULL output buffer, `outlength` 0, `startoffset > length`, every reserved option bit set individually (loop all 32 bit positions) and `0xFFFFFFFF`, invalid UTF-8 in subject and in replacement with and without `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`.\n- a substitute callout that returns a non-zero / negative value (that is how a callout aborts a substitution) and a case callout that reports \"not enough room\" — assert both libraries propagate identically. Copy the EXACT `pcre2_substitute_callout_block` layout from `c_src/include/pcre2.h` (note the padding after the leading `uint32_t version`); `tests/phase_b_a