{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fwhb7jnygvcdqq3256zt23iaegjytb7ublsl32paupyoyeshmrea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md` is written and validated. Nothing in `c_src/` was touched.\n\n## Row count\n`grep -c '^| [0-9]' CONFIGS.md` → **456**\n\nStructure checks all pass: numbering is 1..456 with no gaps or duplicates; all 456 rows are exactly 4 well-formed columns ending in a literal `[ ]` checkbox (verified after normalising the `\\|` escapes); 12 `###` subsections each carry their own header + separator row; all **143** exported symbols from `SYMBOLS.md` are named somewhere in the table.\n\nDistribution: compile 153, match 140, dfa_match 28, substitute 30, substring 13, pattern_info 8, serialize 7, convert 15, context 12, low-level helpers 38, tables 7, jit stubs 5.\n\nNote on the count: it exceeds the 150–300 expectation by ~50%. That came from the explicit instruction to bias toward the low-level exported entry points *without* dropping the option cross-products — 31 compile option bits × 17 EXTRA bits × 24 start-of-pattern verbs × 6 newline conventions on the compile side alone. I merged aggressively wherever the C shares a branch (e.g. one row for the 27-cell quantifier grid, one for all 14 POSIX classes under UCP, one for all 13 `PT_*` types), so further reduction would mean collapsing genuinely distinct code paths into cells too coarse to sign off in Phase B. Compile+match at 64% of rows tracks the 63% of non-data C source they occupy.\n\n## Axes with the most interaction risk\n\nThe highest-risk clusters are all places where **two independently-set flags reach the same branch through different fields**. First, `UTF × UCP × CASELESS × EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT × EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING`: these decide between `OP_CHARI`, `OP_PROP/PT_CLIST`, and the `REFI_FLAG_*` byte on `OP_REFI`/`OP_DNREFI`, and 8-bit has a UCP-without-UTF path (`first_cu > 127 && ucp && !utf` ⇒ `UCD_OTHERCASE`) that exists in no other width — and `pcre2_substitute` deliberately does *not* consult `TURKISH_CASING` at all, so its casing diverges from matching. Second, the **start-of-match optimization block** × `{anchored, firstline, startline, has_first_cu, start_bits, has_req_cu, minlength} × partial × MATCH_INVALID_UTF`: the strict `else if` precedence (`has_first_cu` > `startline` > `start_bits`), the `memchr_found_first_cu`/`_cu2` caches that survive bumpalong iterations but are reset on `FRAGMENT_RESTART`, and the fact that some checks compare against the firstline-clamped `end_subject` while others compare against `mb->end_subject`, make this the densest source of off-by-one and stale-state bugs. Third, **`ovector` sizing × capture participation × `\\K`**: `rc == 0` means \"matched but too small\", slots above `top_bracket+1` are left stale, slots above `Foffset_top` are explicitly `PCRE2_UNSET`, partial matches write only pair 0, and DFA reuses the ovector for many *ends* of one start with the count latched to 0 once it overflows — four different contracts on the same array. Fourth, **newline convention × BSR × partial**, where `IS_NEWLINE` under ANY/ANYCRLF *writes back* `mb->nllen` and `OP_EODN`/`OP_DOLL` read it immediately afterwards, and where the CRLF bumpalong skip is additionally gated on `PCRE2_HASCRORLF`. Fifth, **`MATCH_INVALID_UTF` fragmentation** interacting with `check_subject`, `start_subject`, `true_end_subject` and the per-fragment `NOTBOL`/`NOTEOL` synthesis — `\\A`, `\\G`, `\\z`, `\\Z` and lookbehind each use a *different* floor/ceiling pointer. Sixth, on the substitute side, **case forcing × case callout × OVERFLOW_LENGTH**: with a callout the transform is deferred and re-applied in place over everything emitted since the escape, and the `(len>>3)+10` pessimistic inflation means the documented two-call sizing protocol is not guaranteed to converge. Finally, `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` is