lus one-too-small, and `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_OVERFLOW_LENGTH` reporting the full required length. Note the row about the `(len>>3)+10` pessimistic inflation meaning the protocol need not converge — assert whatever the C does.\n- case forcing interacting with `pcre2_set_substitute_case_callout_8` (the transform is deferred and re-applied in place) and with `OVERFLOW_LENGTH`. Also note that `pcre2_substitute` does NOT consult `PCRE2_EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING`, so its casing differs from matching — test a Turkish-casing pattern both ways and assert the C's behaviour.\n- `pcre2_set_substitute_callout_8`: compare the whole callback sequence, recording every field of `pcre2_substitute_callout_block` (exact layout from `c_src/include/pcre2.h`, note the padding after the leading `uint32_t version`), including a callout that returns a positive and a negative value.\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` reusing a pre-filled match_data.\n- UTF subjects and replacements, empty matches with GLOBAL (the anchored-retry dance), and `\\K` in the pattern.\n\nWhere a row names an expected outcome explicitly, ALSO assert the C produces it. If the C does not, the row was mis-derived — **the C is ground truth**: keep the C-vs-Rust assertion, correct that row's `configuration` cell in `CONFIGS.md`, and report it.\n\n**Use MANY randomized inputs per row, not one hand-picked value**, with a FIXED seed (`Rng::new(<constant>)`).\n\n## Rules\n- Fix `src/*.rs` if (and only if) you find a genuine C-vs-Rust divergence; rebuild with `cargo build --release`. Report every fix precisely. NEVER touch `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT weaken or delete an assertion to make a failure go away.\n- Set deterministic match/depth/heap limits so runaway patterns cannot hang the test; keep total runtime well under 600 s.\n- Run `timeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_b_cfg_dfa_subst -- --test-threads=1` and iterate until it passes.\n- If the process dies with no message, the Rust `.so` panicked (`panic = \"abort\"`); isolate with `--exact <testname>`.\n- Then run `timeout 300 python3 check_coverage.py` and confirm your file contributes rows 294..351.\n\n## Final report must state\n- the exact commands run and the final PASS output,\n- the `check_coverage.py` CONFIGS line showing your rows covered,\n- every `src/*.rs` fix (file, what was wrong, what the C does),\n- every `CONFIGS.md` cell you corrected and why.","uuid":"b59284a7-cd67-442f-81a1-0313e56e536d","session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7"}
