## What each test must do\nFor each row: set up its exact named configuration, call the function in BOTH libraries through their `.so`, and compare every observable.\n\n- For `pcre2_dfa_match_8` use `read_match_out_of(api, md, rc, Engine::Dfa)` — it reads only the fields the C defines for a DFA return code (`pcre2_dfa_match_8` never assigns `startchar` on NOMATCH, for instance). Do NOT read the ovector yourself.\n- For `pcre2_substitute_8` compare the return code, the value written back through `outlengthptr`, and the FULL output buffer including the bytes past the written region (so a buffer overrun is caught).\n\nMake sure each of these is genuinely exercised:\n\n**dfa_match (294-321)**\n- `PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST`, and the multiple-match-ends semantics: one start position can yield many end offsets, so the ovector holds pairs of *ends* and the count latches to 0 once it overflows — sweep ovector sizes across that boundary.\n- `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART`: it forces `anchored`, disables `firstline` and every start optimization, and requires the identical `wscount`. Drive a genuine partial match first, then restart with the same and with a different workspace size, and compare.\n- workspace sizing: sweep `wscount` around the `(wscount-2)/3` sanity bound and the real `(wscount-2)/6` capacity so the exact crossover is compared.\n- `PARTIAL_SOFT` / `PARTIAL_HARD`, `NOTBOL` / `NOTEOL` / `NOTEMPTY` / `NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`, `ANCHORED` / `ENDANCHORED`, `NO_START_OPTIMIZE`, `COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT`.\n- UTF and `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` subjects, newline conventions, `\\R` conventions.\n- the recursion/condition/callout arms the DFA does support (callouts via `pcre2_set_callout_8` — compare the whole callout sequence), and `pcre2_next_match_8` iterating the recorded ends to exhaustion.\n- match/depth limits via a match context, sweeping the limit across the crossover point.\n\n**substitute (322-351)**\n- every `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_*` option and their combinations: GLOBAL, EXTENDED, LITERAL, UNSET_EMPTY, UNKNOWN_UNSET, OVERFLOW_LENGTH, REPLACEMENT_ONLY, MATCHED.\n- the replacement mini-language: `$0`/`$1`/`${n}`/`${name}`/`$*MARK`, `\\1`, the case operators `\\U \\L \\u \\l \\E`, and the EXTENDED conditionals `${n:-default}` / `${n:+yes:no}`.\n- the documented two-call sizing protocol: call with a zero-length buffer to get the required length, then with exactly that length; plus one-too-small, and `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_OVERFLOW_LENGTH` reporting the full required length. Note the row about the `(len>>3)+10` pessimistic inflation meaning the protocol need not converge — assert whatever the C does.\n- case forcing interacting with `pcre2_set_substitute_case_callout_8` (the transform is deferred and re-applied in place) and with `OVERFLOW_LENGTH`. Also note that `pcre2_substitute` does NOT consult `PCRE2_EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING`, so its casing differs from matching — test a Turkish-casing pattern both ways and assert the C's behaviour.\n- `pcre2_set_substitute_callout_8`: compare the whole callback sequence, recording every field of `pcre2_substitute_callout_block` (exact layout from `c_src/include/pcre2.h`, note the padding after the leading `uint32_t version`), including a callout that returns a positive and a negative value.\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` reusing a pre-filled match_data.\n- UTF subjects and replacements, empty matches with GLOBAL (the anchored-retry dance), and `\\K` in the pattern.\n\nWhere a row names an expected outcome explicitly, ALSO assert the C produces it. If the C does not, the row was mis-derived — **the C is ground truth**: keep the C-vs-Rust assertion, correct that row's `configuration` cell in `CONFIGS.md`, and report it.\n\n**Use MANY randomized inputs per row, not one hand-picked value**, with a FIXED seed (`Rng::new(<constant>)`).\n\n## Rules\n- Fix `src/*.rs` if (and only if) you find a genuine C-vs-Rust divergence; rebuild with `cargo build --release`. Report every fix precisely. NEVER touch `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT weaken or delete an assertion to make a failure go away.\n- Set deterministic match/depth/heap limits so runaway patterns cannot hang the test; keep total runtime well under 600 s.\n- Run `timeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_b_cfg_dfa_subst -- --test-threads=1` and iterate until it passes.\n- If the process dies with no message, the Rust `.so` panicked (`panic = \"abort\"`); isolate with `--exact <testname>`.\n- Then run `timeout 300 python3 check_coverage.py` and confirm your file contributes rows 294..351.\n- Finally delete `tests/zz_probe_dfa_subst.rs`.\n\n## Work incrementally to survive interruption\nWrite the file in pieces: create it with the `COVERAGE` block and the dfa tests first, get that compiling and passing, THEN append the substitute tests. Do not try to emit the whole file in one enormous write.\n\n## Final report must state\n- the exact commands run and the final PASS output,\n- the `check_coverage.py` CONFIGS line showing your rows covered,\n- every `src/*.rs` fix (file, what was wrong, what the C does),\n- every `CONFIGS.md` cell you corrected and why."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":436884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":964,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7","uuid":"d946f739-5488-41b5-992e-d472314470b0","timestamp":"2026-08-23T11:06:39.930Z"}
