{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a07abdf538abfbbac","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CEeVNoMBVMS2TgwKsqnpex","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tBNRGp/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-tBNRGp-translated-rust/cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7/tasks/a07abdf538abfbbac.output","summary":"Done. `tests/phase_c_substitute.rs` is complete and green.\n\n## Command run and final output\n\n```\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_c_substitute -- --test-threads=1\n```\n\n```\nrunning 13 tests\ntest coverage_is_exactly_324_to_379 ... ok\ntest substitute_allocation_failure ... ok\ntest substitute_callout_rejects ... ok\ntest substitute_case_callout_errors ... ok\ntest substitute_dynamic_replacements ... ok\ntest substitute_error_paths ... ok\ntest substitute_match_error_propagation ... ok\ntest substitute_matched_consistency ... ok\ntest substitute_null_arguments ... ok\ntest substitute_option_bit_sweep ... ok\ntest substitute_overflow_length ... ok\ntest substitute_unavailable_group ... ok\ntest substitute_unreachable_rows ... ok\n\ntest result: ok. 13 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.07s\n```\n\n(Compiles with zero warnings. Note: an unrelated, concurrently-added `tests/phase_c_api.rs` fails in a whole-suite run — not touched by me; all other pre-existing suites still pass.)\n\n## Row coverage — exactly 324..379\n\nThere is a self-checking test, `coverage_is_exactly_324_to_379`, that re-parses every `rows: &[...]` annotation out of the file via `include_str!` and asserts the union equals `324..=379` (no gaps, nothing out of scope). Its printed set:\n\n`324 325 326 327 328 329 330 331 332 333 334 335 336 337 338 339 340 341 342 343 344 345 346 347 348 349 350 351 352 353 354 355 356 357 358 359 360 361 362 363 364 365 366 367 368 369 370 371 372 373 374 375 376 377 378 379` — 56 rows.\n\nEvery case asserts three things across both `.so`s: the numeric return code, `*outlengthptr` (distinguishing `PCRE2_UNSET`, the `PTREXIT` replacement offset, the `OVERFLOW_LENGTH` required size, and the success length), and the **entire** output buffer including 16 guard bytes past the usable capacity. Subjects/replacements are copied once into a shared padded buffer so both libraries see the same pointer and the same bytes past the nominal end.\n\nNotable witnesses that took work to find:\n- **-75 (`BAD_BACKSLASH_K`, row 339)**: only reachable via recursion, not syntactic nesting — `(?(DEFINE)(a\\K))b(?=(?1))` on `\"ba\"`.\n- **-60 (row 341)**: `(?<=\\Ka)b` + `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK`, `start_offset = 2` on `\"aab\"`.\n- **-70 (row 375)**: a `substitute_case_callout` claiming to need `SIZE_MAX-1` units, subject `\"ax\"`, replacement `\"\\Uabc\"`, `EXTENDED|OVERFLOW_LENGTH` — trips `pcre2_substitute.c:1752`.\n- **-48 rows 334/335**: fallible allocator with separate per-library counters, budget swept 0..9. Discovered (and documented in the test) that `pcre2_substitute` memcpy's the external `match_data` — `memctl` included — over the internal one, so the internal block is freed through the *external* block's allocator; the external block must therefore share the match context's allocator.\n- Rows **342/343/377** are flagged unreachable with reasons, and assert C≡Rust plus `rc != -65 / -61 / -50` over the nearest reachable inputs (empty-match global loops, a 5000-substitution global run, duplicate-name patterns).\n- Not tested, deliberately, with a comment: `code == NULL` and `outlengthptr == NULL` — the C dereferences both before any validation (`pcre2_substitute.c:758` and `:778`), so they are out-of-bounds in the C itself (HARNESS.md pitfall 6). Every other pointer/length boundary is exercised, including `buffer == NULL` with `*outlengthptr == 0`, and all 32 option bits individually plus `0xFFFFFFFF`.\n\n## `src/*.rs` fixes\n\n**None.** No C-vs-Rust divergence was found anywhere in rows 324..379 — return codes, `*outlengthptr`, output buffers, guard bytes, substitute-callout block contents, and case-callout argument sequences all matched byte-for-byte on every input, including the allocator-failure sweeps. No assertion was weakened and `c_src/` was not touched.\n\n## ERRORS.md corrections\n\nEvery **`expected C result`** cell in rows 324..379 turned out to be correct — the C returns exactly what each row documents. The mis-derivations were all in the **trigger** cells, which I corrected (the C being ground truth):\n\n1. **Row 341** — the stated example `a\\K` with `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL` does *not* reach the `-60` branch; `pcre2_substitute_8(\"aaa\", \"a\\K\", \"X\", GLOBAL)` returns `3`. Replaced with the verified witness (`(?<=\\Ka)b` + `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK`, `start_offset = 2`) and noted why the extra option is both necessary (compile-time block) and sufficient (it also disables the match-time `-75`). The test keeps the old example as an explicit control case.\n2. **Row 348** — \"name longer than 32 (`MAX_NAME_SIZE` in this file)\" is wrong: `MAX_NAME_SIZE` is **128** (`c_src/src/config.h:223`). The stated trigger `\"${\" + 35 'a's + \"}\"` *succeeds*; 129 is the first rejected length. Corrected the limit and the example.\n3. **Row 362** — the parenthetical \"`\"${1:x}\"` is too short for the `ptr < repend - 2` guard and yields -58\" is wrong: with the closing brace the replacement is 6 units, the guard passes, and the C returns **-59**. It is `\"${1:x\"` / `\"${1:\"` (no closing brace) that yield -58. Corrected, and both variants are now test cases.\n4. **Row 375** — added the reachable witness (naughty `substitute_case_callout`), since the trigger as written (plain `GLOBAL|OVERFLOW_LENGTH`) cannot be reached without a multi-exabyte subject.","usage":{"total_tokens":291999,"tool_uses":50,"duration_ms":1463866},"uuid":"b6a15570-589c-4b60-a122-48ae63d92d06","session_id":"cde48455-d5ce-4cd5-a0b0-2154082e5ad7"}
